<node id="047623b2-d42b-4c49-b3db-a3c7f3da0b43">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"Policy Provisions &amp; Ownership Rights","text":", the death benefit shall be reduced accordingly. If the Insured \nis found to be outside of an insurable age range at issue, the Policy shall be void ab initio and all premiums shall \nbe refunded.  \nAssignment  \nThe Policy Owner may assign this Policy or any rights under it by written notice satisfactory to the Company. The \nassignment shall take effect upon the Company’s receipt and recording of such notice. The Company assumes no \nresponsibility for the validity, sufficiency, or tax consequences of any assignment. Unless otherwise agreed in \nwriting by an irrevocable beneficiary, the rights of the assignee are subordinate to those of any such beneficiary. \nAn assignment may limit or preclude the exercise of certain rights under the Policy.  \nPolicy Owner Rights  \nWhile the Insured is living, and unless otherwise restricted by an assignment or irrevocable beneficiary \ndesignation, the Policy Owner may exercise all contractual rights without the consent of any other person. \nThese rights include, but are not limited to: changing the Beneficiary, assigning the Policy, electing optional \nforms of benefits, and requesting policy information. Actions of the Policy Owner shall be binding on all parties \nwith an interest in the Policy, subject to applicable law and the terms herein. \nNonparticipating  \nThis Policy is nonparticipating and shall not share in any surplus or earnings of the Company. No dividends are \npayable to the Policy Owner now or in the future. Premium rates are based on the underwriting class of the \nInsured and the Company’s pricing standards at the time of issue.\n\n===== Page 5 =====\nPremiums and Grace Period  \nPremium Payments  \nPremiums are payable in advance on or before the due date shown in the Policy \nSpecifications. The Policy Owner may change the payment mode with the \nCompany’s approval. Premiums must be paid to the Company at its Administrative \nOffice or to an authorized agent in exchange for an official receipt.  \nGrace Period  \nA grace period of 31 days will be allowed for the payment of each premium after the first. \nDuring this period, the Policy shall remain in force. If the Insured dies during the grace period, \nany unpaid premium due will be deducted from the death benefit.  \nLapse for Nonpayment  \nIf any premium is not paid before the end of the grace period, the Policy will lapse as of \nthe due date of the unpaid premium, and coverage will terminate. No","summary":"This document details critical aspects of an insurance policy, including adjustments to the death benefit if the insured falls outside the insurable age range, which can lead to the policy being voided with full refunds. Assignments require written notice and do not override irrevocable beneficiaries; assigned rights are subordinated. The policy owner retains broad rights while the insured lives, provided there are no restrictions. The policy is nonparticipating, meaning no dividends or shared profits occur. Premiums are due in advance, with a 31-day grace period allowing continued coverage—failure to pay results in lapse.","topics":["Insurance Policy Terms","Death Benefit Adjustments","Policy Assignment","Premium Payment Rules"],"facts":[{"name":"Death Benefit Reduction Due to Age Ineligibility","sentence":"The death benefit shall be reduced if the Insured is found to be outside of an insurable age range at issue.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["death benefit adjustment","insurable age range","policy invalidity at issue"],"entities":[{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"individual covered by policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"issuing insurer of the policy","relational_anchors":["Administrative Office"]},{"name":"Policy Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"contractual holder of policy rights","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Assignment","type":"CONCEPT","role":"transfer of policy rights via notice","relational_anchors":["written notice satisfactory to the Company","recording of such notice"]},{"name":"Death Benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"payout amount upon insured's death","relational_anchors":["reduced accordingly","unpaid premium due will be deducted"]},{"name":"Grace Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"extension for late premium payment","relational_anchors":["31 days","after the first"]},{"name":"Lapse for Nonpayment","type":"CONCEPT","role":"termination of coverage due to missed premium","relational_anchors":["end of the grace period","as of the due date of the unpaid premium"]},{"name":"Premium","type":"CONCEPT","role":"periodic payment required for coverage","relational_anchors":["due date shown in the Policy Specifications","advance on or before the due date"]},{"name":"Refund","type":"CONCEPT","role":"return of paid premiums if policy voided","relational_anchors":["all premiums shall be refunded"]},{"name":"Irrevocable Beneficiary","type":"CONCEPT","role":"beneficiary whose rights override assignees","relational_anchors":["unless otherwise agreed in writing"]},{"name":"Nonparticipating","type":"CONCEPT","role":"no sharing in company surplus or earnings","relational_anchors":["shall not share in any surplus or earnings","No dividends are payable"]}]},{"name":"Void Ab Initio Due to Age","sentence":"If the Insured is found to be outside of an insurable age range at issue, the Policy shall be void ab initio.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["void ab initio","insurable age range","underwriting conditions"],"entities":[{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"individual covered by policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"issuing insurer of the policy","relational_anchors":["Administrative Office"]},{"name":"Policy Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"contractual holder of policy rights","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Assignment","type":"CONCEPT","role":"transfer of policy rights via notice","relational_anchors":["written notice satisfactory to the Company","recording of such notice"]},{"name":"Death Benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"payout amount upon insured's death","relational_anchors":["reduced accordingly","unpaid premium due will be deducted"]},{"name":"Grace Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"extension for late premium payment","relational_anchors":["31 days","after the first"]},{"name":"Lapse for Nonpayment","type":"CONCEPT","role":"termination of coverage due to missed premium","relational_anchors":["end of the grace period","as of the due date of the unpaid premium"]},{"name":"Premium","type":"CONCEPT","role":"periodic payment required for coverage","relational_anchors":["due date shown in the Policy Specifications","advance on or before the due date"]},{"name":"Refund","type":"CONCEPT","role":"return of paid premiums if policy voided","relational_anchors":["all premiums shall be refunded"]},{"name":"Irrevocable Beneficiary","type":"CONCEPT","role":"beneficiary whose rights override assignees","relational_anchors":["unless otherwise agreed in writing"]},{"name":"Nonparticipating","type":"CONCEPT","role":"no sharing in company surplus or earnings","relational_anchors":["shall not share in any surplus or earnings","No dividends are payable"]}]},{"name":"Age Ineligibility Refund","sentence":"If the Insured is found to be outside of an insurable age range at issue, all premiums shall be refunded.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["insurable age range","premium refund","void ab initio"],"entities":[{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"individual covered by policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"issuing insurer of the policy","relational_anchors":["Administrative Office"]},{"name":"Policy Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"contractual holder of policy rights","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Assignment","type":"CONCEPT","role":"transfer of policy rights via notice","relational_anchors":["written notice satisfa