<node id="ddbe6061-d55e-43bf-ac47-31ce4f169b9e">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"Policy Lapse, Reinstatement &amp; Death Benefits","text":" will be deducted from the death benefit.  \nLapse for Nonpayment  \nIf any premium is not paid before the end of the grace period, the Policy will lapse as of \nthe due date of the unpaid premium, and coverage will terminate. No benefits shall be \npayable under a lapsed Policy, except as provided in the Reinstatement provision.  \nReinstatement Rights  \nA lapsed Policy may be reinstated within five years from the date of lapse if the following \nconditions are met: 1) written request for reinstatement is received, 2) evidence of insurability \nis submitted and accepted, and 3) all overdue premiums are paid with interest at the rate \nspecified by the Company at the time of reinstatement. Upon reinstatement, coverage will \nresume as though the Policy had remained continuously in force, subject to the \nIncontestability and Suicide Exclusion provisions starting anew from the date of \nreinstatement.\n\n===== Page 6 =====\nDeath Benefit  \nBenefit Payable Upon Death  \nIf the Insured dies while this Policy is in force and before the Expiry Date, the Company will \npay the death benefit to the designated Beneficiary, subject to all terms and conditions herein. \nThe death benefit will be equal to the Face Amount shown in the Policy Specifications, less \nany unpaid premiums or indebtedness.  \nProof of Death  \nBefore any death benefit is payable, the Company must receive due proof of the Insured’s \ndeath, including a certified death certificate and any additional documentation the \nCompany reasonably requires. The Company reserves the right to investigate the cause \nand circumstances of death and to contest the claim if within the contestability period.  \nPayment of Proceeds  \nDeath benefit proceeds will be paid in a lump sum unless an alternative payment option is \nelected by the Policy Owner during the Insured's lifetime or by the Beneficiary after the \nInsured’s death. Payment shall be made promptly upon receipt and approval of all required \nclaim documentation.  \nInterest on Death Benefit  \nInterest shall accrue on the death benefit from the date of death to the date of payment, at \na rate not less than required by applicable state law.  \nContingent Beneficiaries and Simultaneous Death  \nIf no designated Beneficiary survives the Insured, proceeds will be paid to the \nContingent Beneficiary, if any. If no Contingent Beneficiary survives, proceeds will be \npayable to","summary":"If a premium is not paid within the grace period, the policy lapses, terminating coverage unless reinstated within five years. Reinstatement requires a formal request, proof of insurability, and payment of overdue premiums plus interest. When the insured dies while the policy is active, the company pays the face amount minus outstanding debts, contingent on proper proof of death and compliance with claims procedures. Proceeds are typically paid in a lump sum, include accrued interest, and go to designated beneficiaries; otherwise, they pass to contingent beneficiaries or the estate.","topics":["Life Insurance Terms","Policy Lapse and Reinstatement","Death Benefit Claims","Beneficiary Designation"],"facts":[{"name":"Policy Lapse Due to Nonpayment","sentence":"If any premium is not paid before the end of the grace period, the Policy will lapse as of the due date of the unpaid premium.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["premium nonpayment","grace period","policy lapse"],"entities":[{"name":"Lapse for Nonpayment","type":"CONCEPT","role":"trigger condition for policy termination","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"end of the grace period","type":"DATE","role":"deadline for premium payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"due date of the unpaid premium","type":"DATE","role":"effective date of policy lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Policy","type":"POLICY","role":"contractual instrument subject to lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Reinstatement provision","type":"PROVISION","role":"legal mechanism enabling revival post-lapse","relational_anchors":["within five years from the date of lapse"]},{"name":"written request for reinstatement","type":"CONDITION","role":"requirement for initiating reinstatement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"evidence of insurability","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"medical/underwriting requirement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"all overdue premiums","type":"PAYMENT","role":"financial obligation prior to reinstatement","relational_anchors":["with interest at the rate specified by the Company"]},{"name":"Incontestability and Suicide Exclusion provisions","type":"CONCEPT","role":"post-reinstatement limitations on claims","relational_anchors":["starting anew from the date of reinstatement"]},{"name":"Death Benefit","type":"BENEFIT","role":"amount payable upon insured's death","relational_anchors":["equal to the Face Amount shown in the Policy Specifications","less any unpaid premiums or indebtedness"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"individual covered by life insurance","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurer issuing and administering policy","relational_anchors":["rate specified by the Company at the time of reinstatement"]},{"name":"Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"recipient of death benefit payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Contingent Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"secondary recipient if primary beneficiary predeceases","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"certified death certificate","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"primary proof of death required","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Proof of Death","type":"PROCESS","role":"verification step before benefit disbursement","relational_anchors":["including a certified death certificate"]},{"name":"right to investigate","type":"RIGHT","role":"company authority over claim validity","relational_anchors":["contestation possible within contestability period"]},{"name":"lump sum","type":"PAYMENT","role":"default method of death benefit distribution","relational_anchors":["unless alternative election was made"]},{"name":"interest rate","type":"RATE","role":"accrual applied to delayed payments","relational_anchors":["not less than required by applicable state law"]}]},{"name":"Policy Lapse Due to Nonpayment","sentence":"Coverage terminates when the Policy lapses due to nonpayment.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["Policy Lapse","Nonpayment of Premium","Termination of Coverage"],"entities":[{"name":"Lapse for Nonpayment","type":"CONCEPT","role":"trigger condition for policy termination","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"end of the grace period","type":"DATE","role":"deadline for premium payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"due date of the unpaid premium","type":"DATE","role":"effective date of policy lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Policy","type":"POLICY","role":"contractual instrument subject to lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Reinstatement provision","type":"PROVISION","role":"legal mechanism enabling revival post-lapse","relational_anchors":["within five years from the date of lapse"]},{"name":"written request for reinstatement","type":"CONDITION","role":"requirement for initiating reinstatement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"evidence of insurability","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"medical/underwriting requirement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"all overdue premiums","type":"PAYMENT","role":"financial obligation prior to reinstatement","relational_anchors":["with interest at the rate specified by the Company"]},{"name":"Incontestability and Suicide Exclusion provisions","type":"CONCEPT","role":"post-reinstatement limitations on claims","relational_anchors":["starting anew from the date of reinstatement"]},{"name":"Death Benefit","type":"BENEFIT","role":"amount payable upon insured's death","relational_anchors":["equal to the Face Amount shown in the Policy Specifications","less any unpaid premiums or indebtedness"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"individual covered by life insurance","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurer issuing and administering policy","relational_anchors":["rate specified by the Company at the time of reinstatement"]},{"name":"Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"recipient of death benefit payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Contingent Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"secondary recipient if primary beneficiary predeceases","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"certified death certificate","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"primary proof of death required","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Proof of Death","type":"PROCESS","role":"verification step before benefit disbursement","relational_anchors":["including a certified death certificate"]},{"name":"right to investigate","type":"RIGHT","role":"company authority over claim validity","relational_anchors":["contestation possible within contestability period"]},{"name":"lump sum","type":"PAYMENT","role":"default method of death benefit distribution","relational_anchors":["unless alternative election was made"]},{"name":"interest rate","type":"RATE","role":"accrual applied to delayed payments","relational_anchors":["not less than required by applicable state law"]}]},{"name":"Lapse Benefits Exception","sentence":"No benefits shall be payable under a lapsed Policy, except as provided in the Reinstatement provision.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["Policy Lapse","Reinstatement Rights","Benefits During Lapse"],"entities":[{"name":"Lapse for Nonpayment","type":"CONCEPT","role":"trigger condition for policy termination","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"end of the grace period","type":"DATE","role":"deadline for premium payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"due date of the unpaid premium","type":"DATE","role":"effective date of policy lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Policy","type":"POLICY","role":"contractual instrument subject to lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Reinstatement provision","type":"PROVISION","role":"legal mechanism enabling revival post-lapse","relational_anchors":["within five years from the date of lapse"]},{"name":"written request for reinstatement","type":"CONDITION","role":"requirement for initiating reinstatement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"evidence of insurability","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"medical/underwriting requirement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"all overdue premiums","type":"PAYMENT","role":"financial obligation prior to reinstatement","relational_anchors":["with interest at the rate specified by the Company"]},{"name":"Incontestability and Suicide Exclusion provisions","type":"CONCEPT","role":"post-reinstatement limitations on claims","relational_anchors":["starting anew from the date of reinstatement"]},{"name":"Death Benefit","type":"BENEFIT","role":"amount payable upon insured's death","relational_anchors":["equal to the Face Amount shown in the Policy Specifications","less any unpaid premiums or indebtedness"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"individual covered by life insurance","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurer issuing and administering policy","relational_anchors":["rate specified by the Company at the time of reinstatement"]},{"name":"Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"recipient of death benefit payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Contingent Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"secondary recipient if primary beneficiary predeceases","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"certified death certificate","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"primary proof of death required","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Proof of Death","type":"PROCESS","role":"verification step before benefit disbursement","relational_anchors":["including a certified death certificate"]},{"name":"right to investigate","type":"RIGHT","role":"company authority over claim validity","relational_anchors":["contestation possible within contestability period"]},{"name":"lump sum","type":"PAYMENT","role":"default method of death benefit distribution","relational_anchors":["unless alternative election was made"]},{"name":"interest rate","type":"RATE","role":"accrual applied to delayed payments","relational_anchors":["not less than required by applicable state law"]}]},{"name":"Policy Reinstatement Window","sentence":"A lapsed Policy may be reinstated within five years from the date of lapse.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["policy reinstatement","lapse duration","five-year reinstatement"],"entities":[{"name":"Lapse for Nonpayment","type":"CONCEPT","role":"trigger condition for policy termination","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"end of the grace period","type":"DATE","role":"deadline for premium payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"due date of the unpaid premium","type":"DATE","role":"effective date of policy lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Policy","type":"POLICY","role":"contractual instrument subject to lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Reinstatement provision","type":"PROVISION","role":"legal mechanism enabling revival post-lapse","relational_anchors":["within five years from the date of lapse"]},{"name":"written request for reinstatement","type":"CONDITION","role":"requirement for initiating reinstatement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"evidence of insurability","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"medical/underwriting requirement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"all overdue premiums","type":"PAYMENT","role":"financial obligation prior to reinstatement","relational_anchors":["with interest at the rate specified by the Company"]},{"name":"Incontestability and Suicide Exclusion provisions","type":"CONCEPT","role":"post-reinstatement limitations on claims","relational_anchors":["starting anew from the date of reinstatement"]},{"name":"Death Benefit","type":"BENEFIT","role":"amount payable upon insured's death","relational_anchors":["equal to the Face Amount shown in the Policy Specifications","less any unpaid premiums or indebtedness"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"individual covered by life insurance","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurer issuing and administering policy","relational_anchors":["rate specified by the Company at the time of reinstatement"]},{"name":"Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"recipient of death benefit payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Contingent Beneficiary","type":"PERSON","role":"secondary recipient if primary beneficiary predeceases","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"certified death certificate","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"primary proof of death required","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Proof of Death","type":"PROCESS","role":"verification step before benefit disbursement","relational_anchors":["including a certified death certificate"]},{"name":"right to investigate","type":"RIGHT","role":"company authority over claim validity","relational_anchors":["contestation possible within contestability period"]},{"name":"lump sum","type":"PAYMENT","role":"default method of death benefit distribution","relational_anchors":["unless alternative election was made"]},{"name":"interest rate","type":"RATE","role":"accrual applied to delayed payments","relational_anchors":["not less than required by applicable state law"]}]},{"name":"Written Request for Reinstatement","sentence":"To reinstate a lapsed Policy, a written request for reinstatement must be received.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["Policy Reinstatement","Grace Period","Nonpayment Lapse"],"entities":[{"name":"Lapse for Nonpayment","type":"CONCEPT","role":"trigger condition for policy termination","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"end of the grace period","type":"DATE","role":"deadline for premium payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"due date of the unpaid premium","type":"DATE","role":"effective date of policy lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Policy","type":"POLICY","role":"contractual instrumen