<node id="87aee738-6956-4951-bcbc-431f93d42897">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"Policy Contestability &amp; Reinstatement Clauses","text":", including one who incurred \nexpenses related to the Insured’s last illness or burial. Such payment shall discharge the \nCompany’s liability to the extent of the amount paid.\n\n===== Page 8 =====\nContestability and Suicide Clause  \nIncontestability  \nThis Policy shall be incontestable after it has been in force during the lifetime of the Insured \nfor a period of two (2) years from the Issue Date, except for nonpayment of premiums. During \nthe two-year contestability period, the Company may rescind the Policy or deny a claim if \nthere was a material misrepresentation in the application. After the contestability period \nexpires, the Company may not contest the validity of the Policy, even in the event of \nmisstatement, unless such misstatement constitutes fraud as defined by applicable state law.  \nContestability After Reinstatement  \nIf the Policy is reinstated, a new two-year contestability period shall apply from the date \nof reinstatement, but only with respect to statements made in the reinstatement \napplication.  \nSuicide Exclusion  \nIf the Insured dies by suicide, while sane or insane, within two (2) years from the Issue Date \n(or from the date of reinstatement, if applicable), the Company’s liability shall be limited to \nan amount equal to the total premiums paid, without interest. After two years, the full death \nbenefit is payable regardless of cause of death, subject to all other terms of this Policy.\n\n===== Page 9 =====\nReinstatement and Continuation  \nRight to Reinstate  \nIf this Policy has lapsed due to nonpayment of premiums, it may be reinstated within five (5) \nyears from the date of lapse, provided the following conditions are met: 1) The Policy Owner \nsubmits a written application for reinstatement; 2) Satisfactory evidence of the Insured’s \ninsurability is submitted; and 3) All overdue premiums are paid with interest at a rate \ndetermined by the Company, compounded annually.  \nEffect of Reinstatement  \nUpon reinstatement, the Policy shall be deemed to be in full force as if it had never lapsed, \nsubject to the following: 1) A new two-year contestability period shall begin as of the date of \nreinstatement; 2) The suicide exclusion shall apply anew from the date of reinstatement; 3)  \nThe Company shall not be","summary":"This section details critical clauses in an insurance policy, including a two-year contestability period during which the insurer can void coverage due to misrepresentation, except for fraud. If the insured dies by suicide within two years of issue or reinstatement, benefits are limited to returned premiums. Policies can be reinstated within five years of lapse if proof of insurability and unpaid premiums plus interest are provided, restarting both the contestability and suicide exclusion periods.","topics":["Insurance Policy Terms","Contestability Period","Suicide Clause","Policy Reinstatement"],"facts":[{"name":"Two-Year Incontestability Rule","sentence":"This Policy shall be incontestable after it has been in force during the lifetime of the Insured for a period of two years from the Issue Date.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["incontestability","two-year period","issue date","policy validity"],"entities":[{"name":"two (2) years","type":"DATE","role":"duration of contestability period","relational_anchors":["Issue Date"]},{"name":"this Policy","type":"POLICY","role":"insurance contract under consideration","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"issuing insurer with enforcement authority","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"individual covered by life insurance policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the Policy Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"party entitled to reinstate policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"nonpayment of premiums","type":"CONCEPT","role":"condition leading to policy lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"five (5) years","type":"DATE","role":"maximum time window for reinstatement","relational_anchors":["date of lapse"]},{"name":"material misrepresentation","type":"CONCEPT","role":"basis for company to deny claims during contestability","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"fraud as defined by applicable state law","type":"CONCEPT","role":"exception allowing post-contestability challenge","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"suicide exclusion","type":"CONCEPT","role":"limitation on payout when death occurs by suicide","relational_anchors":["within two (2) years from the Issue Date"]},{"name":"full death benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"payout available after two-year suicide exclusion ends","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"Two-Year Incontestability Rule","sentence":"This Policy shall be incontestable after it has been in force during the lifetime of the Insured for a period of two years from the Issue Date, except for nonpayment of premiums.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["incontestability","two-year period","policy enforcement","issue date"],"entities":[{"name":"two (2) years","type":"DATE","role":"duration of contestability period","relational_anchors":["Issue Date"]},{"name":"this Policy","type":"POLICY","role":"insurance contract under consideration","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"issuing insurer with enforcement authority","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"individual covered by life insurance policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the Policy Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"party entitled to reinstate policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"nonpayment of premiums","type":"CONCEPT","role":"condition leading to policy lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"five (5) years","type":"DATE","role":"maximum time window for reinstatement","relational_anchors":["date of lapse"]},{"name":"material misrepresentation","type":"CONCEPT","role":"basis for company to deny claims during contestability","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"fraud as defined by applicable state law","type":"CONCEPT","role":"exception allowing post-contestability challenge","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"suicide exclusion","type":"CONCEPT","role":"limitation on payout when death occurs by suicide","relational_anchors":["within two (2) years from the Issue Date"]},{"name":"full death benefit","type":"CONCEPT","role":"payout available after two-year suicide exclusion ends","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"Policy Contestability Period","sentence":"During the two-year contestability period, the Company may rescind the Policy if there was a material misrepresentation in the application.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["contestation period","material misrepresentation","policy invalidation"],"entities":[{"name":"two (2) years","type":"DATE","role":"duration of contestability period","relational_anchors":["Issue Date"]},{"name":"this Policy","type":"POLICY","role":"insurance contract under consideration","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"issuing insurer with enforcement authority","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"individual covered by life insurance policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the Policy Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"party entitled to reinstate policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"nonpayment of premiums","type":"CONCEPT","role":"condition leading to policy lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"five (5) years","type":"DATE","role":"maximum time window for reinstatement","relational_anchors":["date of lapse"]},{"name":"material misrepresentation","type":"CONCEPT","role":"basis for company to deny claims during contestability","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"fraud as defined by applicable state law","type":"CONCEPT","role":"exception allowing post-contestability challenge","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"suicide exclusion","type":"CONCEPT","role