<node id="9e7f61df-201d-43fd-b076-db5b8e859f8e">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"Reinstatement &amp; Legal Terms","text":" the following: 1) A new two-year contestability period shall begin as of the date of \nreinstatement; 2) The suicide exclusion shall apply anew from the date of reinstatement; 3)  \nThe Company shall not be liable for any claim arising from an event occurring during \nthe period in which the Policy was lapsed.  \nExtension or Conversion at Expiry  \nThis Policy does not provide automatic renewal beyond the term period. However, prior to the \nExpiry Date, the Policy Owner may be eligible to convert this Policy to a permanent life \ninsurance policy offered by the Company without evidence of insurability, provided: 1) The \nrequest is made during the conversion period specified in the Policy Specifications; 2) The \nInsured is not older than the maximum conversion age established by the Company at the \ntime of request; and 3) Premiums for the new policy are paid in accordance with the terms of \nthe selected product.\n\n===== Page 10 =====\nLegal Provisions and Governing Law  \nGoverning Law  \nThis Policy shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of \nNew York. Any dispute arising under or related to this Policy shall be resolved in a court of \ncompetent jurisdiction located in the State of New York, unless otherwise required by \napplicable law.  \nNotice and Correspondence  \nAll notices to the Company must be sent to its Administrative Office as shown in the Policy \nSpecifications, unless otherwise directed by the Company. The Company will send notices to \nthe last known address of the Policy Owner as reflected in its records. It is the Policy Owner’s \nresponsibility to notify the Company promptly of any change in address.  \nPolicy Statements and Confirmations  \nThe Company may provide periodic statements or confirmations of coverage, premium \npayment status, or other relevant information. These shall not modify the terms of the \nPolicy unless accompanied by a properly authorized amendment or rider.  \nPrivacy and Confidentiality  \nThe Company collects and maintains personal information in connection with this Policy. \nSuch information shall be kept confidential and used only for underwriting, claims, and \nadministrative purposes, in accordance with applicable privacy laws and regulations.  \nSeverability  \nIf any provision of this Policy is held to be invalid or unenforceable under applicable law, \nthe remaining provisions shall remain in full force and effect to the extent permitted by law.  \nEntire Agreement and Waiver  \n","summary":"Upon reinstatement, a new two-year contestability period starts, suicide exclusions resume, and the insurer is not liable for claims during the lapse period. The policy does not renew automatically but allows conversion to permanent life insurance without proof of insurability if certain criteria—such as timing, age limits, and payment—are met. This policy is governed by New York law, requires proper notice delivery, ensures data confidentiality, and includes standard legal clauses like severability and entire agreement.","topics":["Policy Reinstatement","Conversion Options","Governing Law","Legal Clauses"],"facts":[{"name":"Reinstatement Contestability Reset","sentence":"A new two-year contestability period begins on the date of reinstatement.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["contestability period","policy reinstatement","claim investigation window"],"entities":[{"name":"date of reinstatement","type":"DATE","role":"trigger point for new exclusions","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"two-year contestability period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"new evaluation window post-reinstatement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"suicide exclusion","type":"EXCLUSION","role":"applies afresh after reinstatement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"this Policy","type":"POLICY","role":"subject of non-liability during lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"period in which the Policy was lapsed","type":"PERIOD","role":"non-covered timeframe for claims","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"extension or conversion at expiry","type":"ACTION","role":"eligibility condition for policy upgrade","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"issuer and administrator of policy","relational_anchors":["Administrative Office"]},{"name":"Policy Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"requester of conversion option","relational_anchors":["last known address"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"eligible candidate for conversion","relational_anchors":["maximum conversion age"]},{"name":"conversion period specified in the Policy Specifications","type":"CONDITION","role":"timing constraint for conversion request","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"maximum conversion age","type":"AGE","role":"upper limit for Insured's eligibility","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"State of New York","type":"LOCATION","role":"governing jurisdiction","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"court of competent jurisdiction","type":"LEGAL_ENTITY","role":"venue for resolving disputes","relational_anchors":["State of New York"]},{"name":"last known address of the Policy Owner","type":"ADDRESS","role":"notification destination","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Policy Specifications","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"reference guide for conversion criteria","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"periodic statements or confirmations","type":"STATEMENT","role":"informational updates issued by insurer","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"properly authorized amendment or rider","type":"AMENDMENT","role":"formal modification mechanism","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"personal information","type":"DATA","role":"confidential data collected by company","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"applicable privacy laws and regulations","type":"LAW","role":"legal framework for data handling","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"severability","type":"PROVISION","role":"clause preserving validity of rest","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"Suicide Exclusion Resumes on Reinstatement","sentence":"The suicide exclusion applies again from the date of reinstatement.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["suicide exclusion","policy reinstatement","contestability period"],"entities":[{"name":"date of reinstatement","type":"DATE","role":"trigger point for new exclusions","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"two-year contestability period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"new evaluation window post-reinstatement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"suicide exclusion","type":"EXCLUSION","role":"applies afresh after reinstatement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"this Policy","type":"POLICY","role":"subject of non-liability during lapse","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"period in which the Policy was lapsed","type":"PERIOD","role":"non-covered timeframe for claims","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"extension or conversion at expiry","type":"ACTION","role":"eligibility condition for policy upgrade","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the Company","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"issuer and administrator of policy","relational_anchors":["Administrative Office"]},{"name":"Policy Owner","type":"PERSON","role":"requester of conversion option","relational_anchors":["last known address"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"eligible candidate for conversion","relational_anchors":["maximum conversion age"]},{"name":"conversion period specified in the Policy Specifications","type":"CONDITION","role":"timing constraint for conversion request","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"maximum conversion age","type":"AGE","role":"upper limit for Insured's eligibility","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"State of New York","type":"LOCATION","role":"governing jurisdiction","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"court of competent jurisdiction","type":"LEGAL_ENTITY","role":"venue for resolving disputes","relational_anchors":["State of New York"]},{"name":"last known address of the Policy Owner","type":"ADDRESS","role":"notificati