  <data key="d3">The policy’s long-term coverage (2025–2045) depends on timely premium payments; failure to pay within the grace period causes it to lapse, nullifying future protection despite its stated duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c0901ed-f52a-4ce9-9d52-9547016ca265" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The initial coverage period specified in fact_sentence_1 may be shortened if premiums are not paid within the grace period, causing the policy to lapse before its nominal end date.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c0901ed-f52a-4ce9-9d52-9547016ca265" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">The stated coverage period in fact_sentence_1 determines when the policy can lapse, making it relevant to whether the condition in fact_sentence_2 — about no benefits being payable post-lapse — becomes applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c0901ed-f52a-4ce9-9d52-9547016ca265" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">The stated coverage period in fact_sentence_1 establishes the timeframe during which the policy remains effective, making the reinstatement process described in fact_sentence_2 pertinent should the policy lapse due to non-payment prior to expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
