<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="c80d6a5f-8ecf-4513-841a-708102ad7bc0">
  <data key="d3">The grace period of 31 days allows time after the due date to pay the premium without losing coverage. This temporal buffer supports the maintenance of the policy's active status despite late payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="6027da96-db64-41d1-9b1e-c3ef1d338bd7">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payment without immediate policy lapse, while policy anniversaries define key recurrence points based on the issue date that may trigger renewals or evaluations.</data>
  <data key="d4">related to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payments, supporting the requirement that premiums be paid in advance by providing a short window post-due-date to avoid lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the existence of a 31-day grace period, which fact_sentence_2 elaborates on by clarifying its application across all subsequent premiums beyond the initial one.</data>
  <data key="d4">elaborates on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums without losing coverage, but failure to do so leads to policy lapse, making the grace period essential for maintaining active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures uninterrupted coverage after a missed payment, so the policy stays effective until the end of the grace window unless canceled.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides a buffer preventing immediate lapses, thereby affecting whether the policy remains active long enough to avoid triggering the clause where the company denies claims due to lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="a68f05ee-b6c2-4a27-be1f-bfafeddf4b0c">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period enables continued coverage despite late payment, potentially leading to policy reinstatement, which in turn initiates a new two-year contestability period affecting claim eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="be5d9596-fd48-4642-93c3-1033cc1a3da6">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period helps maintain policy continuity, ensuring that failure to pay promptly doesn't immediately terminate coverage, thereby preserving the opportunity to exercise the conversion right before expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables conversion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes a specific policy feature—the 31-day grace period—which operates under the legal framework established in fact_sentence_2, where the policy is governed by New York law.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="e9992b58-f0cb-4309-aa8b-99ccf5ca595c">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides time to pay overdue premiums before the policy lapses, enabling potential reinstatement. If reinstated, the suicide exclusion begins anew, meaning death by suicide within two years of reinstatement remains non-payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows the policyholder extra time to pay the premium without losing coverage, ensuring continuity of the policy’s validity despite late payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides a buffer allowing timely premium payment before the policy lapses due to nonpayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the exact length of the grace period in a particular policy, while fact_sentence_2 explains the general role and timing of grace periods across policies, providing foundational understanding for interpreting the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums before the policy lapses, enabling the possibility of reinstating it later through formal procedure.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time for late premium payments without lapse, ensuring continuity of coverage when claims may later arise. If the insured’s sex was misrepresented, the death benefit could be recalculated accordingly, potentially altering payout amounts even after coverage remains active through the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums without termination, whereas the two-year incontestability period protects against future disputes over initial application details. These mechanisms serve complementary roles in balancing policyholder rights and insurer safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period specified in fact_sentence_1 is part of the official policy terms included in the full contract outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay a missed premium without immediate loss of coverage, but failure to do so results in policy lapse as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period provides temporary protection against policy lapse, meaning coverage remains active even if the premium isn't paid on time. If payment still doesn’t occur during this window, coverage terminates per the stated rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay a delinquent premium without immediate termination, setting up the condition under which the policy might later become eligible for reinstatement within five years.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures continued coverage beyond the due date, preventing automatic lapse and allowing time to avoid losing benefit entitlements described in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period prevents immediate policy lapse upon missed payment, reducing the likelihood of needing reinstatement. If the grace period ends without payment, the policy lapses, triggering the reinstatement process described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay the premium before the policy lapses, but if unpaid, reinstatement later requires submission of evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payment without immediate lapse, but if unmet, reinstatement becomes necessary—requiring repayment of overdue amounts with interest as stipulated in the second fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums without immediate lapse, but any unpaid premiums still reduce the final death benefit when claimed.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures that the policy remains active beyond the due date, allowing the death benefit to be paid if the insured passes away during this window. Without it, the policy could lapse prematurely, voiding the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures continued coverage beyond missed premium payments, allowing the policy to remain active so that the death benefit can be paid out less any outstanding indebtedness when the insured passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period maintains policy validity post-premium default, enabling the insurer to process a death benefit claim only upon receipt of verified proof of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures the policy remains active long enough for a death claim to be processed, making timely submission of proof such as a certified death certificate essential for receiving benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures that the policy remains active even if a premium is delayed, thus maintaining eligibility for the death benefit that is promised to be paid promptly upon verification of a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures continued coverage despite late premiums, enabling the policy to remain active so that when death occurs, the full death benefit—including accrued interest—is payable to the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums without immediate lapse, but if missed, reinstatement incurs interest; this interest cannot drop below legally mandated levels, ensuring fair treatment under state regulations.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452" target="1fa01fa6-dfb3-4343-85a2-88951da5f49b">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period maintains policy validity long enough to ensure that the primary beneficiary remains eligible for payout upon the insured’s death, preventing premature activation of the contingent beneficiary clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
