  <data key="d3">Taylor Ellis, as the named beneficiary, can receive the policy payout only if the coverage remains active; if the policy lapses due to nonpayment, the right to benefits ceases regardless of the beneficiary designation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">Taylor Ellis, as the designated beneficiary, can only receive benefits if the policy remains in force, which hinges on timely premium payments beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">Taylor Ellis, as the named beneficiary, can only receive the policy proceeds if the policy remains active or is successfully reinstated after a lapse. This makes the reinstatement clause critical to ensuring the beneficiary’s entitlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">Taylor Ellis’s status as beneficiary depends on the policy remaining active; if it lapses due to non-payment, reinstatement via a written request becomes necessary to restore her right to claim benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary designation remains relevant even if the policy lapses, but reinstating it requires additional steps such as providing evidence of insurability, which could affect future benefit distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">Taylor Ellis, identified as the spouse and named beneficiary, is legally entitled to receive the death benefit if Jordan Ellis passes away while the policy remains in force prior to its expiry date.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
