<edge source="abcb40ee-de9a-4039-a28a-20a1a7730e94" target="8e30e475-28a1-405f-a460-f39669dcace1">
  <data key="d3">The individual designated as the Insured Person in the Policy Specifications is the subject of the life insurance contract. This contract constitutes a binding legal arrangement between the policy owner and Equivita Mutual Life Insurance Company.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abcb40ee-de9a-4039-a28a-20a1a7730e94" target="67d36255-3afc-4467-aed5-e7826b482101">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies who is considered the insured, making it possible to determine whether the coverage promised in fact_sentence_1 extends to them.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abcb40ee-de9a-4039-a28a-20a1a7730e94" target="89a5fa8b-5750-4733-b272-83eb8682ac40">
  <data key="d3">Knowing the insured person ensures that the contractual obligations and protections described in the policy’s terms are correctly assigned and applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="abcb40ee-de9a-4039-a28a-20a1a7730e94" target="34b4c70a-636a-4872-a459-16f1604cca89">
  <data key="d3">Defining the insured as the individual specified in the Policy Specifications ensures accurate identification of the party covered. This definition is substantiated when the policy is formally executed, such as through the secretary’s signature at the corporate headquarters.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
