  <data key="d3">The existence of a designated beneficiary, as stated in fact_sentence_1, directly informs the application of fact_sentence_2, which outlines the fallback procedure when that beneficiary does not survive the insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216" target="38974002-cdef-417b-abe4-05fe910d1ed4">
  <data key="d3">The presence of a specified beneficiary (Taylor Ellis) determines whether the estate receives proceeds only if that beneficiary predeceases or fails to survive the insured, as clarified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216" target="ac1a6b74-dc59-4a4f-a24b-16a083744b91">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary in fact_sentence_1 becomes critical in applying the rule from fact_sentence_2, which governs distribution when death order is uncertain. Without knowing who the beneficiary is, the procedural assumption cannot be applied.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216" target="23a68193-61ae-40df-becb-863cc2fa667b">
  <data key="d3">The presence of a specified beneficiary (Taylor Ellis) establishes the default distribution path, but if contact fails within 90 days, the insurer defaults to paying the estate—a fallback mechanism tied to the initial designation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary designation depends on the policy remaining active through timely premium payments, ensuring the death benefit is payable when due.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period ensures that the policy remains active beyond the premium due date, preserving the right of the designated beneficiary to receive the death benefit should the insured pass away during this window.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary in fact_sentence_1 sets up who receives the death benefit, while fact_sentence_2 clarifies how the amount received may change if the insured's age was incorrectly reported, thereby influencing the final payout to the named beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to nonpayment after the grace period, the beneficiary will not receive the death benefit, rendering the designation ineffective.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The designation of the beneficiary depends on the corrected death benefit amount if the insured's sex was misrepresented, meaning the actual payout may alter the intended distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The designation of a beneficiary depends on the policy remaining active; reinstatement allows the policy to regain validity after lapse, thereby ensuring the beneficiary retains claim rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary relies on the official documentation forming the complete contract, including the application and policy details referenced in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the beneficiary relies on the policy being valid, which is protected under the incontestability period, ensuring claim payouts aren't voided due to past inaccuracies.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
