  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6027da96-db64-41d1-9b1e-c3ef1d338bd7" target="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3">
  <data key="d3">Policy anniversaries mark key dates that may determine eligibility timelines for converting the term policy into permanent insurance without evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6027da96-db64-41d1-9b1e-c3ef1d338bd7" target="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2">
  <data key="d3">The concept of a policy anniversary relies on the policy’s effective dates, which fall under the governance of New York law as specified in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6027da96-db64-41d1-9b1e-c3ef1d338bd7" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d3">Policy anniversaries mark key points in the policy timeline where premiums are due; failure to pay within the grace period could lead to lapse, triggering the exclusion of liability described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
