<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 identifies the death benefit, which is the primary payout under the policy. Fact sentence 2 explains how ongoing premiums sustain the policy’s validity, ensuring that the death benefit remains available.</data>
  <data key="d4">necessary condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit described in fact_sentence_1 depends on the policy remaining active; the grace period helps maintain this activity by providing time to pay premiums before cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="b0682bc0-a0b2-4059-b458-c16bdb0d9fb4">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit outlined in the policy may be restricted if the insured dies by suicide within the first two years, meaning the full amount specified in the policy does not apply universally.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount is determined within the official policy documentation, which forms part of the comprehensive contract described in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount is determined by the policy specifications, but its final enforceability may be challenged within the first two years due to potential misrepresentations. The incontestability period limits the company’s right to dispute coverage based on earlier inaccuracies.</data>
  <data key="d4">protects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount defined in the policy specifications may only be altered through formally authorized changes, requiring written approval from a company executive officer.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount defined in the policy specifications depends on the validity of the contract, which cannot be altered by agents—ensuring consistency and legal protection against informal modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount depends on information formally recorded in the policy specifications, which themselves rely on accurate disclosures made during the application process.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is determined by official policy details, ensuring consistency regardless of external influences. This stability is maintained because no individual employee can unilaterally allow late premium payments, preserving the policy’s defined parameters.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount defined in the policy specifications is subject to adjustment if the insured’s sex was misrepresented, ensuring fairness by recalculating benefits based on accurate gender-based rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount defined in the policy specifications serves as the foundation for determining payouts. When the insured’s age is misrepresented, the actual death benefit adjusts proportionally—reflecting what the same premiums would have secured at the accurate age.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit outlined in the policy specifications may be adjusted downward if a misstatement of sex leads to insufficient premium payments, ensuring financial alignment with actual risk assessment.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit stated in the policy specifications may be adjusted downward if a misstatement of age causes insufficient premium payments, ensuring proportional fairness based on actual risk exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit described in fact_sentence_1 only applies if the policy remains valid; however, if the insured was ineligible due to age at issue, the policy is void from inception, negating any claim entitlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">voids</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount, as stated in the policy specs, serves as the foundation for calculating potential overpayments due to misstated age. When inaccuracies lead to higher premiums being paid, the company uses the correct death benefit figure to determine the surplus.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="bff67a86-bdb2-4ccc-9c13-8e25d42f6ad3">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount defined in the policy specifications serves as the foundation for determining if a misstatement in gender led to an overpayment of premiums. This establishes the baseline against which corrections are measured.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit outlined in the policy is conditional on the insured being within the eligible age range at issuance. If not, the policy becomes voidable, leading to full premium refunds instead of payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="d680623c-b8e6-4216-87fc-f28fbd801474">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy determines what the designated beneficiary will receive upon the insured's death, linking the quantified payout to its recipient.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="75149b06-31da-4902-818b-05639e24c747">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy relies on a formally designated beneficiary being recorded; without a valid, written beneficiary designation, the payout process cannot be executed despite clear terms on payables.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="5c01ae55-a8cf-4383-9489-8098cb74d07d">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy determines the pool available for distribution; thus, the rule about equal sharing applies only after the total payable sum has been established by the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="a2150cee-d022-441d-940f-3a1ca38fb293">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount is determined by the policy specifications, and its distribution depends on whether a revocable or irrevocable beneficiary is named, allowing the policyholder flexibility in designating recipients.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="38974002-cdef-417b-abe4-05fe910d1ed4">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy determines what is paid out; if no beneficiary survives, this sum flows to the estate, making the payment rule dependent on the initial specification of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="bca821e4-dd36-4856-bd49-b34de7e5162f">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy governs what is available for payment, including scenarios involving non-surviving primary beneficiaries. This ensures clarity on funds allocated before determining successor recipients.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="0d942949-f688-4e68-85e8-07b70d1319c6">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount is fixed per policy specifications, and naming an irrevocable beneficiary ensures that only with their consent can the recipient be altered—this preserves the integrity of intended disbursement even after the insurer confirms the payment sum.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="a1058e7f-8f18-49f2-bc24-6b94e7ac24c5">
  <data key="d3">The specification of the death benefit amount informs what is owed, while the presumption of beneficiary predecease determines who receives it; together, they shape post-death disbursement protocols.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="ac1a6b74-dc59-4a4f-a24b-16a083744b91">
  <data key="d3">The specification of the death benefit amount informs the financial scope of payouts, which becomes relevant when applying the default rule that beneficiaries are presumed to have predeceased the insured in simultaneous-death scenarios. This ensures clarity in case distributions even when identity of recipient is uncertain.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="57f5cb31-60fc-403b-8faf-61bb58c44d33">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy determines what is available for distribution, which becomes relevant only after resolving beneficiary eligibility—such as whether the primary beneficiary survived the insured—as outlined in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="927cb107-8365-4668-bb63-e17e86722615">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy determines the sum available for distribution, which influences whether a disclaimer by a beneficiary affects the overall payout or triggers alternate distributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount, explicitly defined in the policy, becomes available for distribution to the estate if no living beneficiary exists at the time of the insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="3e91835e-9ad1-4260-b452-07cf78be6476">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy governs what is available for distribution; if no beneficiary survives, this sum may be paid to another party determined equitable by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="91d5242d-2ab5-43dd-a6c9-1df492a48caf">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy determines the maximum sum that can be paid to settle the company’s liability, including payments to the estate or equitable recipients.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="f075e888-0cb1-43c8-8ebf-84c98e1c462f">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy sets the financial ceiling for distributions, including those made to persons equitably entitled due to end-of-life expenses. These claims are subject to the same contractual limits established by the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="23a68193-61ae-40df-becb-863cc2fa667b">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy governs what is owed, and if no beneficiary can be found within 90 days, the insurer may distribute those funds to the estate, ensuring payment occurs even in absence of a named recipient.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit specified in the policy only applies if the policy remains active, which depends on paying premiums before the grace period ends. If the policy lapses due to non-payment, the death benefit ceases to be payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit specified in the policy only applies if the policy remains in force at the time of death; once it lapses due to nonpayment, the obligation to pay ceases.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy is conditional on the policy being active; it cannot be paid if the policy has lapsed unless reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount remains fixed per the Policy Specifications even after reinstatement, meaning the original payout term applies once coverage resumes. This ensures consistency in beneficiary compensation regardless of prior lapse status.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy terms remains relevant even when reinstating a lapsed policy, ensuring continuity of benefits once coverage resumes.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy depends on the policy being actively in force, which requires successful reinstatement after lapse via evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount, fixed in the Policy Specifications, remains intact when a lapsed policy is reinstated, ensuring continuous entitlement under revived coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy is subject to reinstatement terms, including repayment of overdue premiums with interest, ensuring continuity of coverage and potential payout upon death.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines the death benefit amount in the policy specifications, which directly determines the payout described in fact_sentence_2 when the insured dies while the policy is active.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">The specific death benefit amount defined in the policy specifications is contingent upon fulfilling all policy terms, including timely premium payments and correct claim submission processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit specified in the policy may be reduced by unpaid premiums at time of claim, meaning the initial amount set forth in the specifications is subject to deduction based on outstanding obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that the death benefit is defined in the Policy Specifications, and fact_sentence_2 clarifies that this amount corresponds exactly to the Face Amount stated therein, confirming consistency across documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy cannot be paid until the insurer receives official proof of the insured's death, ensuring accurate and authorized disbursement based on documented evidence.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit specified in the policy is adjusted downward by any outstanding indebtedness when payouts occur, ensuring the insurer recoups prior loans or advances before releasing proceeds.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy must be paid only after submission of a certified death certificate, ensuring verification before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="7b26fed4-7c69-4d32-aa07-45ab4d3be614">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount is fixed per policy terms, but its payout may depend on submitting supplementary documents to verify eligibility or resolve discrepancies.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="9a3ebe6d-6903-418b-acd4-b78709d3f595">
  <data key="d3">The specified death benefit depends on verified circumstances of death, requiring the insurer’s investigation to confirm entitlement before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="6b2f5e21-9f40-4e43-859c-578858c6f470">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy may be challenged by the insurer if the claim arises during the contestability period due to material misrepresentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy determines the lump-sum payment made upon the insured's death, linking the stated value directly to the payout mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy directly determines the value eligible for the alternate payment option chosen by the beneficiary after the insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount is predetermined per policy terms, and an alternate payment method can be chosen before death, allowing customization of how the fixed benefit is delivered.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">The specified death benefit amount from the policy terms directly determines what will be paid out once the claims process is complete, ensuring clarity in the financial obligation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount is formally set in the policy, and interest begins accruing from the date of death onward, increasing the final payout above the nominal benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="1fa01fa6-dfb3-4343-85a2-88951da5f49b">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy determines what is available for disbursement, including cases where the primary beneficiary predeceases the insured. Thus, the fixed payout amount informs the financial scope of distributions to contingent beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in the policy governs what is paid out, and fact_sentence_2 clarifies how those funds are distributed among beneficiaries or the estate when primary ones do not survive the insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
