  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">role</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="9577dfed-8374-4c87-ba07-8e98f49c6af3">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">role</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="54f45c38-e6fc-47bc-a98a-94234f1c6c1b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">condition</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="94241359-1b4b-4090-a80a-fbfd0ae415c5">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">status</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="8e24a7b7-8932-4e44-ae56-f7142058bc75">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">action</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 states that regular premium payments are necessary to keep the policy active. Fact sentence 1 clarifies that if the insured dies while the policy is in force, the stated death benefit will be paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Premiums must be paid to sustain the policy’s validity; however, a 31-day grace period allows continued coverage even if payment is not made on time.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the required premium results in the policy entering a grace period; if unpaid beyond that window, it leads directly to lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">Premium payments are necessary to prevent a policy from lapsing, and if it does lapse, reinstatement becomes possible through specific procedures defined by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">Payment of premiums maintains the policy's active status, enabling the start of the incontestability period after two years. Without consistent premium payments, the policy could lapse before this period begins.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums ensures the policy remains active under the terms outlined in the full contract, which encompasses the policy, application, and related documents.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums ensures ongoing policy validity, but only if all prior representations were accurate; otherwise, any misstatement could invalidate the policy despite continued premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums to keep the policy active is upheld because no intermediary can override or waive this condition, preserving the formal agreement's enforceability.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums to keep the policy active is reinforced by restricting any individual from unilaterally extending payment deadlines, preserving the insurer's control over terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is adjusted according to the premium actually paid if the insured’s age was incorrectly reported. This adjustment ensures fairness by reflecting what the original premium could have secured had the true age been disclosed.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The amount of the death benefit is adjusted if the insured's sex was incorrectly stated, based on the premium actually paid. Since the premium determines coverage level, its role is central to recalculating benefits when demographic data is inaccurate.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums ensures ongoing policy validity, and any overpayment arising from a corrected age misstatement triggers a refund process by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="bff67a86-bdb2-4ccc-9c13-8e25d42f6ad3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums establishes the basis for potential overpayments due to misstatements. If a misstatement of sex causes higher-than-accurate premiums to be collected, the insurer must refund any surplus.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums ensures ongoing coverage; if a misstated age causes lower-than-required premiums, the insurer adjusts the death benefit downward to reflect the shortfall.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums ensures ongoing policy validity, and any shortfall due to a misstated sex triggers a proportional reduction in the death benefit to reflect underpayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f">
  <data key="d3">Failure to meet the insurable age criteria renders the policy void regardless of premium payments. Thus, even if premiums are paid, the policy lacks legal foundation if issued outside acceptable age limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">voids if outside age range</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d">
  <data key="d3">Premium payment is required to keep the policy active; however, if the insured does not fall within the acceptable age range at issuance, the insurer must refund all premiums paid because the policy is considered voidable due to misrepresentation or ineligible status.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional reversal</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay the premium to maintain the policy in force makes the 31-day grace period a crucial buffer against lapse due to missed payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="c80d6a5f-8ecf-4513-841a-708102ad7bc0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 gives a general definition of the premium's purpose, which directly supports and contextualizes the specific instance described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="7363bacb-3824-48b8-b24a-eb9aac000329">
  <data key="d3">Premium payments sustain the policy's existence, enabling the promised face amount to be paid at death, assuming all terms are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216">
  <data key="d3">Without consistent premium payments, the policy may lapse, preventing the beneficiary from receiving the death benefit even if properly designated.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75" target="8bede6b4-c4a3-430e-b23d-f9f00ea119d7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 emphasizes the necessity of paying the premium to sustain the policy, which aligns directly with fact_sentence_1’s assertion that the premium is a foundational element of the official policy package.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
