<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="4bd0c6c6-6ef5-460a-a8c1-b51fff060101">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">action</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period allows the policyholder to avoid losing coverage, thereby preserving the right to receive the death benefit outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">A 31-day grace period ensures that failure to timely pay the required premium does not immediately terminate coverage, preserving the policy's enforceability under its terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provides a 31-day window post-premium due date during which the policy stays active. If the premium isn't paid by the end of this period, the policy terminates, leading to a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">If the premium is not paid within the 31-day Grace Period, the policy lapses, triggering the necessity for Reinstatement to regain active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows continued coverage for 31 days past the due date, but its enforcement depends on official policy rules rather than agent discretion.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 offers a universal definition of a grace period, which helps clarify and validate the specific instance described in fact_sentence_1 regarding the 31-day allowance on Jordan Ellis’s policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="c80d6a5f-8ecf-4513-841a-708102ad7bc0">
  <data key="d3">The grace period exists specifically to support the ongoing obligation of paying premiums, enabling policyholders to maintain coverage beyond the due date until the next payment is made.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="7363bacb-3824-48b8-b24a-eb9aac000329">
  <data key="d3">The grace period enables ongoing protection for the face amount, ensuring beneficiaries receive the stated death benefit unless the policy lapses beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216">
  <data key="d3">A clearly designated beneficiary depends on the policy remaining in force, which is maintained through mechanisms like the 31-day grace period described in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="8bede6b4-c4a3-430e-b23d-f9f00ea119d7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes the grace period's role in maintaining policy validity post-premium due date. This directly aligns with fact_sentence_1, which lists the grace period among the legally binding parts of the policy agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows continued coverage despite late payment, but failure to pay within it results in immediate policy lapse, making the duration of the grace period crucial to maintaining validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage beyond the due date, delaying the termination of benefits until its expiration, thereby making it a prerequisite condition before the policy lapses and coverage ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums without losing coverage, preventing automatic lapse and thus maintaining eligibility for benefits unless reinstatement occurs later.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows time to pay a missed premium before the policy lapses, creating the condition under which reinstatement may later become necessary through a formal request.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows continued coverage after a missed premium, preventing automatic lapse; if unpaid during this time, the policy lapses but remains eligible for reinstatement up to five years later.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provides temporary protection after a missed premium payment, preventing immediate lapse; however, if the policy lapses beyond this period, reinstatement—including submission of evidence of insurability—becomes required to restore coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows temporary continuation of coverage after missed premiums, enabling reinstatement later only if overdue amounts—including interest—are paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">The grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums before the policy lapses, making reinstatement feasible. Without it, there would be no opportunity to restore coverage under the terms described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage beyond the due date, allowing the death benefit to remain applicable even if a premium is late, provided the claim occurs before lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continuous coverage beyond the premium due date, allowing the death benefit to be payable even if a premium is delayed, thus supporting the fulfillment of the obligation described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">The grace period provides temporary protection allowing delayed premium payment, but any unpaid amounts still reduce the final death benefit when claimed.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">The grace period preserves policy status so that the death benefit remains payable if the insured passes away during this interval, ensuring continuity of coverage tied to the stated face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">The grace period preserves policyholder protection by maintaining coverage temporarily after missed payments, enabling the insurer to process death benefits upon receipt of required proof of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures ongoing coverage even after missing a premium, preventing immediate lapse and allowing time to pay dues before indebtedness accrues. This directly influences whether the death benefit will later be reduced by unpaid amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage beyond the due date, allowing time for late premium payments before lapse; however, if a death occurs during this phase, timely submission of a certified death certificate is still necessary to process the claim properly.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="7b26fed4-7c69-4d32-aa07-45ab4d3be614">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage despite late payment, and the requirement for additional documentation may arise when verifying circumstances during or leading into this period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="9a3ebe6d-6903-418b-acd4-b78709d3f595">
  <data key="d3">The grace period maintains policy validity long enough for the insurer to exercise its right to investigate the cause of death should the insured die during this interval.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables investigation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage until renewal, enabling the insurer to honor the death benefit payout, including the default lump-sum provision when the insured passes during this window.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage until renewal, enabling the policyholder to avoid lapse before death occurs, thus allowing the beneficiary to access payout options upon the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage despite delayed payment, providing time to utilize alternative payment options like those mentioned in fact_sentence_2. This allows the policyholder more flexibility in fulfilling obligations before lapse occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures ongoing policy coverage, allowing the insurer to fulfill its obligation to pay the death benefit if the insured dies before the next premium is paid. Without the grace period, the policy might lapse prematurely, potentially preventing a claim from being processed.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage despite late premiums, enabling the insurer to later pay the death benefit with accrued interest upon claim submission.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="1fa01fa6-dfb3-4343-85a2-88951da5f49b">
  <data key="d3">The grace period preserves policy validity, ensuring that if the insured dies during this time, the death benefit can still be claimed by the named beneficiaries, including contingents, under the terms outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage despite late premiums, enabling the policy to remain active so that death benefits can be paid according to beneficiary designations outlined later in the process.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ebf2226-8e5a-4c64-9692-76a37418cb96" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has grace period after due date</data>
</edge>
<edge source="547ab600-f687-4a48-9811-5099dc7bd04d" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">prevented by grace period</data>
</edge>
