  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">status</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="c75d36ec-0023-4962-8164-c9fe94dd2eb6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">action</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">A policy may lapse if the required premium is not paid within the grace period, underscoring the necessity of timely premium payments to sustain coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="4c33d125-939d-4a32-9967-049926703be9">
  <data key="d3">If premiums remain unpaid past the grace period on a Policy Anniversary, the policy may lapse, terminating coverage unless reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse occurs when the premium remains unpaid past the 31-day grace period. This outcome directly depends on the existence of the grace period, which serves as a buffer before cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment after the grace period, it becomes inactive. Reinstatement allows the policyholder to bring the lapsed policy back into force under specified conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3">
  <data key="d3">The definition of lapse depends on the absence of extended payment deadlines; if agents could extend payment times, lapses might not occur even after the grace period ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">The definition of lapse highlights a key risk point in policy maintenance, emphasizing why strict rules on alterations are necessary to preserve contractual integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">A lapse occurs precisely when a premium remains unpaid beyond the 31-day grace period specified in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="c80d6a5f-8ecf-4513-841a-708102ad7bc0">
  <data key="d3">A lapse, as defined in fact_sentence_2, occurs when the required premium payment (defined in fact_sentence_1) is not made within the allowed grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="7363bacb-3824-48b8-b24a-eb9aac000329">
  <data key="d3">A lapse occurs when premiums are not paid even during the grace period, thereby preventing the payout of the face amount specified in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216">
  <data key="d3">A lapse invalidates the policy’s ability to deliver the death benefit, thereby negating the purpose of designating a beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="8bede6b4-c4a3-430e-b23d-f9f00ea119d7">
  <data key="d3">The second statement clarifies a potential outcome tied to a component explicitly listed in the first statement: failure to meet premium payment requirements results in policy lapse, affecting the enforceability of the entire agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines what constitutes a policy lapse due to missed premiums, and fact_sentence_2 elaborates by specifying when the lapse occurs—on the due date of the unpaid premium—thereby clarifying the timing mechanism described in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The first statement explains that lapse occurs due to nonpayment beyond the grace period, which directly supports the second statement that coverage terminates under those circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">The definition of lapse provides the foundational condition under which reinstatement becomes necessary, establishing the temporal and procedural trigger for the actions outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">The definition of lapse in fact_sentence_1 explains when coverage ends, justifying why benefits are unavailable per fact_sentence_2 unless reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">The definition of lapse in fact_sentence_1 establishes the condition that triggers the potential for reinstatement described in fact_sentence_2, creating a temporal and procedural link between policy termination and recovery.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">The termination of a policy due to nonpayment (lapse) creates the condition requiring reinstatement, which depends on submitting acceptable evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">The occurrence of a lapse due to missed premiums creates the scenario necessitating reinstatement, allowing coverage to resume seamlessly as if uninterrupted.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">The termination of a policy due to nonpayment (lapse) necessitates reinstatement, which requires repayment of overdue premiums plus interest as stipulated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse invalidates coverage, preventing the death benefit from being payable unless reinstated. Therefore, the existence of the death benefit depends on avoiding lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse terminates coverage, preventing the death benefit from being paid even if the insured dies during the term. Therefore, maintaining the policy’s active status by avoiding lapse is essential for triggering the payout described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse ends coverage due to unpaid premiums, meaning the death benefit defined by the face amount cannot be claimed upon the insured's death during the lapsed period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment after the grace period, any unpaid premiums may still affect the final death benefit, reducing it when a claim is made.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse terminates coverage due to unpaid premiums, but the insurer still owes a death benefit if the insured dies while the policy was active, provided proper proof of death is submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy results in no death benefit payout, whereas if the policy remains active, any indebtedness reduces the payable death benefit. This creates a conditional dependency where debt deduction only applies when the policy has not lapsed.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse prevents the payout of death benefits, meaning that even if a certified death certificate is provided, no claim can proceed if the policy has lapsed and not been reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="9a3ebe6d-6903-418b-acd4-b78709d3f595">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse terminates coverage, preventing any future claims and thereby eliminating the need for the insurer to investigate the cause of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6">
  <data key="d3">The lapse condition arises from nonpayment despite available alternatives, suggesting that electing an alternative payment method could prevent policy termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="6b2f5e21-9f40-4e43-859c-578858c6f470">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse occurring after the grace period terminates coverage, potentially affecting whether a claim is eligible for contestation under the contestability clause, especially if the death occurs shortly after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy prevents the beneficiary from accessing any benefits, including alternative payment options, meaning the ability described in fact_sentence_2 depends on the policy remaining in force beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">The occurrence of a lapse due to missed premiums prevents the death benefit from being payable, making it crucial that policies remain active. Therefore, ensuring timely payments avoids lapse and enables prompt processing of benefits per the stated procedure.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">The lapse condition determines whether the policy remains active to trigger death benefit payouts, including those accruing interest after death. If the policy has lapsed, no death benefit—including accrued interest—is payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">The occurrence of a lapse invalidates the policy’s ability to pay death benefits, making it conditional on maintaining active status through timely premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse terminates coverage, preventing any future benefit payouts regardless of beneficiary designations. If the policy has lapsed, the contingency described in fact_sentence_2 would not apply because there would be no active policy to trigger a death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c" target="1fa01fa6-dfb3-4343-85a2-88951da5f49b">
  <data key="d3">The lapse of a policy due to nonpayment ends coverage before death, potentially affecting whether benefits are payable to a beneficiary. This contrasts with the scenario where the insured dies while covered, triggering payout rules based on beneficiary designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a66f9006-b140-44ec-b77d-0967a8632ec4" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">nonpayment causes</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ad63686-7c96-41eb-b2d9-ecf17bb21b5a" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">expiration triggers</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d19daafd-4a52-4334-ada9-7e7f8e83dbba" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is result of</data>
</edge>
<edge source="55616571-2a98-40a0-a5a0-a017b3320125" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">can follow</data>
</edge>
