  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">status</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="366d72cb-0972-4f57-adda-eceadfdfd6a8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">action</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to missed premium payments, reinstatement allows restoration of coverage, contingent upon fulfilling requirements including back-payment of premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires premium payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement becomes applicable only after a lapse occurs, typically resulting from failure to pay premiums within the Grace Period.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of reinstating a lapsed policy depends on the occurrence of a lapse caused by failure to pay premiums after the grace period has expired.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores a lapsed policy to active status, but only if it remains part of the legally binding contract defined by the policy documents. The existence of reinstatement rights depends on the formal definition of the contract itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores a lapsed policy, potentially requiring official documentation and approvals. Any such restoration would need written authorization from a company executive officer per contractual rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires approval</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement applies when a policy lapses due to missed payments, but only if formal procedures are followed; however, no one can unilaterally extend the deadline for paying premiums, making timely payment crucial before reinstatement attempts.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement cannot occur if the policy was void ab initio due to being issued outside the insurable age range; thus, the concept of restoration is irrelevant under such circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">voids reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="a68f05ee-b6c2-4a27-be1f-bfafeddf4b0c">
  <data key="d3">The definition of reinstatement in fact_sentence_1 establishes the foundation for fact_sentence_2, which describes a key consequence: the initiation of a new contestability period after reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="e9992b58-f0cb-4309-aa8b-99ccf5ca595c">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores the policy’s active status, triggering renewed applicability of the suicide exclusion clause effective from the reinstatement date.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement revives the policy’s validity, but it does not retroactively cover events that occurred during the lapse; therefore, claims from the lapse period remain ineligible despite restoration.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores a lapsed policy’s original terms, while conversion provides an option to switch to permanent coverage without medical underwriting; these processes may serve similar goals but operate through different pathways.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="be5d9596-fd48-4642-93c3-1033cc1a3da6">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores a lapsed policy, whereas conversion enables switching to permanent coverage before expiry—both provide pathways to maintain protection, though at different stages.</data>
  <data key="d4">alternative path</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="6b3c39b6-2af6-4210-bf69-47e128370b19">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy depends on fulfilling ongoing premium obligations under the chosen product's terms, making timely payment a prerequisite for restoration.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="cf26351d-1aa6-446d-8320-a1b56d723009">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement depends on meeting age-related requirements; specifically, the insured must not exceed the company's maximum conversion age when requesting restoration of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="0c4d1411-9c02-4d7d-ae5c-767cd2ba2497">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores a lapsed policy’s validity, potentially enabling future conversion opportunities if done before expiration of the conversion period. However, conversion cannot occur unless initiated within the designated timeframe regardless of reinstatement status.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement depends on timely action during or shortly after the grace period ends, meaning the 31-day grace period sets the window within which reinstatement may still be possible.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="c80d6a5f-8ecf-4513-841a-708102ad7bc0">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy depends on fulfilling conditions including paying overdue premiums, often tied to the original definition of premium obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="7363bacb-3824-48b8-b24a-eb9aac000329">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement depends on the existence of a clearly defined face amount, as the restored policy must reinstate the same death benefit previously agreed upon at issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses, reinstatement restores its functionality, enabling the originally named beneficiary to still receive the death benefit as intended at inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="8bede6b4-c4a3-430e-b23d-f9f00ea119d7">
  <data key="d3">The concept of reinstating a lapsed policy presupposes the presence of official policy components—including applications, endorsements, and declarations—as detailed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">The inability to pay a premium by the end of the grace period results in policy lapse, creating the scenario where reinstatement becomes necessary to restore coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy enables the resumption of benefit entitlements after a lapse, directly addressing the restriction stated in fact_sentence_2 regarding non-payment of benefits during lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment, coverage ends, but it may be restored through reinstatement by meeting specific criteria such as proving insurability and paying back premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes reinstatement as a defined process, while fact_sentence_2 provides a key constraint—reinstatement must occur within five years of lapse—which operationalizes the abstract definition.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes reinstatement as a restoration process, while fact_sentence_2 specifies that a written request is required to begin this process, showing procedural implementation of the concept.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement requires payment of overdue premiums with interest, making this financial obligation a key component of restoring a lapsed policy's active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires submitting acceptable evidence of insurability, which serves as a conditional requirement for restoring the policy’s active status as defined in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores the policy’s active status, enabling coverage to resume retroactively as if there were no interruption.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement ensures the policy remains active, which is necessary for the death benefit to apply. Without reinstatement after a lapse, the death benefit would not be payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement ensures the policy remains eligible for death benefit payouts by reactivating coverage after a lapse, thereby enabling the scenario described in fact_sentence_2 where the insurer pays the beneficiary upon the insured's death during the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement process requires repayment of unpaid premiums, directly tying it to the rule that such premiums are deducted from the death benefit upon claim settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement preserves the policy’s active status, ensuring the death benefit remains available when the insured passes away. Without reinstatement, the death benefit would not be payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">The reinstatement of a lapsed policy involves paying overdue premiums and interest, which constitute indebtedness that reduces the eventual death benefit when the insured passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy ensures continued coverage, which allows the insurer to pay the death benefit when the insured passes away—but only after receiving official proof of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables claim</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="7b26fed4-7c69-4d32-aa07-45ab4d3be614">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for additional documentation ensures that insurers can verify insurability and financial obligations during reinstatement, supporting the process defined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="9a3ebe6d-6903-418b-acd4-b78709d3f595">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy enables continued coverage, making the insurer’s right to investigate the cause of death applicable should the insured die afterward. This ensures legitimacy before payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="6b2f5e21-9f40-4e43-859c-578858c6f470">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy restores its active status, enabling the insurer to exercise its right to contest claims during the applicable contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement ensures ongoing coverage so that death benefit proceeds may be payable upon the insured’s passing, making it foundational for triggering the lump-sum payout described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6">
  <data key="d3">The ability to elect an alternative payment option may help prevent policy lapse, thereby reducing reliance on reinstatement after termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement preserves the policy’s validity so it can fulfill obligations like paying the death benefit upon the insured's passing, ensuring the claim process applies only to currently effective policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement ensures the policy remains active so that upon the insured’s death, the beneficiary may receive proceeds via standard or alternative payment options. Without reinstatement, the policy would remain inactive, potentially voiding any future benefit disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement involves paying overdue premiums plus interest, which aligns with the broader principle that interest applies when delays occur in financial obligations related to policies. However, the interest in reinstatement pertains to past-due premiums, whereas the interest mentioned here applies specifically to death benefits post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement of a lapsed policy depends on charging interest on overdue premiums, which must comply with state-mandated minimum rates to remain legally valid.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="1fa01fa6-dfb3-4343-85a2-88951da5f49b">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement ensures ongoing policy validity so that death benefits remain payable, which enables the contingency plan described in fact_sentence_2 regarding beneficiary payouts. Without reinstatement, the policy would not be active at time of death, potentially invalidating beneficiary designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores a lapsed policy’s validity, enabling future benefits to be distributed according to beneficiary designations, including contingents, should the insured die afterward.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="104000dd-74a7-419f-a594-d7571eb60c37" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">triggered by</data>
</edge>
