<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period ensures that after two years, the insurer cannot contest the policy’s validity, thereby protecting the insured’s right to receive the death benefit as defined in the policy specifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">The existence of the incontestability period depends on the policy remaining in force long enough, which requires continuous premium payments by the owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="4c33d125-939d-4a32-9967-049926703be9">
  <data key="d3">The Incontestability Period starts at the policy’s issue date and ends two years later, establishing a legal timeframe where the insurer cannot challenge the policy’s validity. Since the Policy Anniversary occurs annually from the same issue date, it serves as a periodic landmark within the duration of the incontestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">temporal context</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="b0682bc0-a0b2-4059-b458-c16bdb0d9fb4">
  <data key="d3">The Incontestability Period ensures the policy cannot be challenged after two years, indirectly supporting the rationale behind limiting benefits during the Suicide Exclusion Period, which also applies within the initial two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period depends on whether prior statements were treated as representations, ensuring insurers cannot later dispute claims based on misrepresentations after two years, assuming no fraud was involved.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period limits when the company can dispute the policy’s validity, but its effectiveness depends on whether all relevant information was accurately recorded in the written application.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period limits when the company can challenge the policy’s validity; having the written application attached ensures those prior statements are available for review if contested.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period sets a timeframe within which the insurer can question the policy’s validity due to misrepresentation, ensuring claims cannot be contested after two years. This supports the broader principle stated in fact_sentence_2—that only formal, written changes can affect the policy, preserving its enforceability against informal actions by agents.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period limits when insurers can challenge policy validity due to misrepresentation, including age errors. This sets the stage for how misstatements affect benefits, such as adjusting the death benefit based on corrected age.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period allows the insurer to verify accuracy of information at policy inception; if a misstatement of age is discovered during this window, it triggers corrective actions including possible premium refunds.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period defines when insurers can act upon misstatements; if a misstatement of age is discovered within this window, it triggers recalculations affecting the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period sets the timeframe during which insurers can investigate and act upon misstatements like incorrect sex reporting. After this period ends, any misstatement becomes legally unchallengeable, meaning benefits are adjusted per corrected terms only if discovered before expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period allows the company to verify claims related to misstatements, including those involving gender. This verification directly affects the calculation of adjusted death benefits when inaccuracies lead to underpayments.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period limits when the company can challenge policy validity, but it doesn't override fundamental eligibility requirements like being within the insurable age range, which alone renders the policy void from inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">The first fact defines the standard two-year incontestability window post-issue; the second clarifies that this window resets upon policy reinstatement, ensuring continuity of the insurer’s right to challenge validity even after revival.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50">
  <data key="d3">The initial incontestability period sets baseline rules for contesting policy validity, while the second fact clarifies that reinstating a lapsed policy triggers a new two-year window focused solely on representations made during reinstitution.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="e8364bc1-ea45-49ba-a605-1c2c3dd2dd6c">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period sets a foundational timeframe for challenging policy validity, and its reactivation at reinstatement ensures ongoing scrutiny; thus, the second fact extends the first’s logic into post-lapse scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="c8a217fc-b379-48eb-80d2-edc84b27f3c5">
  <data key="d3">The initial incontestability period defined in fact_sentence_1 is reset when a policy is reinstated, meaning the two-year window for challenging the policy's validity restarts from the reinstatement date, as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="a68f05ee-b6c2-4a27-be1f-bfafeddf4b0c">
  <data key="d3">The first statement defines the original incontestability window, while the second clarifies that this window restarts upon policy reinstatement, ensuring ongoing scrutiny applies even after revival.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7" target="e9992b58-f0cb-4309-aa8b-99ccf5ca595c">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability period sets a foundational timeframe for claim challenges; when a policy is reinstated, this period resets, restarting conditions like the suicide exclusion, thereby linking the first fact to the second through procedural renewal mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
