<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">Statements made by the insured are considered representations—not guarantees—which limits the insurer’s ability to void coverage, especially once the two-year incontestability period has passed.</data>
  <data key="d4">underpins</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">Statements made by the insured or owner being considered representations (not warranties) reinforces the importance of the documented contract defined in fact_sentence_1, ensuring clarity on liability and enforcement when discrepancies arise.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs contract scope</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">Statements made by the insured or policy owner are treated as representations rather than binding warranties, but they cannot serve as grounds for denying a claim unless explicitly recorded in the formal written application.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8">
  <data key="d3">The status of statements as representations rather than warranties depends on them being formally documented in a written application attached to the policy, ensuring they can be used defensively in claims disputes.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">Statements made by the insured or policy owner are treated as non-binding representations, which strengthens the rationale behind restricting agents from altering policy terms, since informal assurances do not override official contract language.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">Statements made by the insured are treated as representations, meaning they do not create absolute guarantees but may affect benefits if inaccurate. Consequently, if the insured's age was misrepresented, the death benefit adjusts accordingly to reflect what could have been purchased at the true age.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence defines that statements from the insured are representations, meaning they carry less weight than warranties but still affect contractual outcomes if false. The second sentence uses this concept to determine how a misstatement of sex impacts the death benefit calculation.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="bff67a86-bdb2-4ccc-9c13-8e25d42f6ad3">
  <data key="d3">Statements made by the insured or policy owner are considered representations rather than guarantees, meaning they do not create absolute obligations but may trigger corrections upon discovery. This framework enables the insurer to adjust benefits or premiums based on factual inaccuracies, including returning any overpaid amounts due to misstated gender.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d3">The statement that declarations are representations (not warranties) enables the insurer to adjust benefits upon discovery of misstatements, such as inaccurate age reporting, leading to proportional reductions in the death benefit if premiums were underpaid.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7">
  <data key="d3">The statement that declarations are representations—not warranties—sets the stage for understanding how inaccuracies, such as misstated age, affect liability and benefits. In turn, if a misstatement causes overpayment of premiums, the insurer agrees to refund the surplus, reflecting a fair adjustment based on representation-based corrections.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82">
  <data key="d3">The classification of statements as representations rather than warranties means that errors like misstating sex do not invalidate the entire policy but may trigger adjustments. Consequently, when a misstatement of sex leads to lower premiums, the death benefit is proportionally reduced.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f" target="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f">
  <data key="d3">Statements made by the insured are considered representations rather than warranties, meaning inaccuracies may lead to consequences only under certain conditions. If those representations include false claims about age placing the individual outside the insurable range, the policy becomes void from inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bf5ae6ee-a0db-49c5-90c3-acd87b1f7579" target="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
</edge>
