  <data key="d4">condition</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="d7734894-a026-42ed-9322-03bd71513786">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">status</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="38742120-d7f8-41ae-b5f6-09b1752b7c8e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">action</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Only information explicitly included in the written application may serve as grounds for assessing or defending the payment of the death benefit outlined in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">Accurate statements in the written application are necessary to support the legitimacy of premium payments and prevent denial of benefits, ensuring that financial obligations align with lawful policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">Only statements in the written application can serve as grounds for denying a claim, ensuring that the incontestability period applies consistently based on documented disclosures.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="b0682bc0-a0b2-4059-b458-c16bdb0d9fb4">
  <data key="d3">Only information explicitly stated in the written application can be used to defend against a claim, meaning any details related to suicidal intent during the two-year exclusion period would need to have been formally recorded beforehand.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 enforces the authority of the written application—defined as part of the total contract in fact_sentence_1—by ensuring claims cannot rely on unwritten statements, thereby preserving the boundaries established in the primary clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f">
  <data key="d3">Only statements included in the written application may be invoked during claim disputes; therefore, informal or unrecorded representations lack legal standing despite being acknowledged as non-warranties.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits use</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the principle that only written application content may defend a claim; fact_sentence_2 clarifies that this requires the actual copy of the application to be physically attached to the policy for admissibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 ensures that any defense against a claim must originate from the documented application, aligning with the broader requirement in fact_sentence_2 that all policy changes require explicit written authorization, thus maintaining consistent and verifiable recordkeeping across claims and modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes that only written statements in the application can serve as legal grounds for denying claims, reinforcing the need for documentation. This supports fact sentence 2 by emphasizing that any deviation from official procedures—including extending payment deadlines—is invalid if not formally recorded.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that only written statements in the application can serve as legal grounds for denying claims, reinforcing the need for documented evidence. This supports fact_sentence_2’s assertion that no personnel have unilateral power to change policy terms, ensuring consistency between official records and enforceable conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that only written application statements may be used in defense ensures that any misstatement of age is based on documented data, enabling accurate recalculations of the death benefit according to the correct age.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The rule that only written application statements may defend claims ensures that any misstatement regarding sex is formally documented. This enables the proportional adjustment of the death benefit according to the correct sex, as specified in the application.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that only written application statements may defend claims ensures accuracy in initial submissions. This supports the enforcement of corrective actions, such as refunding overpaid premiums when a misstatement of age results in higher-than-required payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that defenses rely solely on the written application ensures that any corrections due to misstatements—like those affecting premiums and benefits—are based on documented applicant disclosures.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that only written application statements may defend claims ensures that any corrections due to misstatements—like gender—are grounded in documented records. This supports the adjustment of benefits when inaccuracies affect premium calculations.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="bff67a86-bdb2-4ccc-9c13-8e25d42f6ad3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that only written application statements may serve as defenses sets the foundation for holding insurers accountable when misstatements occur. This supports the enforcement of refund obligations when corrections arise from inaccuracies like misreported sex.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional supports</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4" target="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that only written application statements may defend claims ensures that inaccuracies in age or other details are subject to scrutiny. If the applicant misrepresented age and fell outside the insurable range, the policy’s invalidity from the start follows directly from those unverified assertions.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3549ac2e-3841-43a5-b57a-b9ead014d7d6" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is governed by</data>
</edge>
