  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">status</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="55abba85-9e24-4934-a00f-35d84863d74e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">action</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">To enforce the incontestability clause effectively, the written application must be physically part of the policy file so its contents can be used in legal disputes over coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">For the application’s content to be considered admissible in claim defenses, it must be formally incorporated into the policy through physical attachment—a condition directly tied to the comprehensive nature of the contract defined earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f">
  <data key="d3">For a statement to serve as a basis in claim defense, it must first qualify as a representation under the policy’s terms—meaning it must have been made by the insured or policyowner and lack fraudulent intent.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">The necessity of attaching a copy of the application (fact_sentence_2) ensures compliance with the rule that only application statements can be used defensively (fact_sentence_1).</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes that only when the application is physically attached can its contents support claims defenses. This supports the broader requirement in fact sentence 2 that all policy changes require written approval, ensuring consistency in documented proof across the entire contractual lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to attach the written application ensures that only formally documented information can support or defend claims, aligning with the rule that no one can unilaterally change policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to attach the written application ensures documentation integrity for verifying claims-related statements. This supports accurate assessment when adjusting benefits due to misstated age, but does not determine how adjustments are calculated.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to attach the application ensures that any misstatement, such as incorrect gender, can be verified and used to adjust benefits accordingly. This enables fair recalibration of the death benefit based on corrected demographic information.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to attach the application ensures verifiable records exist for evaluating misstatements, which enables accurate determination of whether premium overpayments occurred due to age errors, thus supporting potential refunds under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="bff67a86-bdb2-4ccc-9c13-8e25d42f6ad3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to attach the application ensures documentation integrity, enabling verification of misstatements like those concerning sex. This verified information supports the basis for calculating and issuing refunds when overpayments occur due to such errors.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8" target="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to attach the application ensures documentation supports claims-related defenses; if a misstatement of sex led to underpayment, the death benefit may be adjusted based on corrected terms. This adjustment depends on having proper records, including the original application.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="755e552a-04c7-48df-862c-649dcbf37874" target="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">includes</data>
</edge>
