</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Written approval from an executive officer is required before any adjustment to the death benefit amount outlined in the policy specifications can become effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The policy requires written executive approval for any change, including processes like reinstatement that restore a lapsed policy’s active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">Any proposed change to the policy must follow a formal process requiring written approval, as established by the comprehensive nature of the contract described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 mandates that all policy changes need written executive approval, supporting the principle in fact_sentence_1 that only formally recorded information—in this case, the application—can serve as a basis for legal actions, thereby preserving coherence between policy enforcement and documentation standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 enforces that no alterations to the policy are effective without written consent from an executive officer, reinforcing the necessity described in fact sentence 1—that documents like applications must be formally included to maintain evidentiary credibility during disputes.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes that written approval from an executive officer is required for any policy change. Fact sentence 2 supports this by clarifying that even lower-level personnel lack the authority to alter or waive provisions, reinforcing the need for formal, top-down authorization.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 ensures that any alteration to the policy requires official written consent, reinforcing the authority constraints outlined in fact_sentence_2, which prohibits agents from granting extensions on premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="34477494-c07a-4a94-8d5d-9ab2d18efa69">
  <data key="d3">While most policy changes require written executive approval, automatic integration of legally mandated reforms bypasses this step due to overriding jurisdictional authority.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="ce0fb1c9-347b-430e-a607-ea32da5c639f">
  <data key="d3">While the policy generally requires written executive approval for changes, automatic incorporation of statutory or regulatory mandates overrides this requirement when governed by law.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">The rule requiring written approval for modifications ensures that any official changes to policy terms—including those affecting benefits based on misstated information—are formally documented. This procedural safeguard supports the integrity of claims calculations, including adjusted death benefits when age was incorrectly reported.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written approval of modifications ensures that any correction to policy terms—including those arising from misstatements like gender—is formally validated. This maintains consistency with the provision that misstated information affects benefits proportionally.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written executive approval ensures proper authorization before any policy change takes effect. This formality supports accurate implementation of corrective actions, including refunds arising from corrected information like age misstatements.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written executive approval ensures that any adjustment to the policy—including those triggered by corrected information—is formally validated. This procedural safeguard helps maintain consistency before applying consequential changes like adjusting the death benefit due to misreported age.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 ensures only formally approved modifications affect the policy, which complements fact_sentence_2's mechanism allowing non-invalidated sections to persist when others fail legally.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written executive approval ensures that only formally sanctioned changes affect the policy, which supports the principle in fact_sentence_2 that undisturbed provisions remain effective under the law.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that policy modifications require written approval from an executive officer, which directly supports the requirement in fact_sentence_2 that waivers must also be signed by an authorized officer, ensuring consistency in enforcement procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 reinforces the binding nature of the policy’s terms by requiring written authorization for changes, which aligns with fact_sentence_2’s assertion that the policy represents the complete agreement between parties, thereby preserving its finality and integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
