<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is determined solely by official policy specs, it must remain unaltered by personnel who lack authority to change policy terms, preserving its accuracy and legitimacy.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on agents altering policy terms ensures that the financial responsibility defined in the premium clause remains strictly governed by the written contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against unauthorized changes ensures that lapses occur only according to defined terms, preventing arbitrary exceptions to payment requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition on agents altering policy provisions ensures that no unofficial modifications undermine the policy’s terms, including those related to the incontestability period. This reinforces the importance of the two-year window during which the company retains limited rights to dispute coverage based on initial representations.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="b0682bc0-a0b2-4059-b458-c16bdb0d9fb4">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against unilateral alterations ensures that exceptions like the suicide exclusion remain binding and unchanged unless formally approved.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on agents altering policy terms depends on the definition of the complete contract outlined earlier, making it contingent upon the formally established scope of the policy documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against agents modifying policy provisions ensures that even if they make verbal claims based on representations, those cannot supersede the formal agreement, preserving the distinction established in the prior statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 prevents agents or representatives from altering policy terms, thereby upholding the sanctity of written agreements. This directly enables fact_sentence_1's requirement that only content formally recorded in the application may be used defensively, maintaining control over interpretive authority.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8">
  <data key="d3">Since no representative may modify policy provisions, the written application's attachment becomes crucial to validate any factual assertions made during claims processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 states that no agent or representative may alter policy terms, which directly justifies why written executive approval—as stated in fact sentence 1—is necessary to ensure compliance and prevent unauthorized changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes that no agent may change policy terms; fact sentence 2 exemplifies this by specifying one particular type of alteration—extension of premium payment time—that remains unauthorized.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="34477494-c07a-4a94-8d5d-9ab2d18efa69">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence emphasizes that no individual can unilaterally amend the policy, ensuring control remains within official channels. The second sentence indicates that mandatory legal updates are applied regardless of internal procedures, reflecting a higher-order rule enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">supersedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against unilateral modifications ensures that adjustments due to misstatements, like those affecting the death benefit based on corrected age, follow proper procedures and remain binding through documented processes.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The rule prohibiting unauthorized alterations ensures that corrections due to misstatements—like incorrect gender—are handled strictly according to defined procedures rather than informal adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="bff67a86-bdb2-4ccc-9c13-8e25d42f6ad3">
  <data key="d3">The rule prohibiting unauthorized alterations ensures that corrections like premium refunds due to misstated sex follow official processes. This maintains consistency with the policy’s stated mechanisms for handling inaccuracies.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces procedure</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against unauthorized alterations ensures that policies cannot be adjusted based on misleading claims regarding age eligibility, preserving the validity of exclusion rules like being outside the insurable age range.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d3">The rule prohibiting unauthorized alterations ensures that corrections due to misstatements follow official procedures. This maintains consistency when adjusting benefits based on corrected data, including cases where underpaid premiums require a proportional reduction in the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against unauthorized alterations ensures that adjustments due to misstatements, such as those involving sex, follow official procedures and maintain fairness. This supports the enforcement of proportional reductions in benefits when needed.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d">
  <data key="d3">The prohibition against unauthorized alterations ensures that conditions like age-based eligibility cannot be overridden informally. This supports the rule that if the insured is ineligible due to age, premiums must be fully refunded per policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on altering policy provisions reinforces the principle of legal continuity described in fact_sentence_2, where invalid sections do not undermine the entire agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on altering policy provisions ensures that the "complete agreement" clause remains intact by preventing unauthorized changes, thereby preserving the finality of the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 enforces strict authorization requirements for changes, ensuring policy integrity; this supports the enforcement of remaining provisions described in fact_sentence_2, which preserves the policy's effectiveness when certain sections fail.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that no individual can alter policy provisions, which is reinforced by fact_sentence_2 specifying that even waivers require written approval from an authorized officer, ensuring consistency in enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
