<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Restrictions on extending premium deadlines ensure that policy terms—including those governing the death benefit—are not altered informally. Without such controls, premature adjustments could undermine the accuracy of the death benefit calculation.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">Restricting agents' authority to extend premium payment times ensures that the policyholder’s responsibility to pay remains strictly governed by the contract, maintaining the validity of ongoing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Agent authority limitations ensure that only formally documented procedures govern premium payments, maintaining the validity of the 31-day grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">The rule prohibiting extensions ensures that the grace period remains strictly enforced, directly enabling the condition described in the lapse clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents extension</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The inability to extend premium deadlines ensures that policies may lapse, necessitating reinstatement through official channels if coverage is to be restored.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">Sentence 2 enforces the principle from Sentence 1 by clarifying that only official written instruments can modify payment timelines, reinforcing the idea that the contract’s integrity depends on documented agreements.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 clarifies that no individual representative may alter premium due dates, preserving consistency in payment enforcement. This aligns with fact sentence 1’s requirement that only written applications hold legal weight, ensuring no verbal extensions undermine formal terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 limits agent power by disallowing extension of premium deadlines, thereby supporting the requirement in fact_sentence_1 that only authorized personnel may alter policy conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">underpins authority</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 highlights a concrete restriction on agents' powers—delaying premium payments—which directly supports the overarching rule in fact sentence 1 prohibiting any modification of policy provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on extending premium payment timelines underscores the need for formal, written agreements, supporting the claim that the policy itself represents the complete and final understanding between the parties.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on extending premium deadlines reinforces the need for formal, documented agreements; this aligns with the severability clause, which ensures that any invalidity in one term doesn’t undermine the entire policy’s enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on extending premium deadlines ensures compliance with contractual formality, which supports the broader clause preserving remaining provisions even if some become unenforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9272d1c-c4c9-4fe2-9b5a-f62140c4ffa3" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes limits on who can modify payment timelines, which is reinforced by fact_sentence_2’s assertion that only authorized officers may waive any policy term, including those related to premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
