  <data key="d4">condition</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="363a3698-619f-4352-bfae-1ddbb5ebe008">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">status</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="3d0fbdf8-d5db-4403-aa18-c876ebde1c2b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">action</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">An inaccurate age statement triggers a recalibration of the death benefit, ensuring it aligns with what could have been obtained had the true age been disclosed from the start, thus directly influencing how the originally specified benefit is applied.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">Accurate premium payments determine the extent of coverage; thus, any miscalculation in age affects the final death benefit relative to the premiums paid during the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">Misstating the insured’s age triggers a proportional adjustment to the death benefit, ensuring fair payout relative to actual premiums paid. This mechanism operates within the framework established by the incontestability clause, which governs when such adjustments become enforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">preceded by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">The rule governing adjusted death benefits due to age misstatement relies on the policy being legally constituted by the application and other documents, as specified in fact_sentence_1; thus, the adjustment mechanism only applies if those components form the binding agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f">
  <data key="d3">The rule that misstated age results in a proportional adjustment of the death benefit implies that prior statements regarding age were considered representations—not warranties—and thus subject to correction without invalidating the entire contract due to minor errors.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">Because the death benefit adjusts based on the correct age, the validity of using that corrected figure hinges on having the original age declaration recorded in the written application, making the application central to enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8">
  <data key="d3">Adjustment of the death benefit based on corrected age depends on having proper records; thus, the presence of the signed application is necessary to validate the correction process described in this clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba">
  <data key="d3">When the insured’s age is misrepresented, the death benefit adjusts according to what premiums would have bought at the true age—a provision governed by contractual rules subject to formal amendment via written consent, ensuring consistency with company policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy's rules regarding benefits after misstatement depend on maintaining the integrity of the contract, they rely on the rule that no individual may unilaterally change policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7">
  <data key="d3">When age is misstated, the death benefit adjusts to reflect coverage at the correct age. This may result in overpayment of premiums, triggering a refund of the excess amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 explains how a misstatement of the insured's age affects the death benefit by adjusting it according to what the premium could have bought at the correct age. This principle parallels the treatment of sex misstatements described in fact sentence 2, where benefits are recalculated based on the correct gender’s rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">parallel effects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the standard for adjusting the death benefit when age is misstated, using the correct-age equivalent purchase power. Fact_sentence_2 applies this rule explicitly to cases where correcting the age reveals insufficient premium payment, leading to a reduced benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 explains how misstating age affects the death benefit by adjusting it according to what the actual premium would have bought at the correct age. This sets a precedent applicable to other misstatements, including sex, where similar corrective mechanisms apply if underpayments occur due to inaccuracies.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="c80d6a5f-8ecf-4513-841a-708102ad7bc0">
  <data key="d3">A misstated age affects the death benefit, which relies on the initial premium rate set during underwriting—a key component explicitly mentioned in the first fact regarding premium obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="7363bacb-3824-48b8-b24a-eb9aac000329">
  <data key="d3">While the policy states a fixed face amount of $500,000, it also allows for adjustments to the death benefit based on accurate age, which implies the initial figure might not reflect the final payout if there was a prior misrepresentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 modifies the potential size of the death benefit based on accurate age information, which directly impacts the amount the beneficiary—defined in fact_sentence_1—will ultimately receive.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences amount</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="8bede6b4-c4a3-430e-b23d-f9f00ea119d7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains how discrepancies in applicant information—specifically age—affect payout amounts, reinforcing the importance of accurate data captured in official documents referenced in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">Misstatement of age may lead to inadequate premium payments, potentially causing policy lapse; thus, correcting age-related errors becomes relevant only if the policy is successfully reinstated before death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit adjustment due to age misstatement depends on the overall policy terms, including those governing claim payouts and contractual obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">If the insured's age was incorrectly reported, the death benefit paid upon qualifying death (as per fact_sentence_2) is reduced to reflect what the original premium could have purchased at the accurate age.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">When the insured’s age is incorrectly stated, the death benefit is recalculated based on the premium paid rather than the original face amount, which contradicts the usual rule that benefits equal the face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">The corrected death benefit amount from fact_sentence_1 applies only once the insurer receives verified proof of death as required by fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit adjusted due to age misstatement may still be reduced by any outstanding indebtedness, meaning the corrected benefit amount is further diminished by loans or unpaid charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The accuracy of the insured’s age affects the death benefit amount, which is determined after verifying the cause of death via documents like a certified death certificate.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">The reduction in death benefit due to age misstatement (fact_sentence_1) interacts with the deduction of unpaid premiums (fact_sentence_2), both contributing to a lower net payout. Together, these factors illustrate different ways the actual benefit received could differ from the nominal face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="9a3ebe6d-6903-418b-acd4-b78709d3f595">
  <data key="d3">The misstatement of age affects the payout amount, whereas the investigation into the cause of death ensures legitimacy before any payout occurs. These two processes serve complementary roles in validating and calculating benefits accurately.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="6b2f5e21-9f40-4e43-859c-578858c6f470">
  <data key="d3">Misstatement of age triggers a recalculated death benefit, but only if the insurer exercises its right to contest the claim during the contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">The accuracy of the death benefit amount, as affected by age misstatement, determines what is eligible for prompt payment once claims are processed.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
