  <data key="d3">A misstatement regarding the insured’s sex triggers a proportional reduction in the death benefit, aligning the payment with what premiums would have secured had the correct sex been reported initially.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">Incorrectly stating the sex affects the death benefit by scaling it according to what the same premium would have bought at the correct sex, meaning the original premium requirement remains foundational to determining revised payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement of the insured’s sex triggers a proportional adjustment of the death benefit based on what could have been purchased at the correct rate. This provision operates under the assumption that the error was made early enough to fall within the incontestability window, where claims might still be contested.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement of the insured’s sex triggers a proportional adjustment to the death benefit based on what could have been purchased at the correct sex, operating within the legally defined contract outlined earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement of the insured's sex triggers a proportional adjustment in the death benefit, reflecting the financial implications of inaccurate information; this outcome relies on the foundational rule that such statements are representations rather than binding warranties.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">When the sex of the insured is incorrectly stated, the death benefit is recalculated using premiums adjusted for the accurate sex; this correction relies on the application being the authoritative source, per the clause in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8">
  <data key="d3">When the insured's sex is incorrectly stated, the death benefit is adjusted using premiums calculated at the correct sex; this adjustment relies on having the original application on file to validate the error and support the correction.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement regarding the insured’s sex triggers a recalibration of the death benefit based on what could have been purchased at the correct rate, but such a recalibration requires official written authorization under the company’s policy amendment rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement regarding the insured's sex triggers a recalculated death benefit based on accurate rates, consistent with the requirement that all modifications require official documentation per the policy’s governing principles.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 describes the proportional adjustment of the death benefit when the insured’s sex was incorrectly stated, mirroring the mechanism outlined in fact sentence 1 for age misstatements. Both rules ensure equitable outcomes based on accurate demographic data used in pricing.</data>
  <data key="d4">parallel effects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="bff67a86-bdb2-4ccc-9c13-8e25d42f6ad3">
  <data key="d3">When the insured’s sex is incorrectly stated, the death benefit is recalculated based on the premium’s purchasing power at the correct sex. This recalculation may result in an overpayment of premiums, prompting a refund of the surplus by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is recalculated based on the correct sex using the actual premium paid; if this recalculation shows insufficient premiums were paid, the benefit is reduced accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 discusses how a misstated sex alters the death benefit by aligning it with the coverage obtainable at the correct sex. This concept parallels fact_sentence_2, where an underpaid premium due to age misstatement also triggers a reduction in benefits, reflecting a consistent principle across different types of misstatements.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement regarding the insured’s sex affects the final death benefit calculation, regardless of whether the policy remained active via the 31-day grace period. Thus, timely premium payment preserves coverage, but accurate information determines ultimate payout size.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="c80d6a5f-8ecf-4513-841a-708102ad7bc0">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement regarding the insured’s sex affects the death benefit, which could result in recalculating what the original premium should have covered had the correct information been provided, thereby impacting the validity and financial implications tied to maintaining the policy via premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="7363bacb-3824-48b8-b24a-eb9aac000329">
  <data key="d3">The definition of the face amount relies on accurate personal information; if the insured’s sex was misreported, the payment due upon death reflects the benefit equivalent to the premium paid at the proper sex rating rather than the initially quoted face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="49ede6cd-0ba5-4ff3-af79-5ed128947216">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount may be recalculated based on correct sex classification, potentially changing the sum received by the named beneficiary, Taylor Ellis.</data>
  <data key="d4">affects amount</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="8bede6b4-c4a3-430e-b23d-f9f00ea119d7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains a key consequence of inaccurate data entry during underwriting, specifically affecting the death benefit when sex is misrepresented. This rule operates within the framework described in fact_sentence_1, where the final policy outcome depends on the complete set of official documentation, including the original application and related endorsements.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit adjustment due to sex misstatement depends on the policy being active; if the policy has lapsed from nonpayment, the benefit may not be payable regardless of the correction.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement of the insured's sex alters the death benefit amount, but if the policy lapses due to related issues, benefits remain unpayable unless reinstated per the specified terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit adjustment due to misstated sex is one example of how the overall death benefit is subject to policy terms, illustrating a specific application of the general principle outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">example of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">If the insured's sex was incorrectly stated, the death benefit paid upon death during the policy term is adjusted downward based on the corrected sex, rather than paying the original face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional adjustment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">When the insured's sex is incorrectly stated, the death benefit deviates from the face amount specified in the policy, being adjusted based on the actual premium cost at the correct sex category.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies baseline</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit initially adjusted downward due to misstated sex is further reduced by any unpaid premiums before being disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount specified in fact_sentence_1 depends on verifying the insured's actual sex, which only becomes relevant after the insurer receives official proof of death per fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">The correction of a misstated sex adjusts the initial death benefit amount based on actuarial pricing, which may differ from the nominal face value. Any subsequent deduction for indebtedness occurs after this adjustment, meaning the reduced benefit due to misstatement is further diminished by outstanding loans or debts.</data>
  <data key="d4">affected by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The first fact influences the payout amount when there’s a misstatement of sex, whereas the second mandates evidence needed to initiate any payout. The two operate sequentially: once a corrected benefit amount is determined, proof of death is still required to trigger it.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="9a3ebe6d-6903-418b-acd4-b78709d3f595">
  <data key="d3">Misstatement of sex impacts the payout amount by recalculating it based on correct premium rates, whereas the company’s investigative rights ensure accurate determination of death causes before disbursement. These processes serve complementary roles in risk management and fraud prevention.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="6b2f5e21-9f40-4e43-859c-578858c6f470">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement of the insured's sex affects the death benefit calculation but also provides a basis for the insurer to contest the claim during the contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">The corrected death benefit amount determined by fact_sentence_1 becomes the basis for the prompt payment mandated by fact_sentence_2 once claim documents are verified.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">The first fact determines the base death benefit amount when there’s a misstatement of sex, while the second adds interest to that amount after death. The two together define the final payout: the adjusted benefit amount earns interest from the date of death onward.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7efdbb03-0a58-41b9-af2a-92525d7dd105" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is determined by</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78e8bde7-2c99-42ce-aa7f-7f2dfb780b66" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines</data>
</edge>
