  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">status</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="1aa6d53a-485a-4058-9258-1b0491916467">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">action</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Overpayment recovery based on corrected age relies on the originally defined death benefit amount in the policy specifications, ensuring accurate recalibration of benefits and premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">When premiums were incorrectly calculated due to a misrepresented age, the need to repay excess amounts stems from the initial obligation to make premium payments under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement of age leading to overpayment of premiums justifies a refund by the insurer only if the claim arises before the end of the incontestability period, ensuring timely resolution based on contractual terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">The provision allowing refund of overpaid premiums when age is corrected relies on the established scope of the contract detailed in fact_sentence_1, ensuring that only authorized documents govern such financial recalibrations.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f">
  <data key="d3">When a misstatement of age leads to excessive premium payments, the company returns the difference to the policyholder. This action stems from the principle established earlier—that such statements are treated as representations rather than binding guarantees, allowing adjustments without punitive measures when corrected.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">When a misstatement of age causes excessive premium payments, the company must issue a refund based on corrected calculations. This process relies on the original application being the authoritative source, reinforcing the rule that only documented statements in the application can govern claim-related decisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8">
  <data key="d3">Refunds for overpaid premiums arising from age misstatements depend on having proper documentation—such as the attached application—to validate the error and support the claim for reimbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba">
  <data key="d3">A refund of overpaid premiums occurs when a misstated age results in higher-than-required payments; this resolution depends on official validation and documentation, aligning with the need for written company approval per policy rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">Overpayment due to age misstatement arises from adjusting benefits to match the correct age. In such cases, the company must refund the difference to the policy owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="bff67a86-bdb2-4ccc-9c13-8e25d42f6ad3">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 addresses corrections due to misstated age leading to premium overpayment, requiring a refund without interest. Fact sentence 2 extends the same rule to cases where sex was misrepresented, maintaining consistent treatment across gender-related inaccuracies.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d3">When a misstatement of age causes overpayment of premiums, the insurer refunds the excess amount. This situation contrasts with cases where underpayment occurs, leading instead to a proportional reduction in the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">complementary outcome</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fdf3adf5-70d1-4255-9e26-5ab8405c27d1" target="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">subject to refund in case of overpayment due to age misstatement</data>
</edge>
<edge source="922a5db3-4b76-4fa9-b757-cd0dada418e4" target="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">can trigger</data>
</edge>
