<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">A reduction in the death benefit due to underpaid premiums from a misstated age depends directly on the originally specified death benefit outlined in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">An underpayment of premiums due to a misrepresented age triggers a reduction in the death benefit, highlighting the direct link between timely premium payments and benefit entitlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">A reduction in the death benefit due to underpaid premiums stemming from age misstatement only applies if the error falls within the two-year incontestability period, where claims against the policy remain viable.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement of age triggers a recalibration of financial obligations within the policy; since the total contract governs all such conditions, the adjustment mechanism described in fact_sentence_2 operates under the authority established in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f">
  <data key="d3">When a misstatement of age causes underpayment of premiums, the reduction in the death benefit reflects the contractual treatment of such claims as representational errors—not breaches of warranty—justifying corrective actions per the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">A misstatement of age, if discovered, triggers adjustments to the death benefit when premiums were underpaid; this process hinges on the original application being the authoritative source, per the rule stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="c39b37f1-33a3-4fd2-bedc-c257cc617eba">
  <data key="d3">When a misstatement of age leads to underpaid premiums, the death benefit is adjusted downward—a consequence that only takes effect after proper validation through official channels, including written authorization per company policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">When a misstatement causes underpayment of premiums, the death benefit is reduced per policy terms. This adjustment process depends on adherence to formal protocols, ensuring no unilateral changes by agents override established calculations.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforced by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">When a misstatement of age causes underpayment of premiums upon correction, the death benefit is adjusted downward per the terms established in fact_sentence_1, ensuring alignment with the actual coverage purchased at the true age.</data>
  <data key="d4">derives from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 indicates that if premiums were underpaid because of a false age statement, the death benefit decreases proportionally. Similarly, fact_sentence_1 shows that a misstated sex similarly reduces the benefit to match what was actually funded through premiums, illustrating parallel treatment of misstatements affecting benefit amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="00981cfe-a248-4489-99ff-6dff511e9bd7">
  <data key="d3">An underpayment of premiums due to age misstatement triggers a reduction in the death benefit. Conversely, if premiums were overpaid, the company returns the surplus to the policyholder without interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">complementary outcome</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3" target="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 discusses how correcting a misstated age affects the death benefit if premiums were underpaid. Fact sentence 2 extends this principle to misstatements of sex, showing identical consequences when premiums are underpaid due to inaccurate gender reporting.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8c142e8c-e515-4d37-b7c8-c91758c9ffa2" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is reduced when premium underpaid</data>
</edge>
