  <data key="d3">A reduction in the death benefit occurs only when a prior misstatement of sex causes underpayment of premiums, relying on the initial specification of the benefit amount set forth in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">A failure to pay correct premiums based on misrepresented sex directly impacts the death benefit, underscoring the necessity of accurate premium payments to preserve full coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">A reduction in the death benefit occurs only if a misstatement of sex causes underpayment of premiums, but this adjustment is permissible only during the incontestability period established by the company’s right to review policy validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">Provisions addressing misstatements of sex rely on the foundational understanding that the complete contract encompasses the policy, application, and amendments, ensuring consistent interpretation and enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82" target="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f">
  <data key="d3">A reduction in the death benefit due to a misstatement of sex implies that prior statements were treated as representations—not guarantees—and thus subject to corrective action based on factual accuracy, consistent with the representation clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">When a misstatement of sex leads to underpaid premiums, the death benefit is adjusted downward; this outcome hinges on the validity of the original application details, which governs whether such adjustments apply at all.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82" target="17a08a71-b8b3-4e8a-85f9-e97555d901c8">
  <data key="d3">When a misstatement of sex results in insufficient premium payment, the death benefit is reduced accordingly; however, this outcome relies on the availability of the written application to validate the error and support adjustments during claim evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">When a misstatement of sex causes underpaid premiums, the death benefit is adjusted downward—a process governed strictly by policy terms that cannot be overridden by agents, ensuring consistency and legal enforceability.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 describes the consequence of misstating sex leading to underpayment of premiums, requiring a reduction in the death benefit. This mirrors the mechanism described in fact sentence 1, showing that the same principle applies across different types of personal data misrepresentations.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">An underpayment of premiums due to a corrected misstatement of sex triggers a reduction in the death benefit, which was initially determined based on the original premium payment at the incorrect sex.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82" target="bff67a86-bdb2-4ccc-9c13-8e25d42f6ad3">
  <data key="d3">An underpayment of premiums due to a misstatement of sex necessitates a reduction in the death benefit. Conversely, if too much was paid, the surplus is refunded to the policyholder, ensuring fairness in contractual obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">complementary outcome</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a1e6299-7170-452e-85d0-d0ae6f09cb82" target="630ec11d-5e4f-49ab-9f66-2bd5a622d2c3">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 addresses the outcome of a misstated sex leading to underpaid premiums and a proportional reduction in the death benefit. This mirrors the mechanism described in fact sentence 1 regarding age misstatements, demonstrating consistency in policy enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
