<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">A policy being void ab initio due to invalid age eligibility means the death benefit provision in fact_sentence_1 cannot apply, regardless of its stated terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">A policy's validity hinges on the applicant being within the insurable age range; otherwise, it is void from the start, making any subsequent premium payments ineffective in establishing enforceable coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on eligibility</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">A policy declared void ab initio cannot be reinstated, rendering the reinstatement provision ineffective when the policy's validity is fundamentally compromised at inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents restoration</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">Being outside the insurable age range makes the policy void ab initio, meaning its invalidity exists from the start and cannot be cured by surviving the incontestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">preempts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">A policy declared void due to improper age qualification negates the binding nature of the agreement outlined in the initial clause, meaning even though the policy and application form part of the contract, they do not create enforceable obligations when eligibility criteria are violated.</data>
  <data key="d4">contractual limitation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="2ff2e286-b2f4-46d0-a585-be514606308f">
  <data key="d3">A policy is voided ab initio if the insured was outside the insurable age range at issue, implying that any prior statement claiming otherwise constitutes a material misrepresentation. Since such statements are treated as representations—not warranties—their falsity justifies termination of the contract retroactively.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="a0e459f4-ff70-494b-bb20-e24bfe587be4">
  <data key="d3">A policy being void ab initio due to out-of-range age means its legal foundation fails entirely. Since only information in the written application counts, any false age declaration made therein becomes decisive evidence undermining validity, making the initial fact relevant to enforcing the consequence.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">Being outside the insurable age range renders the policy void from the start, which underscores why no individual—such as an agent—can legally change or excuse this fundamental eligibility requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d">
  <data key="d3">When the insured is found ineligible due to age, the policy is declared void from the beginning, leading to the automatic refund of all premiums paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="02c92a77-4444-4482-b5ba-6fbe3753537c">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the policy becomes void ab initio if the insured is outside the insurable age range, consistent with chunk summary 1’s emphasis on policy nullification due to eligibility errors. This aligns directly with fact sentence 2 and its supporting context.</data>
  <data key="d4">identical to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="fa85ef78-daa9-404e-b6ed-fccb52560244">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that the policy becomes void from inception if the insured is outside the insurable age range, and fact_sentence_2 complements this by specifying that all premiums will be refunded upon such determination, ensuring financial restitution.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f" target="2940b504-0b37-4a43-8502-2feaeb5668ba">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 asserts the policy becomes void if the insured is outside the insurable age range, while fact_sentence_2 suggests the death benefit is merely reduced under the same circumstance. This implies a possible inconsistency in treatment depending on interpretation.</data>
  <data key="d4">contradicts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
