<edge source="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Failure to meet the insurable age requirement negates the basis for paying the death benefit, rendering the stated death benefit irrelevant due to policy nullification.</data>
  <data key="d4">invalidates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d" target="b6c70d4a-bb66-4ce6-8a7e-fcce14499c75">
  <data key="d3">If the insured is determined to be outside the insurable age range at issue, the policy cannot stand, so any prior premium payments made by the policy owner are automatically refunded, negating the need for continued payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes refund</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d" target="474ef3ff-fa30-4661-8d2d-93b34f04b312">
  <data key="d3">A failure to qualify within the insurable age range invalidates the policy, making it subject to cancellation and refund; this outcome relies on the contract being legally constituted per the initial clause specifying the policy’s scope.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d" target="9d18139a-0c83-4f90-b974-a4a7e8663000">
  <data key="d3">When an applicant falls outside the insurable age range, the policy’s invalidity necessitates a refund, consistent with the principle that no party may unilaterally change policy terms—even implicitly—to override eligibility requirements established by law or underwriting standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">triggers refund</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d" target="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to refund all premiums arises directly from the policy being voided ab initio when the insured does not meet the insurable age criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d" target="2940b504-0b37-4a43-8502-2feaeb5668ba">
  <data key="d3">When the insured is found outside the insurable age range at issue, the policy reduces the death benefit, aligning with the provision that all premiums are fully refunded under the same circumstance.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d" target="fa85ef78-daa9-404e-b6ed-fccb52560244">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that premiums are fully refunded if the insured is outside the insurable age range at issue, a condition reiterated and supported by chunk summary 2’s mention of policy voidance and refunds under similar circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">identical to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d" target="02c92a77-4444-4482-b5ba-6fbe3753537c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes a financial remedy (premium refund) when the insured is ineligible by age, while fact_sentence_2 adds that the policy is legally void from its start. Together, they form a complete picture: ineligibility triggers both cancellation and repayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
