<edge source="2940b504-0b37-4a43-8502-2feaeb5668ba" target="fa85ef78-daa9-404e-b6ed-fccb52560244">
  <data key="d3">When the insured is outside the insurable age range, the death benefit is reduced, and as a result, all paid premiums are fully refunded to maintain fairness in the contractual obligation.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2940b504-0b37-4a43-8502-2feaeb5668ba" target="02c92a77-4444-4482-b5ba-6fbe3753537c">
  <data key="d3">When the insured is outside the insurable age range, the death benefit is reduced, which triggers the policy's nullification from its beginning, rendering it void ab initio.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2940b504-0b37-4a43-8502-2feaeb5668ba" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">If the insured is outside the insurable age range, the death benefit is adjusted accordingly, but only within the framework defined by the policy terms, which govern all policyholder actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2940b504-0b37-4a43-8502-2feaeb5668ba" target="5182202e-021d-43a3-9210-05e10387d554">
  <data key="d3">If the insured is outside the insurable age range, the death benefit is reduced, which may reflect higher risk assessed during underwriting. This adjustment aligns with the basis of premium rates tied to underwriting class, where age-related risks influence pricing.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2940b504-0b37-4a43-8502-2feaeb5668ba" target="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a">
  <data key="d3">If the insured is outside the insurable age range at issue, the death benefit is adjusted downward. This adjustment reflects actuarial considerations used when setting initial premium rates based on current pricing standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">related to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2940b504-0b37-4a43-8502-2feaeb5668ba" target="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 reduces the death benefit when the insured is outside the insurable age range, whereas fact_sentence_1 renders the entire policy void ab initio under identical circumstances, suggesting conflicting legal outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">contradicts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2940b504-0b37-4a43-8502-2feaeb5668ba" target="61440afb-3a2c-404a-bde6-11a9b541d36d">
  <data key="d3">A finding that the insured is outside the insurable age range triggers both a reduction in the death benefit and a requirement to refund all premiums paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
