  <data key="d3">A full premium refund occurs when the insured is found outside the insurable age range, which also triggers a reduction in the death benefit to reflect altered risk assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa85ef78-daa9-404e-b6ed-fccb52560244" target="02c92a77-4444-4482-b5ba-6fbe3753537c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to refund all premiums arises directly from the policy’s cancellation when the insured is deemed ineligible due to age. This ensures equitable treatment upon voidance.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fa85ef78-daa9-404e-b6ed-fccb52560244" target="2b82244e-77bd-4daa-b86e-e3bfa2ef021f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that premiums are fully refunded when the insured is found ineligible due to age, which aligns with fact_sentence_1’s assertion that the policy is void ab initio, providing coherence on consequences of age-related ineligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
