  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="00adac65-2eb3-4c5b-aa93-0bc971b14432">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="50b223a6-fca5-4676-a70b-ee9317ae588d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="e928582c-ab01-43ec-b69b-6ca269fcc31a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="d50481f4-fd6e-4b61-9fcd-2f387102d5da">
  <data key="d3">Because the company does not verify assignment validity, it relies on the policyholder’s proper execution via formal written notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="4a4ca44e-1767-405f-8f6b-09fab8417798">
  <data key="d3">The lack of corporate validation responsibility follows directly from the requirement that assignments be communicated via written notice, implying oversight remains external to the insurer's duties.</data>
  <data key="d4">implies restriction</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="a8967232-8d5a-44c6-bf5d-6fefc30ab80d">
  <data key="d3">Even though the company records assignments to make them effective, it avoids assuming liability for their legal validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the company disclaims liability for whether an assignment is legally valid. Fact sentence 2 extends this by noting the company also avoids responsibility for whether the assignment is sufficient, implying incomplete or inadequate documentation may go unchecked.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that the company does not guarantee the legal validity of assignments. This sets a foundation for understanding potential risk, which is extended by fact sentence 2, clarifying that the company also avoids accountability for associated tax outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d3">If the company disclaims responsibility for assignment validity, it increases the likelihood that such assignments may improperly constrain policy rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">implies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="7b4a5d81-6d8d-43cc-94ef-d8cd7aa0e8a8">
  <data key="d3">If the company does not validate an assignment, it may render the assignment ineffective, thereby preventing the assignee from exercising associated policy rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d3">The assumption of no responsibility for assignment validity implies that third parties may face uncertainty about enforcement, but this risk is mitigated by the rule that assignees’ rights are subordinate to irrevocable beneficiaries unless overridden in writing.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">The absence of company liability for assignment validity reinforces the autonomy granted to the policy owner, ensuring that internal decisions about rights management are upheld despite external uncertainties.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">The company’s refusal to validate assignments implies that only legally sound assignments can limit the policy owner’s rights, reinforcing that such constraints are contingent on proper execution.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional restriction</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to assign the policy while the insured is alive is subject to the caveat that the company disclaims responsibility for the assignment’s validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d3">The statement about the company disclaiming responsibility for assignment validity sets context for understanding the limits of transferred rights, which aligns with the idea that only irrevocable beneficiary designations can restrict the policy owner’s authority.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's actions carry legal weight across all stakeholders, even though the insurer disclaims responsibility for validating those actions, particularly regarding assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa">
  <data key="d3">The lack of corporate responsibility for assignment validity implies that such actions may depend on external legal validation, which aligns with the principle that policyholder actions must conform to applicable law.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The lack of corporate validation on assignments means that any action by the policy owner related to assigning rights must still comply strictly with policy conditions to remain effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
