</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="d50481f4-fd6e-4b61-9fcd-2f387102d5da">
  <data key="d3">While the company accepts written notices for assignment, it explicitly avoids accountability for evaluating whether the assignment is sufficient or effective under its criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="4a4ca44e-1767-405f-8f6b-09fab8417798">
  <data key="d3">While the company accepts assignment notifications, it reserves the right to disregard concerns about their completeness or legal sufficiency.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 highlights the company’s refusal to ensure the adequacy of an assignment. Fact sentence 1 supports this by stating the company does not verify the legality of such assignments, reinforcing that neither formal nor substantive quality is guaranteed.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that the company does not guarantee the validity or completeness of an assignment. This sets up a broader disclaimer about responsibilities related to assignments, which extends logically to include tax-related liabilities covered in sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d3">If an assignment is insufficiently documented or handled improperly, it may reduce or restrict the policyholder’s ability to exercise certain rights under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="7b4a5d81-6d8d-43cc-94ef-d8cd7aa0e8a8">
  <data key="d3">The company's disclaimer about assignment sufficiency implies that improper assignments may limit policyholder rights, directly supporting why an assignment could prevent the exercise of certain benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">implies risk</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">The statement about the company disclaiming responsibility for assignments provides context on legal limits around transferability, but does not directly affect the assertion that the policy owner has unrestricted rights while the insured is alive.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that the insurer disclaims liability concerning assignment sufficiency, setting up a condition under which subsequent claims about assignment effectiveness may fail. Fact_sentence_2 builds on this by specifying that without written agreement from an irrevocable beneficiary, the assignee’s rights remain secondary.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">The statement about the company assuming no responsibility for assignment sufficiency sets up context for why assignments might create uncertainty. This justifies the conditionality in the second sentence—that rights are only restricted if an assignment explicitly imposes limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e">
  <data key="d3">The policy allows the owner to assign the policy during the insured’s life, though the insurer disclaims responsibility for whether such assignments meet requirements or expectations.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence notes the insurer does not guarantee the adequacy of assignments, which indirectly supports the second sentence by reinforcing that such actions may have legal limits. This contextualizes why the policy owner’s rights remain subject to external constraints like irrevocable designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual support</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s actions are legally binding on all stakeholders, emphasizing the importance of careful handling of assignments. However, since the company does not vouch for the sufficiency of such assignments, the enforceability depends entirely on compliance with procedural requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The company disclaiming responsibility for assignment sufficiency implies that such actions must still comply with policy terms, making them contingent upon established conditions set forth in the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
