</edge>
<edge source="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244" target="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb">
  <data key="d3">While fact sentence 2 highlights the lack of responsibility for tax consequences tied to assignments, it builds upon the broader disclaimer introduced in fact sentence 1 about assignment legitimacy, reinforcing the limited role of the insurer in such matters.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244" target="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991">
  <data key="d3">Sentence 2 highlights that the company disclaims accountability for tax effects arising from an assignment. Given that such tax issues may stem from improper or incomplete assignments, this follows naturally from the earlier statement about lack of oversight over assignment sufficiency.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d3">The statement about tax liability for assignments provides background on potential financial risks, which contextualizes why the rights of assignees are explicitly made subordinate to irrevocable beneficiaries—to protect beneficiary interests despite tax exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual link</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244" target="7b4a5d81-6d8d-43cc-94ef-d8cd7aa0e8a8">
  <data key="d3">Assignment carries tax risks, and such transactions may also result in limitations on exercising certain policy rights, linking tax consequence awareness to restricted entitlements.</data>
  <data key="d4">implies consequence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.78</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The statement about the company’s lack of responsibility for tax consequences of assignments provides context on risk allocation, which reinforces why the policy owner must act within defined boundaries outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17163d0c-a02b-429a-a6d1-2611afd7b663" target="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has no tax responsibility for</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0688b316-6955-4fb4-84db-d9f9544874b2" target="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is subject to company disclaimer of tax consequences</data>
</edge>
<edge source="98d152e4-dc40-46f8-bad8-934379d0a9c5" target="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">bears tax responsibility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="4160512d-2783-4f66-9cda-5d2e3f3c5461">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="6ee3c0c4-4a32-4a40-a0fa-b973497d0d87">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">organization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="fc97abf8-600c-4473-8b45-11ef67e77997">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="2652ed18-ec48-4699-bab3-6325b5ee33d8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="664f2b5d-e127-44a1-a0bb-3075d1755023">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="db66ac54-f533-4975-b447-1b23f6268287">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="6e2213c3-bbfd-4f85-ab5f-f672a0934593">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="d36d8b94-62c3-4dd4-90f1-e64914c4988b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="3af9e94f-154b-421d-b794-16843890a9f6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="144bb75c-cd22-4578-a7f8-4388268597b6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="b33d85a9-aa6a-4fad-8f8a-bc219e1c524d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="d50481f4-fd6e-4b61-9fcd-2f387102d5da">
  <data key="d3">An irrevocable beneficiary maintains priority over an assignee, so any assignment only takes effect if the beneficiary agrees in writing.</data>
  <data key="d4">modified by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="4a4ca44e-1767-405f-8f6b-09fab8417798">
  <data key="d3">Even when rights are assigned, they cannot take priority over irrevocable beneficiaries without explicit written consent, preserving the beneficiary’s superior standing.</data>
  <data key="d4">superseded by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="a8967232-8d5a-44c6-bf5d-6fefc30ab80d">
  <data key="d3">Even though assignments become effective only after proper notice, they cannot elevate the assignee above an irrevocable beneficiary without explicit agreement, ensuring beneficiary rights maintain precedence over transferred interests.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb">
  <data key="d3">Assignees' rights are legally secondary to irrevocable beneficiaries, ensuring that even if an assignment is made, its effectiveness depends on explicit written agreement from the beneficiary—a safeguard consistent with the insurer's disclaimers around assignment validation.</data>
  <data key="d4">implies limitation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 defines the limitation of assigned rights when an irrevocable beneficiary exists, reinforcing why the company might avoid assuming responsibility for assignments—because they could conflict with superior beneficiary claims. Fact_sentence_1 supports this by stating the company won’t vouch for assignment adequacy, aligning with the risk of invalidity highlighted in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244">
  <data key="d3">The subordination of assignee rights ensures that even if an assignment occurs, it does not affect the priority of irrevocable beneficiaries, making the lack of company responsibility for tax outcomes less impactful since beneficiary claims remain protected.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d3">The existence of irrevocable beneficiaries limits the power of an assignee, so any assignment cannot override these protected rights. Thus, an assignment may only affect rights that remain available after honoring beneficiary claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="7b4a5d81-6d8d-43cc-94ef-d8cd7aa0e8a8">
  <data key="d3">The existence of an irrevocable beneficiary limits the power of an assignee, ensuring that assigned rights cannot override beneficiary claims. As a result, an assignment may prevent the holder from exercising certain rights under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">The priority of irrevocable beneficiaries over assignees ensures that even if rights are transferred via assignment, those transfers do not supersede existing beneficiary designations. This supports the notion that the policy owner’s authority remains intact unless explicitly constrained by formal assignment terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e">
  <data key="d3">Assigning the policy while the insured is alive is permitted but subject to the condition that the assignee’s rights remain secondary to those of any irrevocable beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the policy owner to change the beneficiary is limited by the existence of irrevocable beneficiaries, whose rights take precedence over any assignees. This ensures that changes cannot undermine established beneficiary claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d3">Assignee rights are limited by irrevocable beneficiaries, who have priority over them. This limitation explains why the policy owner’s powers may still be constrained even after assignment.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The priority of irrevocable beneficiaries over assignees depends on adherence to policy terms, which govern what actions the Policy Owner may take regarding assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2652ed18-ec48-4699-bab3-6325b5ee33d8" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinate to</data>
</edge>
<edge source="664f2b5d-e127-44a1-a0bb-3075d1755023" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">superior to</data>
</edge>
<edge source="144bb75c-cd22-4578-a7f8-4388268597b6" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has priority over</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b33d85a9-aa6a-4fad-8f8a-bc219e1c524d" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has priority over assignee</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="1acda6ee-ee70-4345-883f-aa16b36d787f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="1bb5c857-44bc-41ed-a7aa-2c53429b3623">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">organization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="ce742fc3-fbcc-4e62-88f0-30d0a680385d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="ddb13c77-a11d-4407-ae4b-502f8d403e0b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="06b918c0-cfb0-4969-81c2-2cbbada7b0e4">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="d474313b-17a1-4e8c-ab93-53aa4a403de5">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="c18f7764-b71a-4f4e-b6da-84eac93150c8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="b0f2a290-64bc-4d8d-ba44-2c139e7ba8fb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="09595f20-d28f-440f-bb5c-42da847db701">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="f24c4525-5803-4bc8-bb94-b40b5fac12b7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="65ae23f0-581d-4542-9f4b-b20d3037e43f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="d50481f4-fd6e-4b61-9fcd-2f387102d5da">
  <data key="d3">Limitations on policy rights arise when the ownership is formally transferred via assignment, requiring prior written notification.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="4a4ca44e-1767-405f-8f6b-09fab8417798">
  <data key="d3">Limitations on exercising policy rights arise when the policy owner assigns those rights via written notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="a8967232-8d5a-44c6-bf5d-6fefc30ab80d">
  <data key="d3">Because assignments take effect only after written notice is processed, any limitation on policy rights arises directly from the official recording of such notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb">
  <data key="d3">Assignments limiting policy rights underscore why the company avoids assuming liability—they may lead to unintended consequences on entitlements.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991">
  <data key="d3">Insufficient assignments, as acknowledged by the company's lack of responsibility, directly contribute to limiting the scope of rights available to the policyholder.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d3">Because an assignment can restrict certain rights, its effectiveness depends on whether it conflicts with pre-existing superior rights held by irrevocable beneficiaries, making such assignments subordinate in priority.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="7b4a5d81-6d8d-43cc-94ef-d8cd7aa0e8a8">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that an assignment can reduce the scope of exercisable rights. Fact sentence 2 extends this by stating that such an assignment might completely prevent the exercise of those rights, reinforcing the idea of restricted control.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">Assignment can impose limits on specific policy rights, but the policy owner generally maintains full control over those rights unless an assignment specifically restricts them.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">Assignment of rights may constrain what the policy owner can do, but the policy owner generally maintains full control over contractual rights as long as the insured is alive and no explicit restrictions exist.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d3">Assignments can curtail specific rights under the policy, but such limitations are subordinate to pre-existing restrictions like irrevocable beneficiary designations, which directly constrain the policy owner’s authority.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e">
  <data key="d3">Assigning the policy limits certain rights, such as control over benefits or changes to beneficiary designations, which only becomes relevant when the policy owner exercises the right to assign it during the insured’s life.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa">
  <data key="d3">The ability of an assignment to restrict policy rights is constrained by overarching legal requirements governing the policy owner’s actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="04c48339-a09a-4dea-809f-8cf26cbb5dd7">
  <data key="d3">Assignment can restrict how some policy rights are exercised, yet the policy owner still maintains the ability to obtain policy information while the insured is alive, regardless of such restrictions.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the Policy Owner to exercise rights may be restricted due to assignments, but such actions remain governed by the overall terms of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to assign rights limits what the Policy Owner can do, but any such action remains legally binding on all involved parties, reinforcing the finality of the Owner’s decisions despite constraints.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">An assignment restricts certain policyholder rights, potentially affecting renewal or premium payments, which could contribute to a lapse. When the policy lapses, coverage ceases entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1acda6ee-ee70-4345-883f-aa16b36d787f" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has limited right due to</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1bb5c857-44bc-41ed-a7aa-2c53429b3623" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">may enforce limitation on rights due to</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ce742fc3-fbcc-4e62-88f0-30d0a680385d" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has restricted authority due to</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ddb13c77-a11d-4407-ae4b-502f8d403e0b" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">limits rights related to</data>
