  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="96a6cbe9-9a45-4132-962d-631747dbc815">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="d50481f4-fd6e-4b61-9fcd-2f387102d5da">
  <data key="d3">The existence of unrestrictive rights for the policy owner implies that assignments are required to impose any constraints, which aligns with the need for formal notification.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="4a4ca44e-1767-405f-8f6b-09fab8417798">
  <data key="d3">Unless restricted by an assignment, the policy owner maintains full freedom to exercise contractual rights, even after formally assigning some interests via written notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">unrestricted</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="a8967232-8d5a-44c6-bf5d-6fefc30ab80d">
  <data key="d3">Unrestricted rights of the policy owner may become restricted only after an assignment has been properly recorded and takes effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy owner’s rights are only restricted by formal assignments, the company’s disclaimer about assignment validity ensures that unverified assignments cannot unjustly curtail those rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">validity dependent</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991">
  <data key="d3">The assertion that the policy owner’s rights are otherwise unrestricted depends on the existence of binding assignments. Since the company avoids accountability for assignment validity, it reinforces that only formally documented assignments can curtail those rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d3">Unrestricted policy owner rights under normal conditions imply that limitations arise solely through documented assignments, which themselves are subject to higher claims from irrevocable beneficiaries, thus maintaining hierarchical control.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d3">Unless constrained by an assignment, the policy owner has complete freedom to exercise contractual rights, even though assignments themselves have the power to curtail such freedoms.</data>
  <data key="d4">exempted by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="7b4a5d81-6d8d-43cc-94ef-d8cd7aa0e8a8">
  <data key="d3">Unless constrained by an assignment, the policy owner holds unimpeded access to contractual rights, ensuring that any limitation on rights arises only from formal assignment actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on the policy owner’s rights arises only through formal assignment, implying that without such an action, the broad powers described earlier remain fully intact.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that assignments limit the Policy Owner’s rights, emphasizing formal transfer conditions. Fact sentence 2 adds another constraint—irrevocable beneficiary designations—that similarly limits those same rights independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s ability to assign the policy creates a scenario where their contractual rights become subject to limitations, consistent with the clause that such rights are only unrestricted if not restricted by an assignment.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s unrestricted contractual rights include the authority to modify beneficiary designations during the insured’s life, consistent with standard policy provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s unrestricted contractual rights allow them to select optional benefit options while the insured is alive, assuming no assignments restrict those powers.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="04c48339-a09a-4dea-809f-8cf26cbb5dd7">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner has broad rights unless restricted by an assignment, enabling them to request policy information while the insured is alive.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner holds unfettered contractual rights unless constrained by an assignment, enabling them to take actions that legally bind all parties with interests in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner has broad rights unless constrained by an assignment, but those rights must still conform to the overall terms of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner has broad rights unless restricted by assignment, but those rights are still governed by applicable laws, ensuring legal accountability regardless of internal policy provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner holds broad, unrestricted rights unless otherwise limited by assignment, enabling them to request changes such as modifying the payment mode, contingent on insurer approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner's unrestricted rights allow them to maintain coverage through the grace period by fulfilling premium obligations without interference from assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner holds broad rights subject only to assignments, ensuring flexibility in exercising contractually granted powers. This autonomy complements the operational allowance of a 31-day grace period for premiums, enabling timely fulfillment without immediate loss of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b40f4e7-fba0-420e-95e2-8fbbfec12678" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has unrestrictable contractual rights</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b66799c9-da2f-4d96-b20c-29fd3576b2bd" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">can restrict policy owner's rights</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="5d4acb5e-1692-4286-8714-0321e7be17b6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="65ec4ae7-41a0-428c-b238-a428ebe3a8a3">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">organization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="81ea956a-4b92-4b7c-a355-ebdd803dfcae">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="35f20f7d-9615-40e1-ae20-cca7068c338d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="6cb667f0-7c11-4743-932b-ca65af69e844">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="ad51b43d-ecf8-4ce4-85ef-9334bd8ebb4e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="a2795565-2226-47c7-a98a-33fc7565e395">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="1f91e324-46e9-43d1-8e0a-6e72c12c5bb6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="3f2ee3a6-be9c-4b11-a94f-ca12186cc43b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="54a0a936-4496-4391-8606-0f542dd2eb43">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="a4cb5456-6f03-4d95-a476-25f4b40407d4">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="d50481f4-fd6e-4b61-9fcd-2f387102d5da">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to assign the policy is conditional upon compliance with restrictions tied to irrevocable beneficiaries, which limit unilateral actions like assignment.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="4a4ca44e-1767-405f-8f6b-09fab8417798">
  <data key="d3">While the policy owner has general freedom to act, any attempt to assign rights is constrained by prior irrevocable beneficiary arrangements, making the assignment process subject to those limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits assignment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="a8967232-8d5a-44c6-bf5d-6fefc30ab80d">
  <data key="d3">Even though the policy owner has broad rights, any assignment only becomes binding once formally recorded by the company, ensuring procedural validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb">
  <data key="d3">The assertion that the policy owner has unrestricted rights unless constrained by an irrevocable beneficiary explains why such designations matter—and underscores why the company would avoid assuming liability for assignments made without proper regard to these constraints.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence establishes that the policy owner has broad rights unless overridden by an irrevocable beneficiary, which explains why the company disclaims responsibility for assignments—they cannot enforce or validate such transfers beyond existing beneficiary terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits by designation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority remains unfettered only until an irrevocable beneficiary is designated, at which point it becomes subject to limitations that affect both the owner and any assignee.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d3">While the policy owner generally holds unrestricted rights, any limitation on those rights—including via assignment—is subject to overriding provisions such as irrevocable beneficiary designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="7b4a5d81-6d8d-43cc-94ef-d8cd7aa0e8a8">
  <data key="d3">While the policy owner generally has unrestricted rights, any assignment could further limit those rights beyond what is already constrained by irrevocable beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">modified by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">An irrevocable beneficiary designation restricts the policy owner’s otherwise unlimited rights under the contract when the insured is still living.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 identifies irrevocable beneficiary designations as a barrier to unimpeded exercise of contractual rights. Fact sentence 1 complements this by noting that assignments also impose such barriers, reinforcing the idea that multiple factors may restrict ownership authority.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s ability to change the beneficiary is contingent upon whether any irrevocable beneficiary designations exist, which restrict ownership rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s unrestricted ability to exercise contractual rights enables them to assign the policy while the insured is alive, assuming no conflicting irrevocable beneficiary constraints.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="04c48339-a09a-4dea-809f-8cf26cbb5dd7">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s ability to obtain policy information while the insured is alive stems directly from their unencumbered contractual rights, which remain intact unless overridden by an irrevocable beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s unrestricted contractual rights allow them to select optional benefit options while the insured is alive, ensuring flexibility in managing the policy under normal conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner holds unfettered rights under the contract unless constrained by an irrevocable beneficiary, enabling them to take actions that legally bind all involved parties.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s ability to act on contractual rights is constrained only by specific provisions like irrevocable beneficiary designations, but those same actions remain bound by overarching legal standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s ability to act freely is conditional upon any constraints imposed by the policy, such as irrevocable beneficiary designations. These conditions are embedded within the overarching terms governing all owner actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="1a6344cf-ea03-47a1-be12-6fbc60df405e">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence establishes that the policy owner has full rights except where overridden by an irrevocable beneficiary. This contextualizes why the second sentence—which specifies no dividends are paid—is consistent with the policy’s nonparticipating nature.</data>
  <data key="d4">consistent with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner has broad rights unless constrained by an irrevocable beneficiary, but those rights cease once the policy lapses, terminating coverage entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="81ea956a-4b92-4b7c-a355-ebdd803dfcae" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has potential limitations on contractual rights when</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6cb667f0-7c11-4743-932b-ca65af69e844" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">can restrict policy owner's rights via irrevocable designation</data>
</edge>
