  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="1425e68f-075c-492a-abee-93d33f1c7a64">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="b3230bcf-9bef-49f8-9105-da091270fdf7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="52c318f1-3df6-4758-89c5-df95d7e5ba78">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="9a3aa6b8-7b59-4c50-b5db-acf7ba310854">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="639b1602-412f-4fd2-b259-a2bb84262b10">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d3">The priority of irrevocable beneficiaries restricts the policy owner’s unilateral power to alter beneficiary designations, ensuring that assignment rights remain secondary.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change the beneficiary reflects the policy owner’s overarching control over the policy during the insured’s lifetime, as explicitly stated in the prior clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">implied by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change the beneficiary reflects the underlying principle that the Policy Owner holds unencumbered rights over the policy, subject only to formal limitations like assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">is example of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d3">If there are no irrevocable beneficiary designations, the policy owner has the unrestricted authority to modify the beneficiary while the insured is alive.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e">
  <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary allows the Policy Owner to update who inherits benefits, while assigning the policy transfers ownership rights, potentially affecting future claims and control. Both reflect ongoing authority retained by the owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="04c48339-a09a-4dea-809f-8cf26cbb5dd7">
  <data key="d3">Changing the beneficiary is one aspect of ownership control, and requesting policy information supports informed decision-making about such changes. Both reflect ongoing administrative privileges retained by the Policy Owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s ability to change the beneficiary is limited by legal requirements, ensuring compliance with governing statutes.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s authority to change the beneficiary is limited by the overall conditions outlined in the policy agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the Policy Owner to change the beneficiary relies on their authority being legally recognized and enforced against all relevant parties, ensuring the action takes effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fd398927-f523-4607-9687-3caed7de1129" target="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has right to change</data>
</edge>
