  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="82a24c37-35b6-478c-b222-1e443a0d3fd6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="d50481f4-fd6e-4b61-9fcd-2f387102d5da">
  <data key="d3">While the policy allows assignment upon meeting formal requirements like written notice, it explicitly restricts this action to periods when the insured is still living.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="4a4ca44e-1767-405f-8f6b-09fab8417798">
  <data key="d3">While the Insured is living, the Policy Owner has the right to assign policy rights, subject to providing proper written notice to the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="a8967232-8d5a-44c6-bf5d-6fefc30ab80d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written notice ensures that any assignment made by the policy owner while the insured is living is formally recognized and recorded by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb">
  <data key="d3">Although the policy allows assignment by the owner during the insured’s life, such actions are not guaranteed to be legally recognized by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991">
  <data key="d3">While the policy permits assignment by the owner while the insured is alive, the company explicitly avoids assuming liability regarding the validity or sufficiency of those assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d3">The rule that assignees’ rights are subordinate to irrevocable beneficiaries applies specifically when the policy owner exercises the right to assign the policy during the insured’s life.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s authority to assign the policy while the insured is alive enables actions that subsequently constrain specific policy rights, creating a direct causal link from ownership action to limitation.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="7b4a5d81-6d8d-43cc-94ef-d8cd7aa0e8a8">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the policy owner to assign the policy while the insured is alive directly enables the scenario described in fact_sentence_1, where such actions may restrict specific policy rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">The ability to assign the policy stems directly from the policy owner’s comprehensive rights during the insured’s lifetime, which include control over contractual terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">Assigning the policy imposes constraints on the Policy Owner’s rights, directly linking it to the conditional limitation mentioned in the prior statement about assignments restricting ownership rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d3">The power to assign the policy while the insured is living depends on the policy owner having unencumbered contractual rights, which holds true unless overridden by an irrevocable beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944">
  <data key="d3">Assigning the policy involves transferring ownership rights, whereas changing the beneficiary alters payout instructions. Though different in function, both are exercises of ownership power granted to the Policy Owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the Policy Owner to assign the policy creates legal obligations that extend to all parties with an interest, ensuring consistency across stakeholders when such assignments occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the Policy Owner to assign the policy is limited by the governing terms of the contract, ensuring compliance with established conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e" target="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s ability to assign the policy is limited by legal frameworks that govern such transactions, ensuring compliance with statutory rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="17bf8ba2-b58f-4bc7-bbb5-fe12cf54a00c" target="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">living status condition</data>
</edge>
