  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a" target="02c92a77-4444-4482-b5ba-6fbe3753537c">
  <data key="d3">The policy owner’s right to elect optional benefits requires that the policy remain valid; however, if the insured was ineligible due to age, the policy is void ab initio, nullifying such rights retroactively.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">The ability to elect optional benefit forms depends on the policy owner already holding comprehensive rights over the policy during the insured’s lifetime.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">The ability to elect optional benefit forms implies that the Policy Owner holds active control over certain policy features, consistent with having unconstrained rights under the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d3">The option to elect beneficial features during the insured’s life depends on the policy owner retaining full control over contractually permitted actions, which holds true only when not constrained by an irrevocable beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a" target="04c48339-a09a-4dea-809f-8cf26cbb5dd7">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s ability to choose optional benefits does not depend on or influence their right to obtain policy information. Both are separate administrative rights available under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s ability to select optional benefits during the insured’s life creates actionable decisions that legally affect all stakeholders involved in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner has the option to select additional benefits while the insured is alive, but any action they take must comply with the established policy provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a" target="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s ability to choose optional benefits is constrained by legal requirements, ensuring that any election remains lawful and enforceable under jurisdictional rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a" target="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 grants the Policy Owner discretion over optional benefits, which includes modifying financial arrangements like premium payments. Therefore, changing the payment mode is a specific instance of exercising such discretionary powers.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
