</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="d50481f4-fd6e-4b61-9fcd-2f387102d5da">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written notice ensures that any action taken by the Policy Owner, such as assignment, is formally recognized and enforceable against third parties.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="4a4ca44e-1767-405f-8f6b-09fab8417798">
  <data key="d3">Because actions by the Policy Owner are binding on all interested parties, assignments made through proper notice carry legal weight throughout the policy ecosystem.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="a8967232-8d5a-44c6-bf5d-6fefc30ab80d">
  <data key="d3">Since actions by the Policy Owner are binding on all parties, it follows that such actions—including assigning rights—are only enforceable after proper documentation (written notice) has been received and recorded by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb">
  <data key="d3">Despite the company’s refusal to assume responsibility for assignment validity, its enforcement of the policy owner’s actions ensures consistency in binding obligations among interested parties.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991">
  <data key="d3">Because the company does not assume responsibility for assignment sufficiency, the binding nature of the policy owner’s actions means that any deficiencies may go uncorrected unless proactively managed by the owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d3">Because the Policy Owner's actions are binding on everyone with an interest, assigning rights—even if it limits future exercises—is effective and recognized across all stakeholder relationships.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="7b4a5d81-6d8d-43cc-94ef-d8cd7aa0e8a8">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s actions are universally binding, ensuring that even when assignments limit some rights, those constraints cannot override official decisions made by the owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">binds</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy owner holds exclusive rights while the insured is alive, their decisions carry legal weight and apply to all stakeholders involved.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">Because the Policy Owner’s actions are binding on all interested parties, their ability to act freely—unrestricted except by assignments—is essential to enforce such obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d3">Because the Policy Owner’s actions are binding on all interested parties, their ability to act freely—unrestricted by any beneficiary designation—is essential to ensuring enforceability.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944">
  <data key="d3">The binding nature of the Policy Owner’s actions ensures that changes to the beneficiary, when executed, are formally acknowledged and upheld throughout the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e">
  <data key="d3">Because any action by the Policy Owner binds all interested parties, the assignment of the policy becomes enforceable against them, reinforcing the authority granted under the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a">
  <data key="d3">Any decision made by the Policy Owner regarding optional benefits becomes enforceable across all parties with an interest in the policy, ensuring consistency and finality.</data>
  <data key="d4">binds</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="04c48339-a09a-4dea-809f-8cf26cbb5dd7">
  <data key="d3">Binding actions by the Policy Owner rely on having accurate knowledge of the policy terms, which requires prior access to policy information.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner's actions have legal effect on all stakeholders but only within the boundaries defined by the Policy itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner's actions have binding effect on all stakeholders, but only within the bounds defined by applicable laws.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner holds authoritative decision-making power, which includes fulfilling financial obligations like paying premiums on time. This ensures compliance with payment terms outlined in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner holds authoritative control over key policy changes, including adjusting the payment mode, which requires formal approval from the insurer. This action reflects the scope of powers granted under the ownership role.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="fc861170-d441-42f0-9df2-68e6af8ebe13">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner's authority ensures that proper premium payments, such as those made to an authorized agent with receipt confirmation, are recognized and upheld across all interests tied to the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner's ability to act decisively ensures that decisions regarding continuation during the grace period are enforceable across all stakeholders, maintaining the policy's active state when intended.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner's obligation to manage premium payments binds all stakeholders, ensuring timely payment prevents lapses during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s control over premium payments determines whether an unpaid premium triggers a deduction from the death benefit during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner has authority over key policy decisions, such as premium payments. Failure to maintain payment obligations causes the policy to lapse, resulting in termination of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0b6bbeae-92bc-4003-8112-892efe65360b" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is subject to</data>
</edge>
