<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="d50481f4-fd6e-4b61-9fcd-2f387102d5da">
  <data key="d3">Legal compliance applies to all actions taken by the policy owner, including the act of assigning the policy via written notice.</data>
  <data key="d4">governed by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="4a4ca44e-1767-405f-8f6b-09fab8417798">
  <data key="d3">Any assignment of policy rights by the Policy Owner is legally constrained and must adhere to relevant statutes and regulations, even after proper notification.</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="a8967232-8d5a-44c6-bf5d-6fefc30ab80d">
  <data key="d3">Policyowner actions, like assigning rights, must comply with applicable law, ensuring procedures such as timely notice submission remain legally enforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">conforms to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb">
  <data key="d3">Since policyowner actions—including assignments—are bound by applicable law, the absence of company oversight over assignment validity underscores the importance of legal compliance in executing such changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d3">Legal compliance limits the scope of what an assignment can enforce regarding policy rights exercised by the owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">bound by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">Legal regulations limit how the Policy Owner may exercise their rights under the policy, ensuring compliance even when they have unilateral control.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">Even though the Policy Owner holds unrestrictive rights under the contract, such powers remain subordinate to overarching legal requirements that apply universally.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d3">Even though the Policy Owner has broad rights unless otherwise restricted, such powers are ultimately subordinate to applicable legal frameworks governing their conduct.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="23213712-f92d-4cba-b4d4-2b1015682944">
  <data key="d3">Any action by the Policy Owner to change the beneficiary must adhere to applicable laws, reinforcing legal accountability.</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="311330de-41eb-43d2-9f52-1faca7a7786e">
  <data key="d3">Any assignment of the policy by the Policy Owner must comply with applicable laws, which define the scope and validity of such actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a">
  <data key="d3">Any decision made by the Policy Owner to select optional benefits must comply with applicable laws, which govern the legitimacy and implementation of those choices.</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="04c48339-a09a-4dea-809f-8cf26cbb5dd7">
  <data key="d3">Any request for policy information by the Policy Owner must adhere to relevant laws governing contractual and privacy obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">While the Policy Owner’s actions are legally binding, they remain constrained by compliance with relevant legislation.</data>
  <data key="d4">bound by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes that the Policy Owner’s actions must comply with external laws, which sets a foundational constraint. Fact sentence 2 adds that those same actions must also conform to internal policy provisions, reinforcing compliance within the contract itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s authority to modify the payment mode is constrained by applicable law, ensuring such changes comply with legal standards before requiring company approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="fc861170-d441-42f0-9df2-68e6af8ebe13">
  <data key="d3">The obligation under applicable law governs how the policy owner conducts transactions, such as paying premiums. This includes ensuring payments are made to authorized agents who provide receipts, aligning with legal compliance standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the Policy Owner’s actions follow applicable law ensures compliance with financial obligations like timely premium payments. Failure to meet such obligations during the grace period triggers automatic policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">The Policy Owner’s ability to maintain coverage depends on complying with laws governing premium payments and policy management. Failure to act legally may result in lapse and subsequent termination of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">The first statement sets the legal boundary for the Policy Owner’s authority, while the second ensures that any such boundaries enforced via law preserve the integrity of the remainder of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the Policy Owner act within the bounds of applicable law supports the principle that only legally permissible provisions remain effective, aligning with the idea that invalid clauses don’t undermine the rest of the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="66d34f7f-f03b-44b9-ae46-16416415bc2a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 highlights that Policy Owner actions are governed by law, reinforcing the necessity of proper procedures. This supports fact_sentence_2’s assertion that only written agreements can waive policy terms, ensuring legal enforceability and consistency.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that policy actions comply with law (fact_sentence_1) supports the necessity of formal authorization for waivers (fact_sentence_2), reinforcing legal validity and preventing unauthorized changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa" target="59ec3491-57bb-4404-9c45-157c0e769471">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that Policy Owner actions comply with law complements the rule that non-enforcement does not waive rights, ensuring consistent adherence to legal and contractual standards over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
