  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="2940b504-0b37-4a43-8502-2feaeb5668ba">
  <data key="d3">Policy owners' ability to influence benefits, such as triggering changes via action, is limited by pre-defined rules—including age-based reductions in death benefits when applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="02c92a77-4444-4482-b5ba-6fbe3753537c">
  <data key="d3">Policy owner actions are constrained by the policy’s rules, including provisions like automatic voidance when the insured is outside the insurable age range at issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="d50481f4-fd6e-4b61-9fcd-2f387102d5da">
  <data key="d3">Any assignment attempt by the Policy Owner must adhere to the policy’s conditions, ensuring it does not conflict with established contractual obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="4a4ca44e-1767-405f-8f6b-09fab8417798">
  <data key="d3">Any assignment of rights must adhere to the policy’s requirements, particularly the need for written notice acceptable to the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="a8967232-8d5a-44c6-bf5d-6fefc30ab80d">
  <data key="d3">Policy owners must follow formal procedures like submitting written notices to make assignments legally effective, reinforcing adherence to established policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="68b1219a-81cc-436d-b9fa-18329365fedb">
  <data key="d3">Policy owners' ability to act freely is limited by contract terms, so even though they may attempt assignments, those efforts won't be recognized unless compliant with established provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="6e440086-23d0-4b7f-adcc-b2cb7b037991">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy owner’s actions are governed by the policy terms, any attempt at assignment must meet formal standards—even if the company does not verify its sufficiency.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="a72ae00e-3120-4673-b199-3e97fab66244">
  <data key="d3">Policy owners' actions are constrained by contractual obligations, ensuring compliance with rules such as those governing assignments, where the company explicitly disclaims tax-related liabilities.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="b42dc01b-3bad-4d3c-991a-41d5cb2909a4">
  <data key="d3">Policy terms restrict the Policy Owner's authority, ensuring that assignment rights remain subordinate to irrevocable beneficiaries when applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d3">Policy terms constrain what the Policy Owner can do, including limiting rights when assignments have been made.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces limitation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="7b4a5d81-6d8d-43cc-94ef-d8cd7aa0e8a8">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the Policy Owner follow policy terms explains why assignments can limit exercised rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">The limitations imposed by the policy’s terms govern the scope of actions available to the policy owner, even though they retain significant control over the policy during the insured’s life.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">Policy terms govern all actions taken by the Policy Owner, even though such actions are otherwise unrestricted except by assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
