</edge>
<edge source="675e6ad8-541e-4de3-8117-4f94ae24cfec" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy is nonparticipating, the owner has no right to shares of surplus, reinforcing that their authority is constrained by predefined policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="675e6ad8-541e-4de3-8117-4f94ae24cfec" target="222e3616-509e-41e7-8e0a-8df9ddd50f95">
  <data key="d3">The statement that the policy shall not share in any surplus clarifies and reinforces the meaning of the policy being nonparticipating, providing semantic confirmation.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="675e6ad8-541e-4de3-8117-4f94ae24cfec" target="497f8eb6-dc59-49fd-b3a0-653bed16b13b">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the policy does not share in company surplus, which is further clarified by fact sentence 2 stating it also does not share in company earnings—a broader category that includes surplus.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="675e6ad8-541e-4de3-8117-4f94ae24cfec" target="1368ebec-9201-44b1-a9ef-90b544575402">
  <data key="d3">The policy's nonparticipation means it cannot share in company surplus, directly leading to the conclusion that no dividends are payable to the policyholder at present.</data>
  <data key="d4">implies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="675e6ad8-541e-4de3-8117-4f94ae24cfec" target="1a6344cf-ea03-47a1-be12-6fbc60df405e">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s exclusion from participating in the insurer’s surplus ensures that no future dividends will be issued to the policyholder, making dividend payments impossible under this arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="675e6ad8-541e-4de3-8117-4f94ae24cfec" target="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a">
  <data key="d3">The nonparticipation clause means the policy won’t benefit from company surpluses, so premiums are fixed based strictly on original pricing models established at issue.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="970f4326-8ece-4e0a-89b6-8d624807c044" target="675e6ad8-541e-4de3-8117-4f94ae24cfec">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">retains surplus without sharing</data>
</edge>
