<edge source="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a" target="2940b504-0b37-4a43-8502-2feaeb5668ba">
  <data key="d3">Premium rates are set according to the insurer’s pricing standards at the time of issue, which include factors like age eligibility thresholds that determine whether a death benefit reduction applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">Policy Owner actions are limited by contractual rules, one of which is the static determination of premium rates at issue, ensuring consistency in payment expectations.</data>
  <data key="d4">informed by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a" target="222e3616-509e-41e7-8e0a-8df9ddd50f95">
  <data key="d3">The fact that premium rates rely on the company’s pricing standards at issue supports the classification of the policy as nonparticipating, as such policies typically lack dynamic rate changes tied to profitability.</data>
  <data key="d4">implied by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a" target="675e6ad8-541e-4de3-8117-4f94ae24cfec">
  <data key="d3">Since premiums are priced according to the company’s standards at issue, they reflect static financial expectations without accounting for future surplus sharing, consistent with the policy’s nonparticipating nature.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a" target="497f8eb6-dc59-49fd-b3a0-653bed16b13b">
  <data key="d3">Since premiums are priced according to the company’s initial standards, the lack of access to company earnings ensures that such pricing remains static and independent of potential profitability.</data>
  <data key="d4">justified by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a" target="5182202e-021d-43a3-9210-05e10387d554">
  <data key="d3">The company’s general pricing standards at issue encompass specific criteria like underwriting class, making fact_sentence_2 a higher-level explanation that includes the detail in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">subsumes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a" target="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d">
  <data key="d3">The fixed premium amount, determined by the insurer’s pricing standards at issue, dictates the specific due date and requirement for advance payment outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a" target="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s premium rates are fixed at issue according to the insurer’s pricing criteria, providing a stable foundation. The policy owner can request changes to the payment schedule, such as switching from annual to monthly installments, contingent upon company approval.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">The base premium rate is set at issuance according to company standards, influencing the amount owed during the grace period. If the insured dies during this period, the outstanding premium is subtracted from the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">The premium rate established at issuance determines the required payment amount. Failure to meet this obligation by the end of the grace period triggers automatic policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s premium rate is fixed at issuance according to the insurer’s standards, and failure to meet payments within the grace period causes the policy to lapse, resulting in termination of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6e84578-ba84-4f16-9c37-421217df726a" target="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">pays premium based on company pricing</data>
</edge>
