<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payments ensure ongoing policy effectiveness, enabling the policy owner to retain full rights during the insured’s lifetime, subject to compliance with terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">Timely premium payment is a responsibility of the Policy Owner, whose actions bind all interested parties, ensuring continuity of coverage through proper execution of duties.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">Since the Policy Owner’s actions are bound by policy terms, paying premiums in advance aligns with those obligations and reflects compliance with contractual requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="5182202e-021d-43a3-9210-05e10387d554">
  <data key="d3">Payment in advance ensures continuous coverage, contingent upon paying the correct amount determined by the underwriting class.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a">
  <data key="d3">Advance payment requirements depend on the originally set premium rates, ensuring timely payments align with the actuarially calculated cost at policy inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the timing for premium payments, requiring them to be made by the due date specified in the policy. This condition necessitates that payments be sent to the designated administrative office, as stated in fact_sentence_2, ensuring proper processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417">
  <data key="d3">The rule requiring premiums to be paid in advance sets the baseline for payment obligations. The ability to change the payment mode provides administrative flexibility under company approval, building upon the existing framework without altering its core requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="fc861170-d441-42f0-9df2-68e6af8ebe13">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the deadline for premium payment, which triggers the requirement in fact_sentence_2 that payments be delivered through proper channels to receive formal acknowledgment.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid by the due date, the policy enters a grace period where it continues to remain in effect, ensuring uninterrupted coverage temporarily.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for premiums to be paid in advance sets the baseline deadline, upon which the subsequent 31-day grace period operates as a leniency window for timely payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">If premiums are not paid in advance by the due date, the policy may lapse, resulting in the termination of coverage as stated in the second fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium by its due date triggers the start of the grace period, but if payment still does not occur within that time, the policy automatically lapses effective from the original due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid in advance sets the condition under which an unpaid premium may exist during the grace period, directly influencing how the death benefit is calculated if the insured passes away within that window.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Requiring premiums to be paid in advance establishes a clear deadline, making the 31-day grace period necessary to accommodate potential delays without immediate loss of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
