<edge source="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change the payment mode depends on the Policy Owner having active rights under the policy, which they retain so long as the insured is alive.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change the payment mode reflects a specific instance of the policy owner’s overarching contractual rights, which remain intact unless constrained by an assignment.</data>
  <data key="d4">subsumed by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417" target="f16e49b5-127a-4da9-9b3d-98d87f3e061a">
  <data key="d3">Changing the payment mode is a concrete example of how the Policy Owner exercises control over optional benefits, demonstrating operational flexibility within the framework of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417" target="04c48339-a09a-4dea-809f-8cf26cbb5dd7">
  <data key="d3">Changing the payment mode relies on prior awareness of policy conditions, making access to policy information essential when initiating such changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">The right to modify the payment mode depends on the Policy Owner having binding authority over the policy, ensuring that any such change legally affects all stakeholders involved.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417" target="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa">
  <data key="d3">Any modification of the payment mode by the Policy Owner must align with applicable law, reinforcing legal oversight over ownership decisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">bound by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">Any change in payment mode by the Policy Owner must conform to the policy’s conditions, reinforcing that such actions are bound by contractual limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">conforms to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417" target="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a">
  <data key="d3">While the policy owner has authority to propose modifications to the payment mode, any such change operates within the framework established by the original premium rates set at issue under the company’s pricing standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417" target="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d">
  <data key="d3">Changing the payment mode requires prior approval from the insurer and operates within the established system where premiums must be paid in advance, ensuring compliance remains central even when modes are adjusted.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinated to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417" target="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9">
  <data key="d3">Changing the payment mode requires company approval, ensuring that any modification aligns with official procedures. This process indirectly supports proper submission by directing the insured to follow designated channels like sending payments to the Administrative Office.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">Changing the payment mode affects when premiums are due, potentially influencing whether they are paid on time. Failure to pay by the end of the grace period leads directly to policy lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
