  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The obligation to pay premiums at the designated office stems from the overarching rule that all Policy Owner actions must follow the policy’s stipulations.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9" target="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the required destination—the Company’s Administrative Office—for premium payments. This delivery point only becomes relevant once the payment deadline from fact_sentence_1 has been established, making it dependent on timely action.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9" target="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417">
  <data key="d3">Payments must be delivered to the Company’s Administrative Office, reinforcing compliance with formal processes required when altering payment arrangements such as switching payment modes.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">Payment of premiums at the designated office ensures eligibility for the grace period, enabling continuous policy coverage despite late payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay premiums at the company’s administrative office sets up the logistical context for when such payments may be made during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums at the designated office before the grace period ends triggers automatic policy lapse effective from the original due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9" target="fc861170-d441-42f0-9df2-68e6af8ebe13">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 identifies the primary location for premium payments—the company’s administrative office—while fact sentence 2 expands on acceptable alternatives by specifying that payments may also be made through an authorized agent, provided an official receipt is issued.</data>
  <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid at the Company’s Administrative Office sets the condition under which unpaid amounts may later affect benefits. This procedural detail enables the enforcement mechanism described in the next sentence regarding deductions from the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">Paying premiums at the designated office maintains active coverage by preventing the policy from lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
