  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="2f19bf8a-0b54-4cac-89e9-c4df0ee344ff">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="775ca55f-580f-4b78-8f96-9fb875dfd32a">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period allows the policyholder time to meet financial obligations, preserving the continuity of benefits and supporting the uninterrupted exercise of policyowner rights under normal circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period reflects a defined term within the policy that constrains the Policy Owner’s ability to delay premium payments without consequence, aligning with overarching contractual limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">subordinates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="5182202e-021d-43a3-9210-05e10387d554">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that a 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payments without immediate lapse. This temporal buffer could affect whether the higher premiums tied to certain underwriting classes (as noted in fact_sentence_1) are paid on time.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period provides a buffer beyond the initial due date established in the prior statement, enabling delayed but acceptable payment under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period allows flexibility in meeting the obligation specified in fact_sentence_1 to pay premiums at the designated office.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="fc861170-d441-42f0-9df2-68e6af8ebe13">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period accommodates delayed premiums, contingent on eventual payment through an authorized agent who provides an official receipt upon receipt.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows time for late premium payment without immediate loss of coverage. During this interval, the policy continues to remain in effect despite overdue premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payment without immediate policy lapse, enabling the application of deductions from the death benefit if the insured passes away before paying.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed payment without immediate consequences, but failure to use it leads to policy termination on the original due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional consequence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period allows delayed premium payment without immediate loss of coverage, preventing premature lapse. If the premium isn’t paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses, resulting in termination of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapsing</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 expands upon fact_sentence_1 by specifying that the 31-day grace period applies repeatedly—not just once but for each premium payment after the first—adding temporal scope to the original statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="e9992b58-f0cb-4309-aa8b-99ccf5ca595c">
  <data key="d3">The grace period enables continuation of coverage after missed premiums, potentially avoiding lapses that would trigger the resumption of suicide exclusions upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="a68f05ee-b6c2-4a27-be1f-bfafeddf4b0c">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period enables continuation of coverage despite late premiums, potentially leading to reinstatement, which triggers a new two-year contestability period. Thus, timely payment via the grace period directly influences whether the later contestability clause becomes active.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period prevents immediate lapse, thereby maintaining coverage eligibility; if premiums aren't paid within it, the policy lapses, triggering exclusion from liability per fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period maintains coverage temporarily, but since the policy lacks automatic renewal, any unpaid premium beyond the term leads to termination regardless of grace period use.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="be5d9596-fd48-4642-93c3-1033cc1a3da6">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period maintains active coverage beyond missed payments, preserving the policyholder’s ability to meet requirements necessary for later conversion to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables conversion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period helps maintain policy validity, which may preserve eligibility for later conversion to permanent insurance without evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables conversion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="0c4d1411-9c02-4d7d-ae5c-767cd2ba2497">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period ensures ongoing coverage, enabling the policyholder to maintain eligibility for conversion before lapsing. Without timely premium payment, the policy could lapse, potentially disqualifying the holder from converting under the required timeline.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="6b3c39b6-2af6-4210-bf69-47e128370b19">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period described in fact_sentence_1 is a concrete manifestation of the broader requirement stated in fact_sentence_2 that premiums adhere to the product’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="cf26351d-1aa6-446d-8320-a1b56d723009">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period supports ongoing policy validity, enabling the insured to maintain eligibility for conversion up until the maximum conversion age. Without timely premium payments, the policy could lapse, potentially disqualifying the insured from conversion even if within the age limit.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e" target="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period for premiums depends on the legal framework established by New York law, which governs the enforceability and application of such contractual terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f0d8814-21c2-4d57-b8b3-b6c55ba0b7ba" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has grace period for premium payment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="decf0255-6a63-42b7-9650-e9471d37a529" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">offers grace period for premium payment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79f961cb-4451-449a-981b-d21879a1a352" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06120641-4bd4-49c3-9773-4ca7d590f643" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has grace period of days</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2f19bf8a-0b54-4cac-89e9-c4df0ee344ff" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">subject to grace period for premium payment</data>
</edge>
