</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">The rule governing deductions from the death benefit during the grace period assumes prior ownership rights held by the policy owner, who controls the policy until the insured’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">The rule about deducting unpaid premiums from the death benefit depends on the Policy Owner having the authority to manage timely payments, making their actions decisive.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">Unpaid premiums during the grace period affect the death benefit, reflecting how the Policy Owner’s failure to act timely may impact payout outcomes under established policy rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="5182202e-021d-43a3-9210-05e10387d554">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies during the grace period, the outstanding premium—determined by the underwriting class—is subtracted from the death benefit, showing how prior risk classification impacts financial outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">determines</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a">
  <data key="d3">An unpaid premium due during the grace period reduces the death benefit if the insured passes away. This obligation stems from the original premium rate established at policy inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">derives from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, the deduction of the unpaid premium from the death benefit implies that timely payment was expected per the initial obligation stated in the prior sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies within the grace period, the outstanding premium—previously required by law to be paid at the administrative office—is subtracted from the death benefit, showing direct impact based on prior payment obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="fc861170-d441-42f0-9df2-68e6af8ebe13">
  <data key="d3">The deduction of unpaid premiums from the death benefit upon death during the grace period underscores the importance of fulfilling payment requirements via authorized agents, as specified in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d3">The deduction of unpaid premiums from the death benefit only applies when the insured dies within the 31-day grace period established by the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, it implies the policy was still in effect at the time, confirming its status as active despite overdue premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, the unpaid premium reduces the death benefit. This outcome depends on whether the policy remains active beyond the due date, which hinges on timely payment—the absence of such payment leads directly to lapse under fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, the unpaid premium is subtracted from the death benefit before payout. This situation arises just prior to potential policy lapse, which ultimately terminates coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, the death benefit remains payable less unpaid premiums, but once the policy has officially lapsed beyond the grace period, no benefits are available unless reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, the unpaid premium is subtracted from the death benefit, but only if the policy has not yet lapsed. This condition depends on the policy still being technically active until the end of the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, unpaid premiums reduce the death benefit, but only if the policy hasn't already lapsed due to non-payment beyond the grace period's end.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, unpaid premiums reduce the death benefit; however, if the policy was instead allowed to lapse, it could potentially be reinstated within five years, restoring benefits before death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">The first statement outlines consequences of dying during the grace period, while the second describes requirements to revive a policy after it has lapsed due to missed payments. Both pertain to financial obligations tied to delayed premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, the death benefit may be reduced by unpaid premiums. This outcome avoids the need for reinstatement since coverage ends upon death. However, had the policy lapsed instead, reinstatement would require a written request, highlighting a procedural pathway distinct from death-related payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, unpaid premiums reduce the death benefit; however, if the policy is later reinstated, those same overdue premiums—including interest—are required to be paid before benefits are released.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies during the grace period, the policy cannot be reinstated because it terminates at death; thus, the rule about reinstatement having retroactive effect becomes irrelevant in such cases.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
