<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium after the grace period ends triggers policy lapse, reinforcing the need for the Policy Owner to act decisively to uphold obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapsing due to missed premium payment reflects a legally mandated consequence tied to the Policy Owner’s duty to act according to governing laws, particularly regarding payment timelines.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">When a premium isn't paid by the due date—even during the grace period—the policy lapses, demonstrating one instance where the Policy Owner’s failure to comply with financial obligations violates the broader principle that all actions must adhere to policy rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">example of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="5182202e-021d-43a3-9210-05e10387d554">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the premium—determined by the underwriting class—within the grace period triggers policy lapse, making the initial classification relevant to enforcement conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapses if the premium remains unpaid after the grace period ends. This outcome depends directly on the originally specified premium rate set at issue.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d">
  <data key="d3">The policy's lapse occurring at the due date depends entirely on whether the premium was paid prior to the expiration of the 31-day grace period, making timely payment essential to maintain coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="daede05c-af65-4efd-8af7-defc13a4b417">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapses if a premium isn't paid during the grace period, regardless of prior arrangements like changed payment modes. This outcome limits the impact of adjusting payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9">
  <data key="d3">The risk of policy lapse arises specifically when premiums are not delivered to the administrative office prior to the expiration of the 31-day grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="fc861170-d441-42f0-9df2-68e6af8ebe13">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make a premium payment prior to the expiration of the 31-day grace period causes the policy to lapse, rendering earlier compliance with payment procedures ineffective once the deadline passes.</data>
  <data key="d4">preceded by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay during the 31-day grace period triggers automatic policy lapse effective from the original premium due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period causes the policy to lapse retroactively, implying it was only temporarily protected under the grace period provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">retroactive effect</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium by the end of the grace period causes the policy to lapse, resulting in the cessation of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium by the end of the grace period causes the policy to lapse as of the original due date. Consequently, if death occurs after the due date but within the grace period, the unpaid amount still affects the payout, linking back to fact_sentence_1’s condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">precondition for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Without the 31-day grace period, the policy would lapse immediately upon missed payments, highlighting the importance of timely premium submission to avoid termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that failing to pay a premium by the end of the grace period causes the policy to lapse on the original due date. Fact_sentence_2 repeats this exact statement, reinforcing the rule without contradiction.</data>
  <data key="d4">identical to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium within the grace period results in policy lapse, which directly causes coverage to terminate. This creates a clear cause-and-effect link between financial default and loss of protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes termination</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">The lapse caused by missing a premium payment necessitates submission of evidence of insurability to revive the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium during the grace period triggers policy lapse, thereby nullifying benefit entitlements unless the policy is later reinstated according to specified terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">The lapse caused by failing to pay a premium during the grace period creates a condition that allows future reinstatement within five years, making the timing of renewal dependent on post-lapse actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium leads to policy lapse, but reinstatement allows coverage to resume as if uninterrupted, restoring continuous protection despite prior lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">The lapse caused by failing to pay a premium within the grace period creates the need for a formal reinstatement process, requiring a written request to restore coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium within the grace period leads to policy lapse, requiring future reinstatement with added interest on overdue amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="a68f05ee-b6c2-4a27-be1f-bfafeddf4b0c">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay a premium leads to policy lapse, creating the condition necessary for reinstatement, which triggers a new contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="e9992b58-f0cb-4309-aa8b-99ccf5ca595c">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse, potentially necessitating reinstatement, at which point the suicide exclusion reactivates.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums within the grace period causes the policy to lapse, which triggers the insurer’s exemption from liability for claims occurring during that inactive period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse, and since the policy does not automatically renew, coverage ends permanently unless conversion or reinstatement occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="be5d9596-fd48-4642-93c3-1033cc1a3da6">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse, which would prevent eligibility for conversion into a permanent policy. Thus, maintaining current status via timely payment enables access to future conversion options.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums within the grace period causes the policy to lapse, yet the policyholder may still convert to permanent insurance afterward without proving insurability, offering a recovery option after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">recoverable after lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="0c4d1411-9c02-4d7d-ae5c-767cd2ba2497">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse, which could terminate the opportunity to convert unless done prior to lapse. Thus, maintaining active status via timely payment preserves access to conversion options.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="cf26351d-1aa6-446d-8320-a1b56d723009">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums leads to policy lapse, which could disqualify the insured from later converting the policy under terms that include age-based limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="6b3c39b6-2af6-4210-bf69-47e128370b19">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay premiums as required by the product's terms leads to policy lapse after the grace period ends, making timely payment contingent on those terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07" target="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for timely premium payment and potential policy lapse is subject to interpretation and enforcement under New York state law, which governs the contract's terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d1c59673-740e-49bf-bcc7-a365c6143495" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">may lose coverage if policy lapses</data>
</edge>
