<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="771de587-5b8c-4772-ae4a-1e306c16617f">
  <data key="d3">If coverage terminates due to a lapse, any prior assignment limiting rights becomes irrelevant because the policy no longer exists. Lapse supersedes earlier contractual arrangements like assignments.</data>
  <data key="d4">supersedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="c973474c-d230-409f-ad33-e1a682af9558">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, it ceases to provide coverage, even though the policy owner had previously held full rights during the insured's lifetime.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="74da563a-668e-4838-9c04-3edc34513cfb">
  <data key="d3">When the policy lapses, coverage ends, thereby nullifying any remaining contractual rights the policy owner might have had under the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">terminates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="48170372-67f9-431b-afea-2352f772cc6e">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to missed premium payments, coverage ceases. This outcome stems from the Policy Owner’s responsibility to uphold financial commitments, making their actions decisive.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="d01b45ac-0eb6-487a-be72-95174a8cf9aa">
  <data key="d3">Termination of coverage through lapse arises from unmet obligations, such as failure to pay premiums, which fall under the Policy Owner’s responsibilities and are constrained by applicable law.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="988c3be0-9555-43fe-a0e7-92bfd1b7079e">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, it signifies that the Policy Owner failed to meet financial obligations outlined in the policy terms, thereby forfeiting active coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="be7f41e9-f83b-4532-b16a-6d60d99dd86a">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to missed premium payments, coverage ceases, which reflects the consequence of failing to uphold obligations tied to the originally established premium rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="e92e0ea5-c65d-41a2-8ffb-fb2ed9910e6d">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage occurs only after the policy has lapsed, which typically happens due to failure to pay premiums in advance, as required by the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="d935b2c7-ac58-442f-bdca-43a72846d5c9">
  <data key="d3">Failure to make payments leads to policy lapse, which means the obligation to pay premiums becomes irrelevant once coverage has terminated.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by payment failure</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="fc861170-d441-42f0-9df2-68e6af8ebe13">
  <data key="d3">Termination of coverage due to lapse implies that prior premium payments were not made on time, possibly failing to meet the requirement of paying to an authorized agent.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d3">Policy lapse leads to termination of coverage, which happens only if the premium remains unpaid beyond the 31-day grace period. Therefore, the existence of the grace period serves as a buffer against early lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by grace period</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">Policy lapse leads directly to termination of coverage. This outcome follows from failure to pay premiums within the 31-day grace period allowed after the due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">When coverage terminates due to lapse, it occurs because a premium was not paid within the allowed grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">When the policy lapses, coverage ceases entirely. This outcome typically follows failure to pay premiums within the 31-day grace period, potentially resulting in a claimant receiving reduced benefits if death occurred during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that policy lapse ends coverage, which is further clarified by fact_sentence_2 identifying nonpayment as the cause of such lapse, reinforcing the conditionality of coverage continuation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, coverage ceases entirely, making it impossible to receive benefits unless the policy is successfully reinstated according to specified terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that coverage ends upon policy lapse, which is triggered by unpaid premiums after the grace period—as detailed in fact_sentence_2. This creates a clear cause-and-effect link where late payments result in loss of protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses, coverage ends, but it can be restored within five years through reinstatement, preserving the original terms subject to requirements like proof of insurability and repayment of missed premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage upon policy lapse sets up the need for reinstatement, which requires a written request as specified in fact_sentence_2. This creates a procedural pathway to restore benefits after termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, coverage terminates, but it may be restored only if evidence of insurability is provided and approved.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">When coverage terminates upon policy lapse, reinstatement remains possible only if overdue premiums—including interest—are paid, linking the end of coverage to future recovery requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">When coverage terminates due to policy lapse, it creates the condition under which reinstatement becomes possible, restoring benefits retroactively.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="a68f05ee-b6c2-4a27-be1f-bfafeddf4b0c">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage upon policy lapse sets the condition for initiating a new two-year contestability period after reinstatement, ensuring renewed underwriting scrutiny applies from the reinstatement date.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d3">When the policy lapses, coverage ends, making it impossible for the insurer to honor claims filed during that time. This justifies why the company explicitly disclaims liability for events occurring during the lapse period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="e9992b58-f0cb-4309-aa8b-99ccf5ca595c">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, coverage ceases entirely. Upon reinstatement, however, the suicide exclusion resumes, reflecting renewed risk assessment despite prior coverage history.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage at lapse, as stated in fact_sentence_1, directly supports the understanding that the policy cannot continue past its term without action, reinforcing why automatic renewal is absent per fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="be5d9596-fd48-4642-93c3-1033cc1a3da6">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of converting the policy prevents its lapse, thereby maintaining coverage beyond the point where it would otherwise terminate under normal circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="6b3c39b6-2af6-4210-bf69-47e128370b19">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage due to policy lapse depends on failure to meet premium payment obligations, which are defined by the product’s terms as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="0c4d1411-9c02-4d7d-ae5c-767cd2ba2497">
  <data key="d3">Conversion eligibility hinges on acting before the policy lapses, so the requirement to act during the conversion period is directly tied to preserving current coverage status.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, coverage ceases, but the individual may still convert it into a permanent policy without proving insurability, preserving access to future benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage upon policy lapse depends on procedural and temporal rules, which are interpreted and enforced according to New York state law as specified in the governing clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad" target="cf26351d-1aa6-446d-8320-a1b56d723009">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to unpaid premiums, the insured loses the opportunity to convert to permanent insurance regardless of age. Therefore, maintaining active coverage through timely premium payments is essential to qualify for conversion under the age restriction.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c1d83546-a1c4-4419-96c3-38873d551189" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">terminates coverage</data>
</edge>
