<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is not paid by the grace period's end, the policy lapses, leading directly to the termination of insurance coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses, resulting in termination of coverage and exclusion from receiving benefits unless reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium by its due date results in policy lapse, but reinstatement remains possible within five years if action is taken promptly.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes reinstatement window</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is not paid by the due date, the policy lapses, creating the need for reinstatement. To initiate reinstatement, a written request must be submitted, making it a necessary procedural follow-up to the lapse event.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes reinstatement request</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses. To restore coverage, the insurer requires proof of insurability as part of the reinstatement process.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes reinstatement requirement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium within the grace period results in policy lapse, but reinstatement allows coverage to resume retroactively as if uninterrupted.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes reversal</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is not paid within the grace period, the policy lapses, triggering the need for reinstatement. To reinstate the policy, the insurer requires full payment of overdue premiums along with interest, ensuring financial recovery for the delay.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes reinstatement conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="b32da2b1-a458-4c5b-bb4d-0cd663f0dd82">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is not paid by the due date, the policy lapses, potentially leading to reinstatement efforts that could restart the incontestability clock.</data>
  <data key="d4">leads to reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">If a premium is not paid during the grace period, the policy lapses, meaning it is no longer active. As such, the death benefit becomes unavailable unless the policy is reinstated under specific conditions outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">If a premium isn't paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses, meaning it's no longer active. As a result, the insurer cannot pay the death benefit upon the insured’s death because the policy was inactive when death occurred.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">When a premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses, potentially leading to an adjustment of the death benefit if the insured passes away later. Unpaid premiums reduce the payout available to beneficiaries at time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">The failure to pay a premium leads to policy lapse, removing active coverage. This outcome affects whether death benefit payments occur at all, but does not alter the standard method of disbursement if the insured dies while covered.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">If a premium is not paid by the end of the grace period, the policy lapses, meaning it ceases to provide coverage. This affects whether a death benefit can be claimed, but does not alter the requirement that proof of death must still be submitted to trigger payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 reiterates the precise consequence outlined in fact_sentence_1—that non-payment during the grace period leads to immediate lapse upon the due date—confirming consistency across both chunks.</data>
  <data key="d4">identical to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay within the grace period leads to immediate lapse, nullifying the protection previously maintained under the grace period provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that failing to pay a premium during the grace period leads to policy lapse, thereby causing coverage to terminate, as stated in fact_sentence_1. Thus, the second fact provides the mechanism behind the first.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay a premium by the end of the grace period causes the policy to lapse, nullifying future benefits—including those payable upon death—even if the insured died earlier during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
