<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage occurs because the policy has already lapsed due to nonpayment of the premium beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment, coverage ends, resulting in no benefit payments being made—except under specific reinstatement conditions outlined later.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment, coverage ends, creating the need for reinstatement through formal steps like submitting a written request.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment, it becomes inactive, necessitating reinstatement through specific steps including providing evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment, it triggers termination of coverage, but this lapse opens a window during which reinstatement remains possible if action is taken promptly.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="b32da2b1-a458-4c5b-bb4d-0cd663f0dd82">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment, it creates the scenario requiring reinstatement, which subsequently triggers the reset of the incontestability provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment, it triggers the need for reinstatement, which includes fulfilling financial obligations such as paying overdue premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">leads to reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment, it triggers termination of coverage. However, if reinstated within the allowed timeframe, coverage resumes retroactively as if never interrupted.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="17de4c88-376a-4e6b-b992-7f89cc84bb9a">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment, it creates the scenario where reinstatement becomes possible. Upon reinstatement, certain provisions—like the Suicide Exclusion—are reset, beginning again from the new effective date.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment, it ceases coverage, meaning any claim based on death would only be honored if the policy was reinstated before death. This makes the lapsed state a key factor affecting eligibility for the death benefit under policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to nonpayment, it ceases to provide coverage, meaning that any subsequent death of the insured would fall outside the scope of active protection, thereby preventing the payout described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to nonpayment, coverage ends, meaning the death benefit would not be payable upon the insured's death. Therefore, maintaining active status through timely payments ensures eligibility for the full face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to nonpayment, the resulting termination of coverage triggers the rule that unpaid premiums are deducted from the death benefit upon claim settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to nonpayment, coverage ceases, meaning any subsequent death would require reinstatement to qualify for benefits. Therefore, proving death becomes necessary only if the policy was active at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to nonpayment, coverage ends, meaning that no death benefit can be claimed even if the insured passes away later. Therefore, the prompt processing of benefits described in sentence 2 assumes the policy remains active.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">The termination of coverage due to nonpayment prevents the activation of post-death benefits, including interest accrual on the death benefit. Therefore, ensuring ongoing coverage through timely premium payments is necessary for such provisions to apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">When coverage terminates due to policy lapse from nonpayment, it confirms the consequence described in the first statement—that the policy ceases to remain effective after missed payments beyond the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">Policy lapse resulting from nonpayment ends coverage, though prior to that point, the policy remains effective during the grace period, maintaining its validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that coverage ends upon lapse due to nonpayment, which supports fact_sentence_1’s general statement that coverage terminates at lapse, providing contextual grounding for the trigger event.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">When the policy lapses due to nonpayment, coverage ends permanently unless reinstated. However, if death occurs during the grace period prior to lapse, the death benefit remains payable after deducting any unpaid premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Policy lapse results from failure to pay within the grace period, meaning the 31-day grace period serves as the final opportunity to maintain coverage before termination occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">The second statement affirms that coverage ends when the policy lapses due to nonpayment, reinforcing the definition provided in the first statement regarding the consequences of missed premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy loses coverage, but its reinstatement restores active status, allowing benefits to resume provided terms like proof of insurability and overdue payments are satisfied.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">A policy’s termination through lapse invalidates any future claim for the death benefit, rendering the previously specified amount unpayable under the policy's terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">A policy lapse terminates coverage, meaning any provision regarding corrected benefits—for example, those triggered by misstated sex—is rendered inapplicable post-lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Coverage termination occurs only if the premium is not paid within the 31-day grace period, which underscores the importance of timely payment to maintain continuous coverage under the policy’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="d822587b-a5be-4232-b595-d6f428b09987">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the $420 annual premium results in the policy lapsing, thereby nullifying ongoing protection despite prior commitment.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="3af0e3a5-6ae4-44d2-9986-8f2a02aac638">
  <data key="d3">If the policy lapses due to nonpayment, no benefit will be paid—even though Taylor Ellis is listed as the beneficiary—meaning the designation becomes irrelevant once coverage ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e">
  <data key="d3">The validity of Taylor Ellis being the beneficiary hinges on the policy staying in force; once coverage terminates via lapse, even though she was originally designated, she cannot claim benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6" target="6c0901ed-f52a-4ce9-9d52-9547016ca265">
  <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 outlines conditions for early termination via lapse, it depends on the existence of a defined coverage window such as the one described in fact_sentence_1 to determine when the policy could expire prematurely.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
