<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">The inability to receive benefits upon policy lapse stems directly from the condition that non-payment of a premium beyond the grace period leads to lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The absence of benefit payments upon lapse is a direct result of coverage termination caused by failure to pay premiums during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">The inability to receive benefits upon policy lapse is overridden if the policy is reinstated within five years, making reinstatement a prerequisite for future claim eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">The inability to receive benefits from a lapsed policy hinges on the possibility of reinstatement, which begins with a written request. Without this step, the exception clause in fact_sentence_1 cannot apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">The inability to receive benefits upon lapse depends on meeting reinstatement criteria, one of which is paying overdue premiums with interest. This creates a conditional pathway back to claim eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">The inability to receive benefits from a lapsed policy hinges on reinstatement eligibility, which depends on submitting acceptable evidence of insurability. Without such documentation, the policy remains inactive and no benefits are triggered.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to non-payment, no benefits are payable unless it's reinstated. Upon successful reinstatement, the policy’s coverage is treated as if it never ceased, allowing future benefits to become available again.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional restores</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="17de4c88-376a-4e6b-b992-7f89cc84bb9a">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy cannot pay benefits unless reinstated, and once reinstated, the suicide exclusion begins again from that new effective date.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="b32da2b1-a458-4c5b-bb4d-0cd663f0dd82">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to non-payment, benefits are generally denied unless reinstated. Upon reinstatement, the incontestability period begins again, ensuring renewed protection against future contestation by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">reinstatement leads to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy cannot pay benefits unless reinstated, illustrating how the death benefit's availability depends on adherence to policy terms like reinstatement requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">The absence of benefits upon policy lapse contrasts with the availability of death benefits when the policy remains active at time of death. This highlights the importance of maintaining active status for claim eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">If a policy lapses due to non-payment beyond the grace period, no benefits—including the full face amount—are payable unless reinstated. This underscores that the death benefit specified in fact_sentence_2 only applies when the policy remains in force.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions on payability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy cannot trigger benefits unless reinstated, which creates a conditionality separate from death claims. Proof of death remains required regardless of whether the policy was previously lapsed.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">When a policy lapses due to non-payment beyond the grace period, no benefits are payable unless reinstated. However, if the policy remains active at the time of death, unpaid premiums are deducted from the death benefit before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional exclusion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">The inability to pay benefits on a lapsed policy (sentence 1) sets up a condition where even if a death occurs after lapse, no proceeds are issued—rendering the concept of deducting indebtedness irrelevant in such cases. This highlights that debt deductions apply only when the policy remains active at death.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">The inability to pay benefits after a policy lapse (sentence 1) contrasts with the prompt payment process once a valid claim is submitted (sentence 2). Sentence 1 sets a restriction based on policy status, while sentence 2 applies only when the policy is still effective.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy cannot provide benefits unless reinstated, which depends on timely action after the grace period ends—a condition directly tied to whether premiums were paid on time.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy cannot pay benefits unless reinstated, making it essential that the grace period (which keeps the policy alive) is utilized to avoid termination and preserve payout eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">The inability to collect benefits after a lapse depends on whether the policy has been formally reinstated, which hinges on timely action post-lapse, consistent with the termination clause tied to premium delinquency.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy generally denies benefits, but if death occurs during the grace period, the insurer still pays the adjusted death benefit after deducting unpaid premiums, preserving limited payout eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Without the grace period, policies would lapse immediately upon missed payments, making reinstatement necessary to restore benefit eligibility—a process explicitly governed by terms outlined in the second summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 reinforces the consequence of lapse described in fact_sentence_1 by specifying that benefits are voided post-lapse unless reinstated, emphasizing the operational outcome of the defined condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">Without the reinstatement provision detailed in fact_sentence_1, the exception allowing benefits post-lapse in fact_sentence_2 would have no operational basis, making it ineffective.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy prevents payment of the death benefit even if one was originally specified, meaning the declared amount is unenforceable until reinstatement occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy cannot pay benefits unless reinstated, which means even if age was correctly stated later, failure to reinstate prevents access to adjusted death benefits from prior misstatements.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">Even if the death benefit is adjusted due to a misstated sex, it cannot be claimed after a lapse unless the policy is properly reinstated within the allowed timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Without the 31-day grace period, policies would immediately lapse upon non-payment, making the reinstatement clause irrelevant since there would be no opportunity to restore coverage before benefits become unpayable.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="d822587b-a5be-4232-b595-d6f428b09987">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the $420 annual premium results in policy lapse, nullifying benefit eligibility unless reinstated—making timely payment critical to preserving the protection outlined in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="3af0e3a5-6ae4-44d2-9986-8f2a02aac638">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s effectiveness in paying benefits to Taylor Ellis depends on avoiding lapse, making the beneficiary status contingent on adherence to renewal requirements outlined in the reinstatement clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390" target="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e">
  <data key="d3">A lapse voids benefit eligibility regardless of beneficiary designation, so even though Taylor Ellis is listed, she cannot collect if the policy fails due to non-payment after the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
