  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a written request for reinstatement is a prerequisite that enables the policyholder to take advantage of the five-year reinstatement window after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">A written request for reinstatement must be submitted before any further requirements, such as providing evidence of insurability, can proceed.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">A written request for reinstatement is necessary to trigger the process that restores the policy's validity. Without such a request, reinstatement cannot occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">A written request for reinstatement is required before any financial obligations can be addressed. Without initiating the request, the subsequent requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest cannot proceed.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="b32da2b1-a458-4c5b-bb4d-0cd663f0dd82">
  <data key="d3">A written request for reinstatement initiates the process that leads to the policy being revived, thereby triggering the start of a new incontestability period effective from the reinstatement date.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="17de4c88-376a-4e6b-b992-7f89cc84bb9a">
  <data key="d3">A written request for reinstatement initiates the process that triggers the reset of the Suicide Exclusion provision, ensuring it begins afresh from the reinstatement date.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">A written request for reinstatement is required to revive a lapsed policy, ensuring it remains eligible for benefits like the death benefit under applicable terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="7b26fed4-7c69-4d32-aa07-45ab4d3be614">
  <data key="d3">After submitting a written request for reinstatement, the insurance company may require additional documentation if deemed necessary based on its assessment of the case.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional requirement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">A written request for reinstatement is necessary only after a policy has lapsed due to nonpayment, making it dependent on the prior occurrence described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">A written request for reinstatement is necessary when a policy lapses due to unpaid premiums beyond the grace period, highlighting the importance of timely payment during the grace period to maintain validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy depends on first having a lapse, which occurs when coverage terminates due to unpaid premiums—a condition described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional reversal</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy involves a written request and proof of insurability. If the insured died before reinstatement but during the grace period, the claim proceeds are adjusted downward by unpaid premiums rather than requiring reinstatement altogether.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Requiring a written reinstatement request applies specifically after the grace period expires, meaning it depends on the prior definition of the grace period’s duration and consequences.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement procedures depend on prior lapse occurrence, making fact_sentence_2 contingent upon the conditions defined in fact_sentence_1 regarding policy termination through nonpayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that a written request is necessary to reinstate a lapsed policy, which operationalizes the definition provided in fact_sentence_1 about restoring a lapsed policy’s active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy restores access to the originally specified death benefit, making the initial definition of payables crucial post-reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy depends on actions taken after the expiration of the grace period. Since the grace period is explicitly stated as 31 days, its existence defines when reinstatement may become required, making it foundational to understanding the timing of such requests.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="d822587b-a5be-4232-b595-d6f428b09987">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy after missing the $420 annual premium payment depends on fulfilling requirements such as submitting a written request, proving insurability, and paying back dues—including the original premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="3af0e3a5-6ae4-44d2-9986-8f2a02aac638">
  <data key="d3">A written request for reinstatement is essential to revive the policy and maintain eligibility for the beneficiary, Taylor Ellis, to claim the death benefit under the original terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables benefit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e">
  <data key="d3">A written request for reinstatement ensures the policy can remain effective, thereby preserving Taylor Ellis’s role as the designated beneficiary and enabling her to receive the death benefit when applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables beneficiary right</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="6c0901ed-f52a-4ce9-9d52-9547016ca265">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a written reinstatement request applies specifically to policies that have lapsed, such as one originally scheduled to run until July 31, 2045, meaning this rule directly impacts whether the full coverage term can be preserved beyond any interruption.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a written reinstatement request (fact_sentence_1) relies on the overall enforceability of policy terms, which is upheld by the severability clause described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement procedures depend on legally binding contract terms, which remain effective per the clause stating that provisions endure unless invalid. This ensures the requirement for a written request remains enforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">The necessity of a written reinstatement request depends on the policy being the full and binding agreement between the parties, ensuring such requests adhere strictly to documented terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="66d34f7f-f03b-44b9-ae46-16416415bc2a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a written reinstatement request (fact_sentence_1) is supported by the rule that no policy term can be waived without written consent (fact_sentence_2), ensuring consistency in formal documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a written reinstatement request in fact_sentence_1 depends on the broader contractual safeguard in fact_sentence_2, which mandates that no policy term—including those related to reinstatement—can be waived without written approval from an authorized officer.</data>
