<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">To reinstate a lapsed policy, one must provide evidence of insurability. This condition arises specifically when a premium was not paid during the grace period, causing the policy to lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The need to submit evidence of insurability arises specifically because the policy has already lapsed due to failure to pay premiums within the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">Submitting evidence of insurability is essential to restore a lapsed policy’s validity so that benefits may eventually be paid, fulfilling the exception stated in the prior clause regarding non-payment during lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">Submitting evidence of insurability is necessary to qualify for reinstating a lapsed policy before the five-year deadline expires.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">Submitting evidence of insurability is dependent on having already initiated the reinstatement process through a written request.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is a mandatory requirement for reinstating a lapsed policy, enabling the restoration of continuous coverage once approved.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that proof of insurability is required before reinstatement, which sets a prerequisite condition. This requirement logically precedes and enables the fulfillment of fact_sentence_2, where overdue premiums with interest must be paid—a step dependent on being deemed eligible through acceptable insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="17de4c88-376a-4e6b-b992-7f89cc84bb9a">
  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of insurability enables policy reinstatement, after which the Suicide Exclusion provision begins anew from the reinstatement date.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="b32da2b1-a458-4c5b-bb4d-0cd663f0dd82">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is necessary to reinstate a lapsed policy, which initiates the renewal of contractual protections such as the incontestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">A prerequisite for reinstating a lapsed policy—proof of insurability—is part of the overall set of terms governing when and how benefits may be paid upon death.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="7b26fed4-7c69-4d32-aa07-45ab4d3be614">
  <data key="d3">The need to submit evidence of insurability creates a foundation upon which insurers may impose further documentation demands, depending on what appears reasonable under the circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required only after a policy has lapsed due to missed payments during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability to reinstate a lapsed policy implies that the grace period serves as a buffer before such stringent requirements apply, ensuring continuity only if timely action occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">A lapsed policy loses coverage, but reinstatement becomes possible upon submission and acceptance of evidence of insurability, effectively restoring prior coverage conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables recovery</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires proof of insurability, which becomes relevant only after failure to pay during the grace period—a scenario covered by the first statement’s condition regarding unpaid premiums affecting the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability to reinstate a lapsed policy implies that the grace period serves as a buffer before reinstatement becomes necessary, making its existence crucial to avoiding the need for medical underwriting.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy necessitates proving insurability, confirming that the original reason for lapse—nonpayment—is now addressable through corrective action.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
