  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is necessary to reactivate a lapsed policy so that the previously specified death benefit under the policy may become payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability is needed only after the grace period expires and the policy lapses, making the 31-day grace period critical in avoiding this requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a" target="d822587b-a5be-4232-b595-d6f428b09987">
  <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability to reinstate a lapsed policy implies that ongoing eligibility depends on meeting underwriting standards, reinforcing the importance of consistent premium payments such as the $420 annual fee mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
