<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">The necessity to pay overdue premiums with interest arises specifically because the policy has already lapsed due to missed payments beyond the grace period, making reinstatement dependent on fulfilling those conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest arises specifically after a policy has lapsed due to failure to make timely payments, thereby terminating coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">Paying overdue premiums with interest is essential to reinstate a lapsed policy, thereby enabling the potential receipt of benefits after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">Payment of overdue premiums with interest is a prerequisite for reinstating a lapsed policy, enabling its restoration within the allowed five-year timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">Payment of overdue premiums with interest is a mandatory step after submitting a written reinstatement request. This financial condition depends on having formally initiated the reinstatement process.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 mandates payment of past-due premiums with interest, a necessary action after eligibility has been confirmed. This financial obligation depends on first satisfying fact_sentence_1, which verifies the applicant’s current insurability status prior to reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">Payment of overdue premiums with interest is a prerequisite that allows reinstatement, enabling coverage to resume retroactively from when the lapse occurred.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="b32da2b1-a458-4c5b-bb4d-0cd663f0dd82">
  <data key="d3">Paying overdue premiums with interest enables reinstatement, which triggers the start of a fresh incontestability period beginning from the reinstatement date.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">Payment of overdue premiums with interest is a specific term under the policy that affects eligibility for benefits upon death. Therefore, it falls under the general rule that the death benefit is subject to all policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">subsumed by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">Overdue premiums paid during reinstatement include interest, whereas if the policyholder dies before reinstatement, those same unpaid premiums reduce the death benefit instead of being repaid directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">alternative consequence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes the requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest at the company’s rate. Fact_sentence_2 ensures that this rate is legally bounded from being too low, providing a minimum threshold based on state regulations.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy demands payment of past-due premiums plus interest, directly stemming from the prior failure to meet the initial payment deadline.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement after lapse depends on fulfilling requirements like paying past-due premiums with interest, implying that prior grace period protection was exhausted.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest enables the restoration of coverage after its termination due to lapse, thus providing a mechanism to reverse the outcome described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables recovery</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">Overdue premiums must be repaid with interest upon reinstatement, which directly affects whether the death benefit remains intact—if the insured died during the grace period, such arrears would already have been subtracted from the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy after the grace period depends on paying overdue premiums with interest, confirming that the initial 31-day grace period was insufficient for timely renewal.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">Requiring interest on overdue premiums during reinstatement implies that failure to pay within the grace period results in a lapse, directly linking back to the definition provided in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest is integral to the reinstatement process, ensuring policies can be revived after lapse under defined conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy requires paying past-due premiums with interest, enabling the original death benefit—defined in the Policy Specifications—to remain enforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Requiring interest on overdue premiums when reinstating hinges on the existence of a grace period, such as the 31-day window mentioned in the first fact, making it essential for triggering the reinstatement condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="d822587b-a5be-4232-b595-d6f428b09987">
  <data key="d3">Failure to pay the $420 annual premium results in potential lapse, requiring reinstatement with added interest—a condition grounded in the existence of the original premium figure described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="3af0e3a5-6ae4-44d2-9986-8f2a02aac638">
  <data key="d3">The obligation to repay overdue premiums with interest ensures the policy stays active so that Taylor Ellis, as named beneficiary, can receive the full face amount upon the insured’s death.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy after a missed premium requires payment of overdue amounts plus interest, ensuring the original beneficiary, Taylor Ellis, retains eligibility for payout provided the process is completed correctly.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="6c0901ed-f52a-4ce9-9d52-9547016ca265">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest during reinstatement (fact_sentence_2) applies specifically to policies with extended durations such as the one described in fact_sentence_1, ensuring continuity of coverage over its full span.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1's requirement for paying overdue premiums with interest is upheld and reinforced by the broader legal principle stated in fact_sentence_2, which preserves contract integrity despite potential challenges.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest ensures financial accountability upon reinstatement, which supports the broader legal framework where policies retain validity even if individual clauses are challenged. This reinforces the policy’s structural robustness when interpreted under applicable laws.</data>
  <data key="d4">suppords legal framework</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="66d34f7f-f03b-44b9-ae46-16416415bc2a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest depends on the enforceability of contractual terms, which cannot be altered without written confirmation per the policy's provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest reflects a specific obligation under the policy, which operates within the broader contractual framework established by the "complete agreement" clause. This ensures such provisions are enforceable only as defined in the entire document.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of contract</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest depends on the enforceability of contractual terms, which cannot be altered without written confirmation from an authorized officer as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
