<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy restores its original status, effectively reversing the consequences described when a premium was missed during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">reverses consequence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores coverage as though the policy was continuous, but this option is only available after coverage has been terminated by nonpayment during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">preceded by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy restores its coverage retroactively, meaning benefits could then be payable from the point of reinstatement onward, fulfilling the exception stated in the prior clause about no benefits being payable during lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables benefits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores full policy coverage retroactively, making the prior lapse irrelevant under the terms of renewal eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement results in coverage resuming as if it were never interrupted, but only after a formal request has been submitted and approved.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">Once a lapsed policy is successfully reinstated through submission of proof of insurability, coverage is treated as if it never terminated.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">The resumption of coverage as though continuous depends directly on fulfilling the requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="b32da2b1-a458-4c5b-bb4d-0cd663f0dd82">
  <data key="d3">When a lapsed policy is reinstated, coverage restarts retroactively, and thus the incontestability clause reinitiates from the reinstatement date to protect the insured's interests under renewed terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores continuous coverage, enabling the policyholder to remain eligible for death benefits should the insured die while the policy is active prior to expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="17de4c88-376a-4e6b-b992-7f89cc84bb9a">
  <data key="d3">When a policy is reinstated, its coverage is treated as if it never lapsed. However, specific exclusions such as the suicide clause begin again from the reinstatement date, ensuring fresh eligibility criteria apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores continuous coverage, ensuring that any subsequent death benefit claim is fully subject to the original policy's terms and conditions, including eligibility requirements and limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores coverage retroactively, but any unpaid premiums remain obligations that reduce the final death benefit if the insured dies after reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="7b26fed4-7c69-4d32-aa07-45ab4d3be614">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores continuous coverage, but the insurance company may require extra documents based on its assessment of reasonableness.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">When a lapsed policy is reinstated, coverage resumes as if uninterrupted, enabling the full execution of death benefit provisions, including lump-sum payments upon the insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement enables the policy to continue as though it never lapsed, reversing the consequence described in the earlier statement about automatic lapse due to missed payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">reverses consequence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores continuous coverage from the point of lapse, implying that prior periods like the grace period were essential for maintaining eligibility to return to active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">The ability to reinstate a lapsed policy implies that prior termination was conditional and reversible, directly linking back to the moment coverage ceases upon lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables recovery</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="a20ed2b4-2a6b-44d6-aa80-4f3de6e88160">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores continuous coverage status, but if death occurred during the grace period prior to reinstatement, the death benefit would still reflect deductions for unpaid premiums under the original terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">exclusionary condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement restores continuous coverage status only if initiated within five years after lapse, implying the grace period’s role in preventing automatic termination and preserving eligibility for revival.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement effectively reverses the consequences of a lapse by reactivating the policy’s original terms, thereby negating its termination caused by nonpayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">reverses consequence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The resumption of coverage as though the policy never lapsed depends entirely on successfully completing the reinstatement process.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a policy restores its prior status, preserving the originally specified death benefit outlined in the Policy Specifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
