<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable if the policy remains in force at the time of death. This implies that timely premium payments—including within the grace period—are necessary to maintain policy status and avoid lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The occurrence of a death claim under fact_sentence_2 presupposes that the policy was active at the time of death, which contradicts the situation described in fact_sentence_1 where the policy has already lapsed due to nonpayment.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">Death benefits are only payable if the policy is in force at the time of death, meaning it cannot have lapsed without reinstatement. Thus, reinstatement becomes essential to preserve payout eligibility after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">ensures payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a death benefit depends on the policy being actively in force, which is ensured through successful reinstatement after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="17de4c88-376a-4e6b-b992-7f89cc84bb9a">
  <data key="d3">The rule that the death benefit is paid if the insured dies during the policy’s term depends on exceptions like the suicide exclusion, which resets upon reinstatement, potentially invalidating the claim despite the policy being active.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes when the death benefit is triggered—upon the insured's death during policy validity. Fact_sentence_2 explains that this trigger depends on fulfilling all policy terms, thus qualifying the conditionality of the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies during the policy term, the insurer pays the death benefit to the beneficiary. This benefit is specifically defined by the face amount stated in the policy's specifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies during the policy term, the insurer pays the death benefit to the beneficiary, but any outstanding debts reduce the final amount received.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies during the policy term, the insurer pays the death benefit to the beneficiary. However, any unpaid premiums are deducted from this amount before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit depends on the submission of verified proof of the insured's death, ensuring legitimacy before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is payable upon the insured's death during policy validity only after submitting required proof, such as a certified death certificate, to verify eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires proof</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="9a3ebe6d-6903-418b-acd4-b78709d3f595">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies during the policy term, the company may pay the death benefit, but first conducts an investigation into the cause and circumstances of death to verify eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="6b2f5e21-9f40-4e43-859c-578858c6f470">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies while the policy is active, the insurer generally pays the death benefit. However, this obligation may be challenged by the insurer if the claim arises within the contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit specified in fact_sentence_1 is generally distributed in a lump sum, as clarified by fact_sentence_2, which details the standard payment format unless modified by election.</data>
  <data key="d4">payment method</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies while the policy is active, the insurer pays the death benefit to the designated beneficiary. After this payment is due, the beneficiary may elect an alternative payment arrangement instead of receiving a lump sum.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies during the policy’s term, the insurer becomes obligated to pay the death benefit. This payment occurs swiftly once all necessary claim documents have been submitted and verified by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies during the policy term, the insurer pays the death benefit to the beneficiary. Interest begins accruing from the date of death onward, increasing the total payout when it is eventually disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">includes interest</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="1fa01fa6-dfb3-4343-85a2-88951da5f49b">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies while the policy is active, the death benefit is payable to the designated beneficiary. If that beneficiary predeceases the insured, the proceeds transfer to the contingent beneficiary, ensuring continuity of distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">When the insured dies while the policy is active, the death benefit is paid to the designated beneficiary. If no contingent beneficiary survives the insured, the proceeds are distributed according to alternative arrangements specified in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit upon the insured's death depends on the policy remaining in force, which is maintained by the grace period defined in fact_sentence_1, making it a necessary condition for claim validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">The promise of a death benefit upon the insured's passing depends on the policy remaining in force; if it has lapsed due to unpaid premiums, the obligation to pay does not arise, rendering the death benefit unenforceable despite the original intent.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of receiving a death benefit hinges on the policy being active at the time of death, making reinstatement crucial—it allows a previously lapsed policy to become active again, thus satisfying the precondition stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes the condition under which the death benefit is paid, relying on the predefined amount established by fact_sentence_1 in the policy documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">The standard death benefit payout triggered by the insured's death while the policy is active depends on corrected terms—if age was misstated, the benefit adjusts accordingly based on the actual age.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The standard death benefit payout applies only after accounting for any misrepresentations; thus, if sex was misrepresented, the actual payout may differ from the nominal benefit described in the standard clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">The provision that the death benefit is paid when the insured dies while the policy is in force depends critically on maintaining coverage through timely premium payments—or via the grace period specified here.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="d822587b-a5be-4232-b595-d6f428b09987">
  <data key="d3">The promise to pay the death benefit depends on the policy being kept current, which requires paying the $420 annual premium on time.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="3af0e3a5-6ae4-44d2-9986-8f2a02aac638">
  <data key="d3">The clause stating that the death benefit is payable upon the insured’s death during the policy’s term directly supports the role of Taylor Ellis as the rightful recipient, confirming the purpose of the beneficiary designation made in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e">
  <data key="d3">The condition outlined in fact_sentence_2—payment of the death benefit—is fully applicable only when the beneficiary is properly designated, such as Taylor Ellis, as confirmed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="6c0901ed-f52a-4ce9-9d52-9547016ca265">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the consequence of dying while the policy is active, which relies entirely on the validity and timing of coverage outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit obligation depends on the overall enforceability of the policy’s terms, including any potentially invalid provisions being severed without affecting the payout clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit obligation described in fact_sentence_1 is upheld by the legal principle in fact_sentence_2, which ensures that key policy provisions survive judicial invalidation, preserving the insurer’s duty to pay when triggered.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="66d34f7f-f03b-44b9-ae46-16416415bc2a">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit provision depends on adherence to formal policy terms, including the requirement for written waivers to ensure contractual stability and prevent unauthorized changes affecting payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit obligation described in fact_sentence_1 relies on the policy's legal integrity, which is affirmed by fact_sentence_2 stating it represents the entire agreement between the parties.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for written approval to waive policy terms supports the enforceability of conditions governing death benefit payments, ensuring that claims are processed according to established, non-waived provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
