<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only available if the policy remains in force at the time of death. Since failure to pay a premium leads to policy lapse, maintaining coverage depends on timely payments, directly affecting eligibility for the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's availability depends entirely on adherence to policy rules, such as maintaining active status through timely payments. Therefore, failure to pay premiums and subsequent lapse invalidates the right to receive benefits, making the timing of payment critical.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit follow all policy terms includes provisions such as reinstatement after lapse, which explains why benefits aren't payable without meeting those conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="e97bc08e-664f-4d67-a896-a8654db9c55e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit follow all policy terms includes provisions such as timely reinstatement after lapse, making reinstatement within five years essential for claim eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="7f26a565-4af4-450c-9a70-1dd435ed96e5">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's availability depends on adherence to all policy provisions, such as timely reinstatement through a formal request after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="e7c4ba5d-2f8a-4bd9-8e77-4018f8285f7a">
  <data key="d3">The condition that death benefits follow all policy terms includes requirements like providing proof of insurability if the policy was previously lapsed and being reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is subject to all policy terms, any requirements related to reinstatement—such as paying overdue premiums with interest—are inherently applicable when determining claim entitlement after death.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is always subject to policy terms—including reinstatement rules—the resumption of coverage upon reinstatement ensures such benefits remain enforceable under the full contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="17de4c88-376a-4e6b-b992-7f89cc84bb9a">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is bound by all policy terms, the reactivation of the suicide exclusion at reinstatement is consistent with those overarching conditions governing payout eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes that the death benefit is governed by policy terms, which includes the scenario described in fact_sentence_1 where the benefit is paid upon the insured’s death while the policy is active.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's value is determined by the policy’s specified terms, including the Face Amount listed in the Policy Specifications. This ensures consistency between contractual obligations and payout amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is subject to all policy terms, including financial obligations like debt repayment. Therefore, any indebtedness reduces the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is governed by all policy terms, including financial obligations like unpaid premiums, which directly affect its final payout amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's availability depends on adherence to policy terms, including providing official proof of death. This ensures only verified claims are processed.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that the death benefit depends on policy terms, and fact_sentence_2 clarifies that one essential part of those terms is providing a certified death certificate as proof.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="7b26fed4-7c69-4d32-aa07-45ab4d3be614">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for additional documentation arises from the need to uphold the policy's terms governing the death benefit. This ensures compliance with established conditions during claim processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="9a3ebe6d-6903-418b-acd4-b78709d3f595">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit adhere to policy terms enables the insurance company to conduct an investigation into the cause and circumstances of death to verify claim legitimacy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's disbursement method, including the default lump-sum payment, is determined by the policy's stated terms and conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="6b2f5e21-9f40-4e43-859c-578858c6f470">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's payout is constrained by policy terms, including the right of the insurer to challenge claims during the contestability period, which limits when benefits can be paid without dispute.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit being subject to policy terms includes mechanisms like interest accumulation, ensuring financial accuracy during claim processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">includes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's availability depends on policy terms, including eligibility and claim requirements. An alternate payout method may be selected by the beneficiary if the claim meets those established conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's availability hinges on adherence to policy terms, including timely submission and approval of claim documents, which triggers prompt payment once verified.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit’s calculation may depend on interest accrual, which is regulated by minimum standards set by state law. This ensures fairness and consistency in payout amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is bound by policy rules, including potential alternatives like different payout methods chosen before death. This allows the policy owner to tailor how proceeds are received after the insured passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions alternative</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="1fa01fa6-dfb3-4343-85a2-88951da5f49b">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's distribution is governed by policy terms, including rules about beneficiary succession. This includes paying proceeds to contingent beneficiaries if no primary beneficiary survives the insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's disbursement depends on policy terms, including beneficiary hierarchy. If no contingent beneficiary survives, the proceeds follow the policy’s default provisions, likely going to the estate.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's availability depends on maintaining policy status through mechanisms like the grace period, making its enforcement conditional on timely premium handling.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's availability hinges on maintaining policy validity; failure to pay premiums within the grace period results in lapse, thereby negating the right to claim the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's availability depends on the policy being active, which requires successful reinstatement if it has lapsed.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit comply with all policy terms relies on the precise definition of the payable amount established in the Policy Specifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">The rule about adjusting benefits based on accurate age applies because the death benefit is ultimately bound by all policy terms, including accuracy requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The general rule that the death benefit follows all policy terms encompasses the specific case where misstatement of sex alters the benefit amount accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">general rule</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
