<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit being equal to the face amount depends on the policy being active at the time of death; if the policy has already lapsed from nonpayment, the beneficiary receives nothing despite the stated face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents payability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit being equal to the face amount assumes the policy is active at time of death; however, if it has lapsed without reinstatement, even this defined benefit becomes unpayable, aligning with fact_sentence_1’s restriction.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on active status</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit payable upon the insured’s death is equal to the face amount detailed in the policy documents, ensuring clarity about the payout size when triggered under qualifying conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">defines</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">The Face Amount serves as the defined death benefit under the policy, but only when consistent with applicable terms and conditions governing payouts upon death.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit starts at the face amount specified in the policy. Unpaid premiums reduce this amount before disbursement, ensuring accurate settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit starts at the face amount specified in the policy. Any outstanding debts reduce this total before disbursement to beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's value is fixed at the face amount only if the insurer receives verified proof of the insured's death, ensuring the claim is legitimate before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is determined by the face amount specified in the policy, but it can only be claimed after providing due proof, such as a certified death certificate, confirming the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires proof</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="6b2f5e21-9f40-4e43-859c-578858c6f470">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is normally equal to the face amount, but the insurer retains the right to dispute the claim if it occurs within the contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="9a3ebe6d-6903-418b-acd4-b78709d3f595">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is defined by the policy’s face amount, but its disbursement depends on an insurer review of the death’s cause and circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's fixed value, defined by the face amount, determines the total sum available for distribution. This ensures clarity in calculating the lump-sum payment when the claim is processed.</data>
  <data key="d4">determines</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is determined by the face amount specified in the policy. After the insured’s death, the beneficiary may elect an alternative payment method instead of receiving the full amount as a lump sum.</data>
  <data key="d4">optional extension</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is determined as the face amount specified in the policy, which directly informs the exact sum payable when claims are approved. This ensures clarity and consistency in the disbursement process once documentation is verified.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is determined by the face amount specified in the policy, and upon the insured’s death, interest starts accruing on this fixed amount until it is paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">determines</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit's final payout depends on accruing interest, which must meet legal standards set by state regulations. This ensures financial integrity and fairness in benefit calculations.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit amount, set at the face amount per the policy specifications, determines what is available for distribution. If no primary beneficiary survives, the proceeds from that fixed amount are directed to an unspecified alternate recipient.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit depends on ongoing policy validity, which is maintained by the grace period allowing delayed premium payments without immediate termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit depends on the policy remaining active; if it lapses due to missed premiums, the promised face amount becomes unpayable regardless of its stated value.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit depends on the policy being active; reinstatement allows the policy to regain its active state so the death benefit can be claimed.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the Face Amount as the death benefit, which is further validated by fact_sentence_1 stating that this figure is explicitly set forth in the Policy Specifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">The standard death benefit being the face amount applies only when there are no material misrepresentations; if age was misstated, the benefit is adjusted downward according to the corrected actuarial value.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on accuracy</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The face amount defined in the policy serves as the default death benefit, but may be reduced if the insured’s sex was misrepresented during application.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
