<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">When a death occurs while the policy is active, the death benefit may be reduced by outstanding debts (sentence 2). However, if the policy has already lapsed without reinstatement, no benefits—including those adjusted for debt—are payable, making the debt deduction conditional on policy status.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding debts are subtracted from the death benefit only when the policyholder dies while the policy is still active and benefits are being paid out.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is reduced by outstanding debts, it reflects a direct consequence of being bound by policy terms, particularly those related to liabilities.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding debts decrease the death benefit, which is initially equal to the face amount stated in the policy specifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">reduces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">Indebtedness reduces the death benefit just as unpaid premiums do. Both types of liabilities are settled from the proceeds prior to distribution to beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">combines with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">The existence of indebtedness affects the final payout but only after the insurer confirms the insured's death through official documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate ensures validity before any financial calculations like debt deductions occur. Without verified proof of death, the insurer cannot proceed with determining the net death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="7b26fed4-7c69-4d32-aa07-45ab4d3be614">
  <data key="d3">The statement that any indebtedness is deducted from the death benefit pertains to the final payout calculation after claims verification. Additional documentation might be needed to confirm the existence or amount of such indebtedness, supporting accurate settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">The presence of indebtedness affects the final payout amount, which influences how much is ultimately due once claim documents are approved and processed.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">The existence of indebtedness directly impacts the final payout amount, which may influence how much interest accumulates over time since the effective claim value changes post-debt deduction.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">The presence of indebtedness reduces the death benefit available for distribution. This adjusted amount would only be distributed if no surviving beneficiaries exist, triggering the contingency clause described in sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">affects outcome</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding indebtedness affecting the death benefit depends on whether the policy remained active through the grace period; if it lapsed, reinstatement could create new liabilities impacting the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">The presence of indebtedness affects claim payouts only if the policy remains in force; however, if it lapses due to nonpayment, there is no payout at all regardless of debt status.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding debts reduce the death benefit, making it necessary to settle these obligations during reinstatement, thereby linking the financial requirements of reinstatement to post-death payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding debt reduces the death benefit, meaning the amount stated in the policy specifications may not reflect the actual cash received by beneficiaries due to deductions for unpaid balances.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding debts reduce the death benefit regardless of whether the benefit was recalculated due to age misstatement, so the adjustment for age does not override deductions for liabilities.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding indebtedness reduces the death benefit regardless of whether the sex was correctly stated. Even if the death benefit is recalculated due to a prior misstatement of sex, the adjusted amount remains subject to reduction by any pre-existing policy loans or liabilities.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding indebtedness reduces the death benefit, but only if the policy was active at the time of death—which depends on timely premium payments or use of the 31-day grace period to maintain validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
