<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">Before the company pays a death benefit, it must verify the insured's death through official documentation. However, this step is irrelevant if the policy has already lapsed due to missed payments, rendering the claim invalid regardless of proof.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is required before the company pays the death benefit, especially relevant when determining whether the policy had been reinstated post-lapse or remained inactive at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary for any death benefit payment, even if the policy had been reinstated after lapsing, ensuring legitimacy of the claim irrespective of prior status.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death must be submitted prior to any payout, serving as a prerequisite for triggering the obligation to pay the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">Requiring proof of death is necessary because the death benefit is subject to all policy terms, ensuring legitimacy and compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is required prior to any payment, including the full face amount specified in the policy, to validate eligibility for the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death must be submitted prior to any adjustment of the death benefit, including deductions for unpaid premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is mandatory before any calculation involving deductions such as indebtedness can take place.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that the company needs verified proof of death to disburse benefits. Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that a certified death certificate serves as such required proof, directly supporting the procedural requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="9a3ebe6d-6903-418b-acd4-b78709d3f595">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is required before payment, and the company may investigate the cause and circumstances to validate that proof.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="7b26fed4-7c69-4d32-aa07-45ab4d3be614">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 mandates submission of proof of death, and fact_sentence_2 clarifies that further documentation could be needed depending on what the insurer deems reasonable under the circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death must be submitted before any death benefit can be processed. Only after validation does the insurer proceed to pay the benefit, typically in a lump sum if no other election exists.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death must be submitted before any action on benefit disbursement can occur. After such verification, the beneficiary may choose an alternate payment method if desired.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death must be submitted before any action regarding the death benefit can occur. Upon receiving and approving such proof, the insurer proceeds to make the payment promptly.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death triggers the start of interest accrual on the death benefit, ensuring compensation reflects the delay in disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="1fa01fa6-dfb3-4343-85a2-88951da5f49b">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death must be submitted before benefits can be processed, ensuring legitimacy. Only after validation does the process proceed to determine whether proceeds go to a contingent beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death must be submitted before the insurer determines who receives the benefits. This step ensures that only legitimate claims proceed to beneficiary designation checks.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary for payout only when the policy is active at the time of death, including cases where the event occurs during the grace period defined in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is required to pay the death benefit, even though the policy may have lapsed earlier due to missed premium payments during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">Proof of the insured's death is required to trigger a death benefit payout, regardless of whether the policy was previously reinstated after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on coverage</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is required to activate the payment of the death benefit already defined in the policy specifications, making it a prerequisite for claiming the stated amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary to trigger any payout, including adjustments made due to age misstatement as specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death, required by fact_sentence_2, enables the claim process through which the adjusted death benefit from fact_sentence_1 is calculated and disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary to trigger the death benefit, but such a claim can only succeed if the policy was still active at the time of death—including through use of the 31-day grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="d822587b-a5be-4232-b595-d6f428b09987">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is necessary to trigger the payout, but only applies if the policy has remained in force—requiring consistent payment of the $420 annual premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="3af0e3a5-6ae4-44d2-9986-8f2a02aac638">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to provide proof of death ensures that Taylor Ellis, the designated beneficiary, receives the policy proceeds under the correct conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for proof of death ensures that the designated beneficiary, Taylor Ellis, can legally receive the proceeds intended for her under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="6c0901ed-f52a-4ce9-9d52-9547016ca265">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is required to activate the death benefit, but only applies if the insured passed away while the policy was still in force, i.e., between August 1, 2025, and July 31, 2045.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1's requirement for proof of death depends on the broader contractual framework upheld by fact_sentence_2, which ensures that key provisions remain enforceable regardless of partial invalidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 enforces a critical step in the claims process, which remains essential regardless of legal challenges to any clause. Fact_sentence_2 supports the stability of such requirements by ensuring that even if parts of the policy are challenged, core obligations like proving death remain intact.</data>
  <data key="d4">severability support</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="66d34f7f-f03b-44b9-ae46-16416415bc2a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for due proof of death aligns with the broader principle that contract terms cannot be altered informally, reinforcing the need for official documentation in claims processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death is required to trigger payout, which relies on the policy's terms being legally binding and comprehensive, as affirmed by the "complete agreement" clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 mandates official documentation for claiming benefits, which aligns with the broader principle in fact_sentence_2 that no policy terms—including claim-related conditions—can be altered without written approval from an authorized representative.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
