<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is needed to validate the claim and trigger the payment of the death benefit when the insured passes away while the policy remains active.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies the need for a certified death certificate as proof, which serves as a key component supporting the broader conditionality described in fact_sentence_1 regarding claim eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is essential documentation needed to validate a claim, ensuring the death benefit—the face amount—is released according to policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate serves as essential evidence confirming the insured's passing, enabling the insurer to proceed with calculating and distributing the death benefit, including accounting for any unpaid premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables calculation of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death via a certified death certificate is necessary prior to applying deductions such as indebtedness from the death benefit. This step validates eligibility for payout distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is defined as one form of due proof necessary for claiming a death benefit. Therefore, it satisfies the prerequisite outlined in fact_sentence_1 regarding documentation needed from the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="7b26fed4-7c69-4d32-aa07-45ab4d3be614">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate establishes a baseline for proof of death. Additional documentation may be needed depending on the insurer's assessment of what is reasonably necessary to validate the claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="9a3ebe6d-6903-418b-acd4-b78709d3f595">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is necessary to initiate the claims process, providing foundational evidence that enables the insurance company to proceed with its right to investigate the cause and circumstances of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="6b2f5e21-9f40-4e43-859c-578858c6f470">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is essential evidence used during the claims process, particularly when the insurance company has the right to contest the claim due to potential misrepresentation during application.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death via a certified death certificate is necessary before the death benefit can be processed and paid out. This requirement ensures legitimacy prior to any distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death via certified death certificate establishes eligibility for claims, enabling the beneficiary to access alternative payment options such as installment payments or annuities.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is a critical document needed to initiate the claims process, ensuring authenticity and legal validity of the death event.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="1fa01fa6-dfb3-4343-85a2-88951da5f49b">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death via certified death certificate enables validation of eligibility, which determines whether proceeds proceed to contingent beneficiaries per the stated order.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death, including a certified death certificate, initiates the claims process, allowing interest on the death benefit to begin accruing from the date of death onward.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is required to validate the insured's passing, enabling the claims process that determines who receives proceeds if no primary beneficiary survives.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is required to validate a claim, especially relevant if the insured died during the grace period when the policy was technically active but unpaid, making documentation vital despite delayed payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for claim</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">Providing a certified death certificate enables a claim only if the policy remains active; otherwise, the requirement becomes moot due to prior lapse caused by unpaid premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">Providing a certified death certificate enables the insurer to validate the event and proceed with paying the pre-specified death benefit outlined in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="ae130c33-876d-4d39-9ee6-6b6250047099">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is necessary to initiate a claim, which may trigger recalculations of the death benefit if the insured’s age was previously misrepresented.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death via a certified death certificate is necessary before any death benefit—even a recalculated one—is disbursed. Thus, even if the benefit is adjusted per fact_sentence_1, the claim cannot proceed without fulfilling the evidentiary requirement stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death via a certified death certificate is necessary to trigger the payout mechanism, but only applies if the policy was still active during the insured's death—which relies on paying premiums within the 31-day grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="d822587b-a5be-4232-b595-d6f428b09987">
  <data key="d3">Providing a certified death certificate enables the beneficiary to receive the policy's face amount only if the policy was active at the time of death, which depends on consistent premium payments such as the $420 annual fee.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="3af0e3a5-6ae4-44d2-9986-8f2a02aac638">
  <data key="d3">Providing a certified death certificate is essential for Taylor Ellis to claim the $500,000 death benefit under the policy where she is listed as the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e">
  <data key="d3">A certified death certificate is essential to activate the benefit payout to Taylor Ellis, whose status as the designated beneficiary determines eligibility under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="6c0901ed-f52a-4ce9-9d52-9547016ca265">
  <data key="d3">Proof of death via a certified death certificate is necessary to initiate a claim only if the policy was still active at the time of death, which depends on the coverage period outlined in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate supports claim processing, which remains viable even if some policy terms are invalidated, thanks to the severability clause ensuring continued functionality of core provisions like beneficiary payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">severability support</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate supports the administrative process governed by the policy’s enduring legal framework, ensuring claims proceed according to valid, enforceable terms despite potential challenges to specific provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">The need for a certified death certificate aligns with the policy’s role as the complete agreement, ensuring documented verification supports claims under its defined rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="66d34f7f-f03b-44b9-ae46-16416415bc2a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate aligns with the need for formal, written documentation under the policy’s rules, reinforcing the principle that changes or exceptions must follow strict written protocols.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a certified death certificate underscores the need for official documentation in claims processing, which aligns with the broader principle that changes to policy terms—including potential exceptions to such requirements—must follow strict written protocols enforced by authorized personnel.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
