<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="6c933248-145a-4629-9244-b471149ae619">
  <data key="d3">Lump-sum payment of death benefits applies when the insured passes away while the policy remains active. This assumes the policy has not lapsed due to missed premiums, making timely payment essential for triggering such payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="3c433250-298a-4a66-9011-6ba31393c55a">
  <data key="d3">The default provision that death benefits are paid in a lump sum depends on the policy being active, which only occurs when reinstatement has successfully resumed coverage after lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains the typical distribution method—the lump-sum payment—for the death benefit mentioned in fact_sentence_1, reinforcing how benefits are delivered upon claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that death benefits follow policy terms includes provisions about payment methods such as lump sums, reflecting contractual obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">subject to terms</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">The standard method of paying out the death benefit—as a lump sum—is directly based on the predetermined face amount stated in the policy’s specifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">derives from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">Lump-sum payment is the default method for death benefits, but it only applies after the insurer confirms the insured's death through required documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The standard payment of the death benefit in a lump sum depends on having properly submitted evidence such as a certified death certificate to validate the claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f">
  <data key="d3">The standard practice of paying death benefits in a lump sum depends on whether the beneficiary chooses an alternative arrangement. The ability to elect an alternative arises only after the insured’s death, allowing flexibility beyond the default method.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6">
  <data key="d3">The standard payment method for death benefits is a lump sum, but this can only be overridden if an alternative was previously elected. This election must occur before the insured’s death, making it dependent on proactive decision-making.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is generally paid in a lump sum, but this disbursement depends on timely processing after submission and approval of required claim documents.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">The lump-sum payment method specified in fact_sentence_1 creates the context in which interest begins accruing from the date of death, as outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence specifies how death benefit proceeds are generally disbursed—in a lump sum—unless changed by election. The second explains what happens if no surviving beneficiary exists, detailing the fallback recipient.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">The standard lump-sum death benefit payment depends on the policy remaining active, which is preserved by timely premium payment or use of the 31-day grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">A policy must remain in force beyond the grace period to ensure death benefit payouts, so avoiding lapse is necessary for the death benefit clause to apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The availability of a lump-sum death benefit depends on the policy being active, which necessitates successful reinstatement if previously lapsed, thus linking the two facts through policy continuity.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">The standard lump-sum distribution of death benefits relies on the pre-defined amount established in the Policy Specifications, making the payment dependent on that initial specification.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
