<edge source="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6" target="49c36df2-25ec-4244-9553-ec686e3f398d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">rate</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">Choosing an alternative payment option during life enables customized distribution of the death benefit, ensuring it aligns with the policyholder’s intent even when subject to standard policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout option</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">The ability to elect an alternative payment option allows the policyholder to deviate from the default lump-sum distribution, directly influencing how the death benefit is disbursed upon claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Alternative payment methods give the policy owner tools to meet premium deadlines, helping avoid triggering the end of the grace period defined in fact_sentence_1, thereby preserving coverage continuity.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">Having an alternative payment option may help avoid lapsing the policy due to missed premiums, thus mitigating the risk described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">avoids termination</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement becomes necessary when a policy lapses due to missed payments, but having flexible payment options might mitigate the risk of lapse altogether.</data>
  <data key="d4">reduces need for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">While the policy specifies the exact death benefit amount, it also permits the policyholder to elect different ways to receive those funds during the insured’s lifetime, offering administrative flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8d186265-a45d-4f5c-95c4-95d6c4eddd77" target="3d2d5591-f61c-4316-9ded-1ed908d5f8e6">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">prevented by</data>
</edge>
