<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">The beneficiary receives the death benefit upon the insured's death if the policy remains in force. This eligibility enables them to select an alternative payment option beyond the standard lump sum.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiaries have the option to choose an alternative payment arrangement post-death, provided it aligns with the policy’s governing terms and conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables option</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiaries have the option to select an alternate payment arrangement following the insured’s death. This choice applies regardless of the death benefit being equal to the stated face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="45eb8281-3543-4e01-bd76-8cddd037b578">
  <data key="d3">The availability of an alternative payment option allows the beneficiary flexibility in receiving proceeds, potentially mitigating the impact of reduced payouts caused by unpaid premiums being subtracted from the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">modified by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">After the insurer confirms the insured's death through proper documentation, the beneficiary gains the right to select an alternative payment arrangement for the proceeds.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The availability of alternative payment options depends on first satisfying proof-of-death requirements like submitting a certified death certificate.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">The availability of an alternative payment option—available post-death—directly modifies how the lump-sum payment may be delivered, providing a mechanism to deviate from the initial default condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">The availability of an alternative payment option for the beneficiary depends on the accumulation of interest on the death benefit, which begins at the time of death and continues until disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary payment options become relevant only if the policy survives beyond the grace period, meaning the grace period condition enables the subsequent claim process described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">The availability of alternative payment options for the beneficiary assumes the policy was active at the time of death, implying it did not lapse during the grace period, thus reinforcing the importance of timely premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The availability of alternative payment options for beneficiaries depends on the policy being active at time of death, which could have been ensured through reinstatement if previously lapsed.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a fixed death benefit, as outlined in the policy specs, enables the beneficiary to exercise alternative payment options based on that predetermined amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
