<edge source="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425" target="dc295506-9994-4bc6-8410-24347075b1d6">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for prompt payment of the death benefit implies that the policy must still be in force at the time of death. This relies on the premise established in sentence 1—that failure to pay leads to lapse and loss of coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">Prompt payment of death benefits depends on timely submission of documentation (sentence 2), assuming the policy was active at death. This condition implicitly excludes cases where the policy has lapsed without reinstatement, as noted in sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes lapsed cases</data>
