  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">Interest accruing from the date of death implies that timely submission of proof of death is essential to avoid prolonged delays in claiming benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The accrual of interest from the date of death implies that timely submission of proof, such as a certified death certificate, is essential to ensure full entitlement to accumulated interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">Since interest accrues from the date of death until payment, it directly affects the total amount received in the lump sum, reinforcing why the lump-sum distribution is significant.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="79ffd32a-ede6-403a-ac15-f636b8aa494f">
  <data key="d3">Accrued interest on the death benefit enhances the total payout value, making it relevant when considering alternative payment methods selected by the beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="81fd1296-c3bf-4581-b20f-126e5d595425">
  <data key="d3">Accrued interest from the date of death enhances the final death benefit amount, justifying why prompt payment is essential once documentation is approved.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8">
  <data key="d3">Interest on the death benefit accrues from the date of death to the payment date, and its rate is legally constrained to meet at least the minimum standard set by state regulations.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">Accrued interest on the death benefit applies only when the policy has remained in force past its due dates, meaning it depends on surviving the grace period without lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">Accrued interest applies only when the policy is still in force at the time of death; thus, it depends on avoiding lapse by timely premium payment during the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest during reinstatement reflects the insurer’s practice of charging interest for delayed payments, consistent with the rule that interest also accumulates on death benefits until payout, showing a shared mechanism of interest application across policy lifecycle events.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">While the death benefit is fixed per policy specs, its actual disbursement includes accumulated interest after death, meaning the effective payout depends on the initially specified amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="c7c925cb-8c15-4c3e-98c7-37dd24303a91">
  <data key="d3">The second fact explains that interest accumulates on the death benefit from the date of death, which applies regardless of whether the benefit was recalculated due to a misstated sex, meaning the corrected benefit still accrues interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">Accrued interest on the death benefit assumes the policy was active at time of death, which depends on timely premium payments or use of the 31-day grace period to avoid lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payout</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="d822587b-a5be-4232-b595-d6f428b09987">
  <data key="d3">Accrued interest on the death benefit depends on the policy remaining active, which relies on timely premium payments, including the $420 annual premium specified here.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="3af0e3a5-6ae4-44d2-9986-8f2a02aac638">
  <data key="d3">As the designated beneficiary, Taylor Ellis is entitled to receive the death benefit with accumulated interest, making the interest provision relevant to her final claim settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="e95a83d3-c700-45d5-abe2-2438276d3c5e">
  <data key="d3">The inclusion of accrued interest in the death benefit ensures that the designated beneficiary, Taylor Ellis, receives a greater payout than just the face amount, enhancing the value of the benefit she inherits.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="6c0901ed-f52a-4ce9-9d52-9547016ca265">
  <data key="d3">The extended coverage period specified in the first statement ensures that any death occurring before July 31, 2045, triggers the interest-on-benefit clause outlined in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">The rule that interest accrues on the death benefit relies on the policy's overall legal stability, which is upheld by the provision ensuring remaining terms stay effective even if some parts fail.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">The statement about accruing interest on the death benefit operates within the boundaries defined by the policy being the full agreement, ensuring such terms are binding and explicitly included.</data>
