<edge source="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8" target="f132426a-4a89-442f-804e-9685b2a8370a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 sets a statutory lower limit on the interest rate used when reinstating a lapsed policy. This constraint directly affects how much interest must be paid under fact_sentence_1, ensuring fairness and compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">The mandated minimum interest rate helps ensure that the death benefit remains compliant with policy terms, particularly regarding how much interest accumulates over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">A legally mandated minimum interest rate guarantees that any growth on the death benefit maintains acceptable returns, supporting the full realization of the stated face amount through compounding.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8" target="a807a94a-e844-41c7-ba21-2154a3872ba5">
  <data key="d3">State laws require a minimum interest rate, which ensures that the interest accruing on the death benefit—calculated from the date of death—is applied consistently and fairly.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that interest rates meet state minimum standards supports the financial integrity of reinstatement processes, ensuring consistent and lawful calculation of past-due charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8" target="9a6577b2-6763-4f14-9b38-f89dde765452">
  <data key="d3">A 31-day grace period exists so that policyholders may avoid lapse due to late payment, though failure to pay within this window results in interest being charged at rates no lower than those set by state law.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8" target="d822587b-a5be-4232-b595-d6f428b09987">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that interest rates meet legal standards ensures fair treatment when processing delayed premium payments tied to the $420 annual charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8" target="3af0e3a5-6ae4-44d2-9986-8f2a02aac638">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that interest rates meet legal minimums indirectly safeguards the financial obligations owed to beneficiaries like Taylor Ellis, ensuring fair treatment in cases involving delayed payments or claim settlements.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="66fc18f4-0f31-46f1-920e-779b2cd1cff8" target="6c0901ed-f52a-4ce9-9d52-9547016ca265">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that interest rates meet legal standards ensures fairness over the extended coverage window described in fact_sentence_1, supporting consistent financial integrity throughout the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">regulatory compliance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
