  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="00cdb05a-7f0a-4945-9a95-f087465d2dfe">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="3beaeca9-bfa6-4fd6-b9ba-9eaec31ac5d0">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">document</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="3daf933f-47d8-4796-96af-a0f66e2192dd">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">process</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="7e7b6217-44c6-462f-98f4-cf31bd077e8a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">right</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="3fd85832-897e-4720-9d8a-f99697442437">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">payment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="9721eaba-7de0-484e-a056-396bcc0c7476">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">rate</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="2a08c0b6-2e7e-4895-939b-cc9797b12f18">
  <data key="d3">The distribution of proceeds upon the insured's death depends on whether any surviving beneficiaries exist. In cases where only a contingent beneficiary remains, they receive the benefits after the primary beneficiary’s absence.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="8453f6b0-fb6e-4aa6-ab20-20d1e0198fd4">
  <data key="d3">When no surviving contingent beneficiary exists, the outcome aligns with the policy’s stated terms governing claim payouts, reinforcing that benefits are subject to contractual conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="2474d284-5bd2-401c-91b1-36a9a5e512cb">
  <data key="d3">When determining who receives the proceeds if no contingent beneficiary survives, the existence of a defined death benefit—the face amount—is essential context, as it establishes the total pool being distributed.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="b8c541a1-08d6-4493-9d12-7e4b17736e50">
  <data key="d3">When no contingent beneficiary survives the insured, the remaining proceeds—including any deductions for indebtedness—are determined by prior terms such as those governing debt settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">subject to debt</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="1ad14f44-4ab9-4865-bd44-65dbcba3e242">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary succession rules apply once death is confirmed through required documentation, ensuring funds are distributed appropriately if primary recipients predecease the insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="0eab6e49-c223-4495-87bb-58f1202750b4">
  <data key="d3">The absence of surviving primary beneficiaries triggers payout to an unspecified alternate recipient, but only after proper proof of death—including a certified death certificate—is submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="b641aff4-f260-4aa8-a157-55e5b6a64e79">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence outlines the contingency plan for distributing proceeds when no contingent beneficiary survives, which complements the first sentence’s focus on standard payout methods.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="1fa01fa6-dfb3-4343-85a2-88951da5f49b">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a surviving contingent beneficiary triggers the transfer of proceeds to an unspecified recipient after the primary beneficiary has already been ruled out.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="a49cafd1-8d48-414f-8488-d5ff6730e3d9">
  <data key="d3">A surviving contingent beneficiary receives proceeds only if the primary beneficiary predeceases the insured, assuming the policy was still in force through any applicable grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="9aff7508-84dd-468d-83c6-658c086cf16c">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary designation determines post-death disbursement only if the policy remains in force at the time of death. Even with clear beneficiary instructions, failure to maintain premium payments results in lapse, rendering those designations irrelevant.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The existence of contingent beneficiaries ensures proceeds are directed appropriately even if the primary beneficiary predeceases the insured, regardless of whether the policy was previously reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">The order of beneficiary payouts described in fact_sentence_2 hinges on the existence and specification of the death benefit amount detailed in fact_sentence_1, ensuring clarity in disbursement based on contractual obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="ac1a6b74-dc59-4a4f-a24b-16a083744b91">
  <data key="d3">When no primary beneficiary survives the insured, proceeds go to a specified alternate recipient; fact_sentence_2 clarifies that in ambiguous death scenarios, the beneficiary is presumed to have died first, thereby triggering such contingency provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="57f5cb31-60fc-403b-8faf-61bb58c44d33">
  <data key="d3">When no primary beneficiary survives the insured, proceeds go to a specified alternate recipient; this outcome hinges on whether the beneficiary is legally presumed dead before the insured, per state rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="0d942949-f688-4e68-85e8-07b70d1319c6">
  <data key="d3">The rule about irrevocable beneficiaries affects whether contingent beneficiaries can receive proceeds by restricting unilateral changes to the beneficiary list, thus influencing the outcome described in fact_sentence_1 regarding contingent distributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="a2150cee-d022-441d-940f-3a1ca38fb293">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a contingent beneficiary depends on the policy owner's ability to update designations, meaning changes allowed by fact_sentence_2 affect whether fact_sentence_1 triggers.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0">
  <data key="d3">The rule about beneficiary changes taking effect upon signature ensures that contingent beneficiaries can be properly designated before death, affecting whether proceeds flow to them per the condition stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="3f213a1e-e278-42fb-8c8b-f3adf267911d">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change after the insured’s death (fact_sentence_2) determines eligibility for receiving proceeds under clause 1, meaning such changes could prevent the default payout to a contingent beneficiary or estate.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="bca821e4-dd36-4856-bd49-b34de7e5162f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a broader contingency plan where proceeds go to an unspecified recipient if no contingent beneficiary survives, building upon the scenario described in fact_sentence_2, which defines the initial step of paying the contingent beneficiary when no primary beneficiary survives.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="23a68193-61ae-40df-becb-863cc2fa667b">
  <data key="d3">When no primary beneficiary survives the insured, proceeds default to a secondary recipient; fact_sentence_2 clarifies that if such a beneficiary remains unlocated within 90 days, the insurer may distribute funds to the estate instead.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="3e91835e-9ad1-4260-b452-07cf78be6476">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a default path for benefit disbursement when no contingent beneficiary survives, while fact_sentence_2 extends this by granting the insurer discretion to assign proceeds to individuals considered equitably entitled, offering broader administrative latitude.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">The clause governing beneficiary payouts remains effective even if parts of the policy are challenged, thanks to the principle of severability affirmed in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">The rule governing beneficiary payouts depends on the overall validity of the policy's clauses; if a key term were struck down, it could affect how proceeds are distributed, though the severability clause ensures such disruptions don’t invalidate the entire process.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">The clause specifying beneficiary disbursement depends on the policy being recognized as the definitive agreement, ensuring such terms are legally binding and self-contained.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="66d34f7f-f03b-44b9-ae46-16416415bc2a">
  <data key="d3">The rule requiring written waivers ensures that changes to beneficiary designations—like redirecting proceeds due to lack of surviving beneficiaries—are formally documented and legally binding.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">The rule requiring written approval for waivers ensures that changes to beneficiary designation—like shifting proceeds away from a contingent beneficiary—are formally validated, supporting the integrity of the payout process described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
