  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">organization</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="61508a60-cf4a-4cf2-b294-55f8621c813f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="d70c1e0e-57bf-45f8-9a44-e2c9c72d5baf">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="5f6753c8-0020-44d2-8a97-7c40512975d2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="0f7069b2-a026-4a72-b0af-49d470a23467">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">date</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="d680623c-b8e6-4216-87fc-f28fbd801474">
  <data key="d3">The timing of a beneficiary change hinges on the definition of who qualifies as the recipient; without defining the beneficiary, changes would lack purpose or meaning.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="75149b06-31da-4902-818b-05639e24c747">
  <data key="d3">Since a change of beneficiary requires a written request, its effectiveness hinges on fulfilling the prior condition set by the formal submission process outlined in the original designation rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="a2150cee-d022-441d-940f-3a1ca38fb293">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change depends on the policy owner having the legal right to make it; without revocability, changes cannot occur regardless of documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="3f213a1e-e278-42fb-8c8b-f3adf267911d">
  <data key="d3">The date a beneficiary change is signed determines its生效 (effectiveness). Even if the insurer records the change after the insured’s death, it still takes effect because the key trigger is the signed request, not the timing of administrative processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">effects from signature</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="0d942949-f688-4e68-85e8-07b70d1319c6">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change depends on whether the beneficiary is revocable; if irrevocable, the change cannot proceed without consent, limiting the applicability of the standard timing rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="bc01826e-0790-4744-905a-5c0919e140df">
  <data key="d3">Changing a beneficiary based on a signed request only applies if the beneficiary is revocable; if the beneficiary is irrevocable, such a change cannot proceed without their explicit consent.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="38974002-cdef-417b-abe4-05fe910d1ed4">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change depends on documentation and timing, which influences whether a contingent beneficiary is active at the time of death. This determines whether proceeds go to the estate under the rule stated here.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relevance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="bca821e4-dd36-4856-bd49-b34de7e5162f">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change depends on timely documentation, ensuring that updated beneficiaries are recognized before death. This supports proper execution of the payout sequence described in fact_sentence_2, especially if the original beneficiary was revoked prior to death.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="57f5cb31-60fc-403b-8faf-61bb58c44d33">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change depends on documentation timing, but its legal impact may be overridden if the new beneficiary is presumed to have predeceased the insured under statutory rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90">
  <data key="d3">The effectiveness of a beneficiary change determines whether an updated beneficiary qualifies to receive proceeds; if not, the proceeds default to the estate, aligning with the scenario described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="f075e888-0cb1-43c8-8ebf-84c98e1c462f">
  <data key="d3">The effective date of a beneficiary change depends on the signature of a written request, ensuring timely updates to distribution plans. This procedural detail supports fair outcomes by allowing accurate designation before death, indirectly enabling equitable claims like those involving funeral expense payers if no proper beneficiary exists.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional precedence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="91d5242d-2ab5-43dd-a6c9-1df492a48caf">
  <data key="d3">When a beneficiary change is formally executed via a signed document, it enables potential payout to the estate if no valid beneficiary exists at time of death. Payment to the estate fully satisfies the insurer’s legal responsibility under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="1fa01fa6-dfb3-4343-85a2-88951da5f49b">
  <data key="d3">Beneficiary changes affect the applicability of the contingent beneficiary provision, ensuring only intended parties receive proceeds per the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0" target="9f7028fc-d597-413b-ae31-675f57f9e024">
  <data key="d3">Properly executed beneficiary changes ensure that a contingent beneficiary exists, making the scenario in fact_sentence_1—that no survivor remains—more likely to trigger payout to the specified alternate recipient.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cdf9e6e6-6ab2-4f3b-b548-619f67f6fbbc" target="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">affected by beneficiary change</data>
</edge>
