<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="d680623c-b8e6-4216-87fc-f28fbd801474">
  <data key="d3">When the beneficiary fails to survive the insured, it triggers the contingency plan described in the policy, requiring payment to the estate instead of the individual originally named.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="75149b06-31da-4902-818b-05639e24c747">
  <data key="d3">When no beneficiary is designated in writing, the lack of formal documentation triggers the fallback mechanism where proceeds are paid to the estate instead.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires designation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="5c01ae55-a8cf-4383-9489-8098cb74d07d">
  <data key="d3">The absence of surviving beneficiaries leads insurers to apply rules about equitable distribution, including dividing proceeds equally if multiple beneficiaries were originally designated without specific allocations.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="a2150cee-d022-441d-940f-3a1ca38fb293">
  <data key="d3">When no living beneficiary exists, the payment to the estate becomes necessary; thus, maintaining up-to-date beneficiary designations prevents such outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="f4dfbce0-ca9c-4a02-8aa7-27e266777ed0">
  <data key="d3">If the proceeds are paid to the estate due to lack of a surviving beneficiary, it implies that either no valid beneficiary was named or any prior changes were ineffective, possibly because the change wasn't properly executed by the required date.</data>
  <data key="d4">implies efficacy</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="3f213a1e-e278-42fb-8c8b-f3adf267911d">
  <data key="d3">When no living beneficiary exists, proceeds default to the estate; however, prior beneficiary changes—effective even after death—can prevent this outcome by designating a valid recipient.</data>
  <data key="d4">prevents</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="0d942949-f688-4e68-85e8-07b70d1319c6">
  <data key="d3">When no beneficiary survives the insured, proceeds default to the estate, which occurs precisely because any prior beneficiary designation—even irrevocable ones—fails due to lack of survival. Thus, the outcome described in fact_sentence_2 depends on whether any designated beneficiary, including irrevocable ones, was alive at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">consequence of survival failure</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="bc01826e-0790-4744-905a-5c0919e140df">
  <data key="d3">Even if an irrevocable beneficiary exists and cannot be removed without consent, the absence of any surviving beneficiary results in proceeds being paid to the estate, overriding individual designation rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="bca821e4-dd36-4856-bd49-b34de7e5162f">
  <data key="d3">Payment to the estate is considered only after confirming no contingent beneficiary is available to receive the proceeds.</data>
  <data key="d4">preempted by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="38974002-cdef-417b-abe4-05fe910d1ed4">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines a general rule about estate payouts when no beneficiary survives, which encompasses the situation detailed in fact_sentence_1 regarding the failure of the contingent beneficiary. Thus, it provides context that makes the conditional outcome in fact_sentence_1 plausible.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="ac1a6b74-dc59-4a4f-a24b-16a083744b91">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of paying proceeds to the estate arises because the beneficiary is legally presumed to have died before the insured in simultaneous-death scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="57f5cb31-60fc-403b-8faf-61bb58c44d33">
  <data key="d3">When the beneficiary is presumed to have predeceased the insured, the payment of proceeds to the estate becomes the default distribution method according to policy rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="a1058e7f-8f18-49f2-bc24-6b94e7ac24c5">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a surviving beneficiary triggers payment to the estate, but only after applying the legal presumption that the beneficiary predeceased the insured when death order is ambiguous. Thus, the outcome described in sentence 2 depends on the assumption established in sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="927cb107-8365-4668-bb63-e17e86722615">
  <data key="d3">If the proceeds are paid to the estate due to lack of surviving beneficiaries, it implies that any potential beneficiaries either did not survive or formally disclaimed their rights, thereby being treated as though they predeceased the insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="3e91835e-9ad1-4260-b452-07cf78be6476">
  <data key="d3">When no beneficiary survives, the insurer may pay proceeds to the estate; this provision serves as a default pathway but does not preclude other equitable recipients identified by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="91d5242d-2ab5-43dd-a6c9-1df492a48caf">
  <data key="d3">When no beneficiary survives the insured, the proceeds are paid to the estate, triggering the company’s full release from further liability upon such payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">discharges</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="f075e888-0cb1-43c8-8ebf-84c98e1c462f">
  <data key="d3">When no beneficiary survives the insured, proceeds typically go to the estate; however, exceptions allow payment to those who incurred qualifying expenses during the insured’s final care or funeral, extending beyond mere estate disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="23a68193-61ae-40df-becb-863cc2fa667b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that if no beneficiary survives the insured, proceeds go to the estate. This scenario overlaps with fact_sentence_2, which specifies that if a beneficiary isn't found within 90 days, the estate receives payment. Both involve estate disbursement due to unavailability of beneficiaries, though fact_sentence_2 includes a time-bound condition absent in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a768f1b0-5081-44f9-8ca1-4d423f35bb90" target="c9a8b525-e466-428a-9f1b-a7e27067ae66">
  <data key="d3">When proceeds are paid to the estate due to lack of surviving beneficiaries, the specific amount disbursed corresponds exactly to the death benefit outlined in the policy specifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
