<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the standard timeline for incontestability, while fact_sentence_2 modifies this rule by excluding cases involving nonpayment of premiums, thereby restricting when the incontestability clause applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause takes effect after two years, but only if there were no material misrepresentations made at application; otherwise, the insurer can still void the policy during the contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period begins at issuance and defines the window during which the insurer can challenge claims due to misrepresentation. This temporal boundary enables the enforcement of denial rights outlined in the subsequent clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period begins at issuance, but once expired, the insurer generally cannot dispute the policy's validity—except when fraudulent misrepresentations are involved.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="76e38f97-59cf-4de6-8497-dce31eec92a1">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period specified in fact_sentence_1 leads to the insurer losing the ability to dispute the policy’s validity afterward, as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period applies initially from the issue date; when a policy is reinstated, this same principle restarts, meaning a new two-year window begins at reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period specified in fact_sentence_1 directly leads to the permanent protection against policy invalidation outlined in fact_sentence_2. After this time elapses, the insurer cannot dispute the policy’s validity based on any prior misrepresentations.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period starts at issuance but resets upon reinstatement, applying only to representations made during the reinstatement application. This ensures ongoing scrutiny of newly submitted information even after the original period expired.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability provision after two years sets the timeframe within which the insurer's ability to deny claims is restricted; this directly enables the application of the suicide benefit limitation clause, which applies specifically within those initial two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause, effective after two years, ensures that the insurer cannot deny claims due to prior misrepresentations, thereby enabling the full death benefit to be paid without restriction.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="6364d71d-2969-4592-8deb-8bc2dc62cbbd">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence sets a baseline two-year incontestability period from the original issue date. The second explains that reinstatement resets this timeline, allowing full benefits after two years post-reinstatement, even if death results from suicide.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts timing</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="dae46bf4-aa0b-48e8-8a30-9eb5461df3a8">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence defines when the policy becomes incontestable under normal circumstances. The second describes how a lapsed policy can be revived, which resets certain protections but does not alter the original contestability rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="7cd9fba9-62dc-4347-a278-9463dcb7691b">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause applies after two years from issuance, but does not govern the process of reinstating a lapsed policy. Reinstatement requires a formal application regardless of whether the policy was previously incontestable.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="7c0199b7-ab48-4404-96ba-e4cf6a976f54">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause prevents future challenges to coverage after two years from issuance, setting a baseline timeframe. This indirectly supports the context for the suicide exclusion rule, which applies similarly within two years—but specifically upon reinstatement rather than original issue.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="a02029bc-d32a-41e0-a806-f525ebfc428c">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability rule applies after two years from issuance, but when a policy is reinstated, its status resets, meaning the two-year clock starts anew. This ensures consistency with the broader policy framework where reinstated policies begin fresh under the same conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="c8a217fc-b379-48eb-80d2-edc84b27f3c5">
  <data key="d3">The initial two-year contestability period starts at issuance and ends after two years. Upon policy reinstatement, this timeline restarts, ensuring continued scrutiny until another full two-year window passes post-reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="9849a0f2-a835-4ab0-9793-62acf42df5ec">
  <data key="d3">After two years from the issue date, the policy becomes incontestable, but liabilities prior to reinstatement remain unenforceable regardless of this timeline.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="e8364bc1-ea45-49ba-a605-1c2c3dd2dd6c">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period established in fact_sentence_1 sets the baseline protection window; however, when a policy is reinstated, this timeline does not carry over fully because the suicide exclusion begins again from the reinstatement date, effectively resetting part of the initial conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="1ca6911d-df92-4ae4-b6bb-99a8272cae42">
  <data key="d3">The contestability provision in fact_sentence_2 depends on the issue date established in fact_sentence_1 to determine when the two-year protection period begins, thereby anchoring its applicability.</data>
  <data key="d4">sets timing for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="6027da96-db64-41d1-9b1e-c3ef1d338bd7">
  <data key="d3">The two-year incontestability period relies on the occurrence of consecutive policy anniversaries to determine when the protection against contestation begins.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables timing</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause depends on the broader legal framework preserving contract integrity; thus, the permanence of policy terms ensures the two-year rule remains enforceable over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause ensures long-term protection once the two-year mark passes, while the severability clause preserves contractual continuity should any term become unenforceable; these mechanisms collectively reinforce the policy’s enduring validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950" target="66d34f7f-f03b-44b9-ae46-16416415bc2a">
  <data key="d3">The two-year incontestability clause relies on clear, enforceable contract rules; this fact ensures such protections cannot be undermined by verbal agreements or implied concessions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
