  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period established in fact_sentence_1 sets the timeframe within which certain claims, such as those involving suicide, trigger specific limitations outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd" target="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability of the policy after two years ensures that insurers cannot deny claims due to prior misrepresentations, enabling the full death benefit to be paid without restriction on cause of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd" target="6364d71d-2969-4592-8deb-8bc2dc62cbbd">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period established in fact_sentence_1 restarts upon policy reinstatement, enabling eligibility for full death benefits after another two years post-reinstatement, as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts</data>
