  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd" target="7c0199b7-ab48-4404-96ba-e4cf6a976f54">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period defined in fact_sentence_1 sets the temporal boundary within which certain claims may be challenged; fact_sentence_2 extends this timeline's implications by applying a similar restriction—limiting payouts—to cases involving suicide occurring within two years of policy reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd" target="a02029bc-d32a-41e0-a806-f525ebfc428c">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period defined in fact_sentence_1 applies anew when a policy is reinstated, ensuring insurers retain the right to challenge claims based on misrepresentation during this window post-reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
