  <data key="d3">The initial two-year contestability period established at issuance sets the foundation for later reset conditions; upon reinstatement, this period restarts entirely, ensuring continued scrutiny over misrepresented information even after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd" target="e8364bc1-ea45-49ba-a605-1c2c3dd2dd6c">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period established in fact_sentence_1 provides the temporal basis for resetting the suicide exclusion upon reinstatement, ensuring consistency in risk assessment timelines.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd" target="9849a0f2-a835-4ab0-9793-62acf42df5ec">
  <data key="d3">The incontestability clause after two years sets the foundation for when liability begins again upon reinstatement; without this rule, the timing of reinstatement would lack context for determining legal exposure.</data>
