  <data key="d3">Material misrepresentation allows the insurer to rescind the policy during the two-year contestability period, thereby preventing the policy from becoming fully incontestable at the end of that time.</data>
  <data key="d4">triggers limitation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="76e38f97-59cf-4de6-8497-dce31eec92a1">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a two-year contestability period allows the insurer to invalidate the policy based on misrepresentation; once this period ends, the company loses the right to challenge its validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">The initial contestability clause applies at policy issuance; when a policy is later reinstated, it restarts the same protection mechanism under identical conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence defines the two-year window during which misrepresentations can lead to policy rescission. After this period, the second sentence confirms that the company loses the right to challenge the policy's validity regardless of prior inaccuracies.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518">
  <data key="d3">If the insurer rescinds the policy due to material misrepresentation during the contestability period, it directly leads to the ability to deny claims based on the same grounds. This reflects a downstream effect where policy invalidation enables claim denial.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50">
  <data key="d3">The initial contestability period allows cancellation based on misrepresentations at issuance; when a policy is reinstated, a fresh two-year contestability window begins solely concerning new disclosures in the reinstatement process.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence sets up the standard condition for policy rescission during the contestability period. The second sentence clarifies that this restriction does not apply if fraud occurred, allowing continued legal recourse regardless of timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821">
  <data key="d3">The contestability period allows the insurer to deny claims based on misrepresentation; if the insured commits suicide within that time, even though it's unrelated to misrepresentation, the payout is capped at premiums paid, showing how multiple exclusions apply simultaneously.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits coverage</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="7c0199b7-ab48-4404-96ba-e4cf6a976f54">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause allows cancellation due to misrepresentation within two years; this period resets upon reinstatement, triggering the same limitation seen in the suicide benefit restriction, where only returned premiums are payable if death occurs within two years post-reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts due to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period limits claim payouts based on misrepresentation; once this period expires, the policyholder’s beneficiaries become eligible for the full death benefit regardless of cause of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="6364d71d-2969-4592-8deb-8bc2dc62cbbd">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause limits the insurer's ability to deny claims based on misrepresentation only during the initial two-year window; once reinstated, this period resets, affecting eligibility for full benefits described later.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions benefit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause limits the insurer's ability to deny claims based on misrepresentation only within the first two years. This condition indirectly relates to reinstatement because demonstrating insurability later ensures continued eligibility despite prior issues.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="a02029bc-d32a-41e0-a806-f525ebfc428c">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a two-year contestability period allows the insurer to void the policy due to misrepresentation early on. Upon reinstatement, however, the policy resumes as if uninterrupted, effectively resetting certain protections and timelines despite earlier risks.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="c8a217fc-b379-48eb-80d2-edc84b27f3c5">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period applies initially after policy issuance; when a lapsed policy is reinstated, this period resets entirely based on the reinstatement date, ensuring continued protection against misrepresentation claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="e8364bc1-ea45-49ba-a605-1c2c3dd2dd6c">
  <data key="d3">The two-year contestability period enables the insurer to void coverage based on misrepresentation; when a lapsed policy is reinstated under this framework, the same rules—including new suicide exclusions—are reactivated from the reinstatement date.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d" target="9849a0f2-a835-4ab0-9793-62acf42df5ec">
  <data key="d3">If a material misrepresentation exists during the initial two-year contestability period, the insurer may rescind the policy. This directly affects reinstatement eligibility, meaning no liabilities arise before reinstatement unless the policy was properly maintained without breach.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
