<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950">
  <data key="d3">The insurer's ability to deny claims over material misrepresentation is contingent upon the existence of a two-year contestability period, which sets the legal limit for such actions post-issue.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd">
  <data key="d3">Material misrepresentations in the application permit the insurer to deny claims even after the two-year incontestability period has begun, thus limiting the scope of the protection offered by the incontestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of denying a claim due to material misrepresentation justifies the authority to rescind the policy, as claim denial reinforces the legal basis for terminating coverage retroactively.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="76e38f97-59cf-4de6-8497-dce31eec92a1">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence sets up a condition under which claims are vulnerable during the initial two years. The second sentence describes the consequence of surviving beyond that window—claims become immune to contestation.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence defines a temporary window where misrepresentations can invalidate claims. The second sentence confirms that once this window closes, the company loses the right to challenge the policy's validity based on prior statements.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence sets up the general rule during the contestability window; the second clarifies its limitation by specifying that even after expiry, fraudulent misrepresentations remain subject to challenge.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional exception</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">The first fact sets up the general rule about contestability due to misrepresentation. The second fact specifies how this rule restarts upon policy reinstatement, maintaining consistency with the overall clause framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50">
  <data key="d3">The initial contestability clause sets the foundation for risk assessment; when a policy is reinstated, this principle extends to cover newly submitted information, triggering a fresh contestability window tied specifically to the reinstatement application.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines grounds for denying a claim based on misrepresentation during the initial two-year period. This condition operates alongside the suicide clause, which similarly restricts payouts when death occurs by suicide within the same timeframe, though it applies regardless of intent or representation.</data>
  <data key="d4">coexists with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="7c0199b7-ab48-4404-96ba-e4cf6a976f54">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes a general condition under which claims can be denied based on misrepresentation during the contestability period. This sets the stage for fact_sentence_2, which applies a similar time-based restriction but specifically to suicide-related deaths after reinstatement, reinforcing the ongoing significance of the two-year timeline.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b">
  <data key="d3">If a claim arises during the two-year contestability period due to misrepresentation, the company may deny payment; however, once two years have passed from the Issue Date, such denial rights expire, and the full death benefit becomes payable irrespective of the cause of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="6364d71d-2969-4592-8deb-8bc2dc62cbbd">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause limits claim payouts early in the policy term unless the insured died from causes unrelated to misrepresentation. After reinstituting the policy and waiting two years beyond reinstatement, the restriction ends, allowing full payout even for non-fraudulent deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">postpones</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="c8a217fc-b379-48eb-80d2-edc84b27f3c5">
  <data key="d3">The initial contestability period allows denial of claims based on misrepresentation; upon policy reinstatement, this same rule restarts, creating a new window where claims can again be contested.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="a02029bc-d32a-41e0-a806-f525ebfc428c">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause limits claim payouts during the first two years unless fraud occurred. Upon reinstatement, the policy's effective date reverts to its original issuance, thereby restarting the contestability window.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="e8364bc1-ea45-49ba-a605-1c2c3dd2dd6c">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause limits claims based on misrepresentation during the first two years; when a policy is reinstated, this restriction resets along with other time-sensitive provisions like the suicide exclusion.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518" target="9849a0f2-a835-4ab0-9793-62acf42df5ec">
  <data key="d3">The contestability clause allows denial of claims based on misrepresentation during the initial two years; when a policy is reinstated, this reset means the company is not responsible for liabilities existing before reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
