  <data key="d3">The immunity from contestability granted in fact_sentence_2 depends entirely on the passage of the two-year period defined in fact_sentence_1; without meeting this temporal condition, the clause does not apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy becomes incontestable after two years unless due to nonpayment of premiums, the insurer forfeits any ability to challenge the policy's legitimacy upon expiry of the contestability window, as outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of the two-year contestability period, described in the second sentence, renders invalid any potential grounds for rescinding the policy based on earlier misstatements, thus reinforcing the significance of the timeline established in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence highlights the permanent protection granted after the contestability period ends, making it clear that any earlier conditions—like those in the first sentence—are no longer enforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="76e38f97-59cf-4de6-8497-dce31eec92a1">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 extends the principle from fact_sentence_1 by emphasizing that misstatements—even non-fraudulent ones—cannot justify invalidating the policy after the contestability period has expired.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969">
  <data key="d3">Sentence 1 establishes a general rule post-contestability period; sentence 2 refines this rule by excluding fraudulent misstatements from its protection, thereby modifying the scope of the initial claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of the original contestability period prevents future challenges based on misstatements unless the policy is reinstated, at which point a new contestability period starts afresh.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of the initial contestability period establishes a permanent protection against challenges based on past misrepresentations. However, when a policy is reinstated, a new contestability period starts afresh—limited to claims arising from the reinstatement application’s disclosures.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of the contestability period ensures the policy remains valid, allowing the full death benefit to be paid upon death after two years, unless excluded by specific provisions like suicide.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="7c0199b7-ab48-4404-96ba-e4cf6a976f54">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of the contestability period ensures that claims based on past misrepresentations cannot be contested, setting the stage for how suicide-related exclusions apply post-reinstatement under similar time constraints.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="6364d71d-2969-4592-8deb-8bc2dc62cbbd">
  <data key="d3">The end of the contestability period ensures the policy’s validity cannot be challenged; once reinstated, another two-year clock starts, after which the full death benefit applies irrespective of cause.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821">
  <data key="d3">The first fact establishes that once the two-year contestability period passes, the insurer loses the right to deny coverage based on misrepresentation. This creates a protective boundary around policyholder rights, but it does not override the suicide clause, which remains enforceable independently within the same timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">coexists with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="c8a217fc-b379-48eb-80d2-edc84b27f3c5">
  <data key="d3">The end of the original contestability period prevents future challenges based on past misrepresentations, but reinstating the policy restarts this protection window, creating a renewed opportunity for the insurer to contest validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="a02029bc-d32a-41e0-a806-f525ebfc428c">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of the contestability period ensures the insurer cannot later invalidate the policy due to misrepresentations. This condition becomes relevant again when a policy is reinstated, as the contestability clock resets, making the original expiration status dependent on reinstitution events.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2" target="9849a0f2-a835-4ab0-9793-62acf42df5ec">
  <data key="d3">Once the contestability period ends, the insurer loses the right to dispute the policy’s validity, reinforcing that no future claim can be denied over prior misstatements. However, the insurer remains exempt from obligations incurred before the policy was reinstated, meaning even validly issued policies have gaps in coverage until reinstatement occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes and limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
