<edge source="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969" target="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950">
  <data key="d3">Fraudulent misstatements allow the insurer to contest the policy beyond the two-year window, thereby preserving the core intent of the contestability clause despite its expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">qualifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969" target="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd">
  <data key="d3">While the first sentence defines when the policy becomes generally incontestable, the second reinforces that certain serious misconduct—fraud—remains actionable regardless of time elapsed, thus preserving legal recourse under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains exception</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969" target="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d">
  <data key="d3">While the second sentence introduces an exception based on fraud, it depends on the prior context established by the first—that without fraud, the contestability window limits the insurer’s ability to dispute claims post-period.</data>
  <data key="d4">exempts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969" target="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence provides a caveat to the first by allowing exceptions beyond the contestability period only when fraud is involved, thereby refining the scope of the original restriction.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits scope</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969" target="76e38f97-59cf-4de6-8497-dce31eec92a1">
  <data key="d3">Sentence 2 restricts the applicability of sentence 1 by specifying that fraud allows contestation despite expiration of the contestability period, making it a conditional override.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969" target="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2">
  <data key="d3">Sentence 2 introduces an important limitation on the broad immunity granted in sentence 1, specifying that fraud remains subject to challenge even after the contestability period ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">The end of the first contestability period allows continued coverage unless fraud occurred; however, if the policy is later reinstated, a new contestability period begins regardless of prior expiration.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969" target="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of the initial contestability period prevents challenges based on non-fraudulent misstatements; however, when a policy is reinstated, a new contestability window starts solely for claims related to the reinstatement application.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
