<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement triggers a new two-year contestability window focused exclusively on disclosures in the reinstatement form, effectively extending potential review beyond the original policy’s initial contestability term.</data>
  <data key="d4">exempts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy triggers a renewed two-year contestability period rooted in the accuracy of the reinstatement application, effectively resetting part of the original condition established in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d">
  <data key="d3">If a policy is reinstated after lapsing, the prior contestability rules do not apply retroactively—the new contestability period starts afresh but only covers representations made during the reinstatement application.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy restarts the contestability clock, but only for representations made at reinstatement—this builds directly on the original rule about misrepresentation being grounds for denial.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="76e38f97-59cf-4de6-8497-dce31eec92a1">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy triggers a renewed contestability period, even though the prior one has expired, ensuring insurers retain scrutiny power over newly submitted information despite past immunity.</data>
  <data key="d4">triggers new period</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy triggers a renewed two-year contestability period focused exclusively on the accuracy of the reinstatement application. This condition depends on the prior existence of a fixed contestability term that lapses over time, as described in the earlier statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a lapsed policy triggers a renewed two-year contestability period focused exclusively on representations made during the reinstatement process, even though prior misrepresentations outside of fraud are no longer contestable after the original term ended.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">The rule about applying a new contestability period after reinstatement depends on its restriction to fresh information submitted during the reinstatement process.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="7c0199b7-ab48-4404-96ba-e4cf6a976f54">
  <data key="d3">The restart of the contestability period at reinstatement ensures that any misrepresentations in the reinstatement application may lead to denial of claims. This condition supports the limitation of suicide benefit payouts to just the premiums paid, reinforcing the risk-based restrictions tied to recent reinstatements.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="6364d71d-2969-4592-8deb-8bc2dc62cbbd">
  <data key="d3">The new contestability period beginning at reinstatement sets a time limit during which the insurer may challenge claims based on misrepresented information in the reinstatement application. After two years from reinstatement, this limitation expires, allowing full death benefits to be paid irrespective of cause.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="dae46bf4-aa0b-48e8-8a30-9eb5461df3a8">
  <data key="d3">The new contestability period after reinstatement relies on the precondition that the policy was previously allowed to be reinstated within five years of lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="7cd9fba9-62dc-4347-a278-9463dcb7691b">
  <data key="d3">The new contestability period after reinstatement relies on the prior act of submitting a formal application to restore the policy's validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96">
  <data key="d3">The new contestability period after reinstatement depends on truthful representations in the reinstatement application, which necessitates providing evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383">
  <data key="d3">The new contestability period after reinstatement depends on submitting a reinstatement application, which requires fulfilling financial terms like paying past premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="a02029bc-d32a-41e0-a806-f525ebfc428c">
  <data key="d3">The new contestability period beginning at reinstatement depends on the policy's restoration to active status, meaning its effectivity hinges on the reinstated policy being considered continuously effective since inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="c8a217fc-b379-48eb-80d2-edc84b27f3c5">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies that the new contestability period after reinstatement applies solely to information given in the reinstatement application. This detail clarifies the boundary of applicability for the broader principle stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="e8364bc1-ea45-49ba-a605-1c2c3dd2dd6c">
  <data key="d3">The reinstitution of the contestability period based on reinstatement application statements directly enables the enforcement of the suicide exclusion clause, ensuring consistency in risk assessment after policy restoration.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="9849a0f2-a835-4ab0-9793-62acf42df5ec">
  <data key="d3">The renewal of the contestability period based on the reinstatement application explains why the insurer cannot be held responsible for obligations existing before reinstatement, ensuring consistency in risk assessment.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="6b3e96fb-fdf8-41b4-8cb5-c43de3bff2e7">
  <data key="d3">While the original incontestability rule applies from policy inception, the revised rule after reinstatement restarts the contestable period based on updated disclosures, effectively extending potential scrutiny beyond the original term.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50" target="b0682bc0-a0b2-4059-b458-c16bdb0d9fb4">
  <data key="d3">The original suicide exclusion period’s applicability is extended through reinstatement, meaning any claim within two years of reinstatement faces similar limitations regardless of prior policy duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47a5336d-f0f2-4777-a219-2468d15cadaa" target="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">defines duration of</data>
</edge>
