<edge source="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821" target="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950">
  <data key="d3">The suicide exclusion clause defines a key exception to coverage within the early policy term, reinforcing why the incontestability period begins at two years—to prevent abuse while still allowing claim restrictions during the risk assessment phase.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821" target="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 illustrates a key exception within the two-year period described in fact_sentence_1, where death by suicide results in restricted benefits despite the general incontestability rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821" target="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d">
  <data key="d3">Suicide within two years limits benefit payments regardless of other factors like misrepresentation, but such cases remain subject to the broader contestability rules unless fraud is involved, meaning misrepresentation could still invalidate coverage independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">exempt from rescinding</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821" target="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518">
  <data key="d3">The suicide exclusion clause limits benefit payments to returned premiums if death occurs by suicide within two years of issue. This restriction coexists with the contestability period rule, where misrepresentation also allows claim denial, forming parallel safeguards against abuse during early policy life.</data>
  <data key="d4">coexists with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821" target="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2">
  <data key="d3">The second fact specifies that suicide within two years results in limited benefits, irrespective of mental state. This restriction operates concurrently with the expiration of the contestability period, meaning that even though the insurer can't dispute the policy's validity post-period, the suicide exclusion still applies strictly.</data>
  <data key="d4">coexists with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">The suicide exclusion rule limits payouts to premiums paid if death occurs within two years of issuance, regardless of reinstatement. This means even if the policy was later revived, the original start date governs eligibility for this restriction.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821" target="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 imposes a limit on benefits if suicide occurs within two years of issuance. This limitation expires after two years, at which point fact_sentence_2 takes effect, allowing full payment of the death benefit irrespective of cause.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821" target="7c0199b7-ab48-4404-96ba-e4cf6a976f54">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes the default limitation on suicide claims tied to the initial policy issuance. Fact sentence 2 extends this limitation to cases where the policy has been reinstated, applying the same benefit cap under similar conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends to reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821" target="6364d71d-2969-4592-8deb-8bc2dc62cbbd">
