<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="2ccc2a1b-cdc3-45ef-9eca-fa939da40950">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of full death benefit payout after two years depends directly on the policy becoming incontestable at that time, removing grounds for denial based on past inaccuracies.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="b1209a03-debc-41d3-aa0a-edcc152854fd">
  <data key="d3">The provision allowing full death benefit payments after two years depends on the policy being incontestable, which is triggered by surviving beyond the initial two-year contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d">
  <data key="d3">Upon completion of the two-year contestability period, the insurer loses the right to cancel the policy over misrepresentation, enabling full payment of the death benefit even if the cause of death is otherwise restricted.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="4ba5aa3e-d14a-4e24-9784-1bfc938f9518">
  <data key="d3">The expiration of the two-year contestability period removes the insurer’s ability to deny claims based on pre-issue misrepresentations, thereby nullifying the conditions outlined in the earlier statement about potential claim denials.</data>
  <data key="d4">replaces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="76e38f97-59cf-4de6-8497-dce31eec92a1">
  <data key="d3">The provision that the full death benefit becomes payable after two years relies on the earlier clause stating the company can no longer contest the policy’s validity post-contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="20a49319-596a-4eb4-9cf6-c48e01ba5bb2">
  <data key="d3">Once the contestability period ends, the insurer loses the right to dispute the policy’s validity, making it possible for the full death benefit to be paid out without qualification based on prior misrepresentations.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969">
  <data key="d3">The provision allowing full death benefit payments after two years relies on the prior condition that the insurer can no longer contest the policy’s validity, ensuring claim eligibility post-contestability.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the full death benefit after two years from issuance sets a key timeline; however, reinstatement may reset this window, meaning the two-year rule applies anew from the reinstatement date rather than the original issue date.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="890edb7e-d6f7-49a2-af24-7d3844f90821">
  <data key="d3">After two years have passed since the policy was issued, the earlier restriction on suicide-related payouts—described in fact_sentence_1—is lifted, enabling full benefit payments under normal conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="7c0199b7-ab48-4404-96ba-e4cf6a976f54">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the standard rule for full benefit payment after two years from issue, while fact_sentence_1 introduces an exception related to suicide within two years of reinstatement, even if the overall term has passed since issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="6364d71d-2969-4592-8deb-8bc2dc62cbbd">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes that after two years from issuance, the full death benefit applies. Fact sentence 2 extends this principle to reinstated policies, stating that the same two-year clock restarts upon reinstatement, ensuring consistent treatment post-reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends to reinstated policies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="a02029bc-d32a-41e0-a806-f525ebfc428c">
  <data key="d3">The condition that the full death benefit becomes payable after two years depends on the policy being active; reinstatement restores the policy’s effective status, ensuring that the two-year clock may restart, thereby enabling future claim eligibility under fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">restarts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="c8a217fc-b379-48eb-80d2-edc84b27f3c5">
  <data key="d3">The rule about full death benefit becoming payable after two years from the issue date sets a baseline timeline. This timeline resets upon policy reinstatement, meaning the same condition applies anew based on the reinstatement date instead of the original issue date.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b" target="e8364bc1-ea45-49ba-a605-1c2c3dd2dd6c">
  <data key="d3">The full death benefit becomes payable after two years from issuance unless the policy is reinstated; if reinstated, the suicide exclusion begins again, potentially delaying full benefit availability beyond the initial two-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="cd31ca9b-0758-431a-a4f4-36cd838b288f" target="78b5d060-8134-489f-89c3-41f10e3bdf1b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">time condition for</data>
</edge>
