<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="3f3c482f-63c7-4446-b46e-136dbb82436d">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of insurability is necessary to reinstate a lapsed policy, which helps maintain compliance with initial underwriting standards, thereby reducing the likelihood of future contestability challenges.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="76e38f97-59cf-4de6-8497-dce31eec92a1">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of insurability allows policy reinstatement, which triggers a restart of the contestability period, thereby re-establishing the insurer’s right to review claims based on misrepresented information.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required before reinstatement can occur, which subsequently activates a fresh two-year contestability period.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50">
  <data key="d3">Providing evidence of insurability is required before reinstatement occurs, thereby enabling the start of a new contestability period based on the reinstatement application's content.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="7c0199b7-ab48-4404-96ba-e4cf6a976f54">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required to reinstate a policy, thereby triggering the reactivation of the suicide exclusion period, under which benefits would be limited if the insured dies by suicide within two years of reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="6364d71d-2969-4592-8deb-8bc2dc62cbbd">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability is required before reinstatement can occur, enabling the subsequent eligibility for full death benefits after two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">precondition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="dae46bf4-aa0b-48e8-8a30-9eb5461df3a8">
  <data key="d3">Providing satisfactory evidence of insurability is necessary to qualify for reinstatement after a policy lapse, ensuring eligibility under the five-year rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="7cd9fba9-62dc-4347-a278-9463dcb7691b">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability is required to support the reinstatement request, which must follow the initial submission of a formal application.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="a02029bc-d32a-41e0-a806-f525ebfc428c">
  <data key="d3">Providing evidence of insurability allows the policy to be restored to its original active state after lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 requires proof of insurability as part of the reinstatement process. This condition operates alongside the requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest, forming essential components of the overall reinstatement criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">parallel requirement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="c8a217fc-b379-48eb-80d2-edc84b27f3c5">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required before a policy can be reinstated, which then activates a fresh two-year contestability window beginning from the reinstatement date.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required to reinstate a lapsed policy, while interest on overdue premiums accrues annually. These requirements operate independently within the reinstatement process.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="e8364bc1-ea45-49ba-a605-1c2c3dd2dd6c">
  <data key="d3">Proof of insurability is required to initiate reinstatement, which then activates a fresh suicide exclusion period beginning at the reinstatement date.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96" target="9849a0f2-a835-4ab0-9793-62acf42df5ec">
  <data key="d3">Providing proof of insurability allows policy reinstatement, after which the company assumes no responsibility for events occurring before that date.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
