<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="b418554b-6c94-4f40-8a92-5c7ae9e4a969">
  <data key="d3">Repayment of overdue premiums with interest is required to restore a lapsed policy, ensuring the policyholder meets financial obligations before reactivation. This step precedes any renewal of protection terms, including those tied to the contestability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating the policy triggers a new two-year contestability period, but only after satisfying the obligation to repay past-due premiums with interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="311d56b0-6554-4971-9166-302d2fb46b50">
  <data key="d3">Payment of overdue premiums with interest enables reinstatement, which may trigger a renewed two-year contestability period based on the reinstatement application's contents.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="7c0199b7-ab48-4404-96ba-e4cf6a976f54">
  <data key="d3">Reinstating a policy necessitates paying past-due premiums with interest; this process restarts the contestability and suicide exclusion periods, making it possible for the suicide clause in fact_sentence_1 to take effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="6364d71d-2969-4592-8deb-8bc2dc62cbbd">
  <data key="d3">Repayment of overdue premiums with interest is required before reinstatement, enabling future access to the full death benefit after the two-year waiting period.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="dae46bf4-aa0b-48e8-8a30-9eb5461df3a8">
  <data key="d3">Reinstatement eligibility within five years requires payment of past-due premiums along with applicable interest charges set by the company.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="7cd9fba9-62dc-4347-a278-9463dcb7691b">
  <data key="d3">Paying all overdue premiums with interest is a necessary financial step that follows the submission of a written reinstatement application.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 mandates payment of past-due premiums with interest to restore coverage. This financial obligation complements the need to provide evidence of insurability, ensuring that both risk and cost factors are addressed before reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">parallel requirement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="a02029bc-d32a-41e0-a806-f525ebfc428c">
  <data key="d3">Paying overdue premiums with interest enables the restoration of the policy's active status after a lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 requires payment of overdue premiums with interest for policy reinstatement. Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that this interest accrues through annual compounding, defining its calculation method.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="c8a217fc-b379-48eb-80d2-edc84b27f3c5">
  <data key="d3">Paying overdue premiums with interest enables policy reinstatement, which in turn initiates a new two-year contestability period starting from the reinstatement date.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="e8364bc1-ea45-49ba-a605-1c2c3dd2dd6c">
  <data key="d3">Paying overdue premiums with interest enables policy reinstatement, which triggers the start of a fresh suicide exclusion period beginning from the reinstatement date.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383" target="9849a0f2-a835-4ab0-9793-62acf42df5ec">
  <data key="d3">Paying overdue premiums with interest allows the policy to be reinstated, after which the insurer assumes responsibility only going forward, meaning they are not liable for claims or obligations that occurred before reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b229652c-667c-48a9-9483-80901941878d" target="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383">
