  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468" target="dae46bf4-aa0b-48e8-8a30-9eb5461df3a8">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay interest on overdue premiums, compounding annually, applies specifically when reinstating a lapsed policy within the allowed five-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468" target="7cd9fba9-62dc-4347-a278-9463dcb7691b">
  <data key="d3">Compounded annual interest accrues on overdue premiums, which must be paid when submitting a written application to reinstate the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468" target="aecb2c75-f016-41ec-b85e-1fcb7b055c96">
  <data key="d3">Annual compounding interest applies to overdue premiums, which must be paid along with proof of insurability when reinstating a lapsed policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.6</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468" target="a00154a8-e11a-439a-bed6-5a4409f0f383">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to pay overdue premiums with interest (fact_sentence_1) depends on knowing how interest accumulates; fact_sentence_2 explains that interest compounds annually, specifying the operational rule behind the obligation.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468" target="a02029bc-d32a-41e0-a806-f525ebfc428c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for annual compound interest on overdue premiums supports the financial conditions necessary for reinstatement, ensuring the insurer recovers costs associated with delinquent payments before restoring coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468" target="9849a0f2-a835-4ab0-9793-62acf42df5ec">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for compounding annual interest on overdue premiums establishes the financial condition necessary for reinstatement, which triggers the start of new liability from the reinstatement date onward.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions reinstatement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468" target="c8a217fc-b379-48eb-80d2-edc84b27f3c5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that interest on overdue premiums compounds annually ensures that reinstatement involves additional costs, which directly enables the initiation of a new contestability period upon reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8df6f649-337c-4947-8756-419be0693e63" target="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">contains overdue premium interest terms</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1405c01e-af52-4cf8-bc68-cde20a3fdf51" target="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">applies compound interest on overdue premiums</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a1aae147-8f39-4aa8-bd16-223cecbe2180" target="2f7c6575-4d94-4771-9874-466c56019468">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">incurs</data>
</edge>
