  <data key="d3">Claims made during the lapse period fall outside coverage entirely, so the resumption of incontestability at reinstatement does not retroactively apply. Therefore, the start of a fresh incontestability window is irrelevant to events prior to reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b" target="17de4c88-376a-4e6b-b992-7f89cc84bb9a">
  <data key="d3">The lack of liability during the lapse period supports the reset of the suicide exclusion upon reinstatement, reinforcing that pre-lapse events are not covered regardless of future policy status.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b" target="38763c7f-abef-4ce9-83af-a9a6ee8c0390">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that the insurer cannot pay claims during the lapse period, reinforcing Fact_sentence_1's rule that only reinstated policies qualify for benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b" target="fa298b78-ed8c-4e0c-bf92-26cf2ce452f8">
  <data key="d3">Claims during the lapse period are explicitly excluded, so even though reinstatement begins a fresh contestability window, it cannot extend liability back into the inactive phase of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">complies with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b" target="c8a217fc-b379-48eb-80d2-edc84b27f3c5">
  <data key="d3">The absence of liability during the lapse period necessitates that reinstatement initiates a fresh contestability window, ensuring fairness under renewed coverage conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b" target="e8364bc1-ea45-49ba-a605-1c2c3dd2dd6c">
  <data key="d3">The lack of liability during the lapse period justifies why the suicide exclusion resets upon reinstatement, preventing abuse through dormant policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b" target="9849a0f2-a835-4ab0-9793-62acf42df5ec">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 complements fact_sentence_1 by clarifying that claims based on events during the lapse period fall outside the company’s obligation, directly supporting the principle established in fact_sentence_1 about post-lapse immunity.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c09c7788-56c0-4fa8-adcd-9d2bd40d6ae9" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is the time frame during which the company is not liable</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5641f11d-2356-4ece-af14-56136882076b" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">possible remedy to avoid loss of coverage due to lapse</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0323955c-7a16-4967-84ec-be93f0092821" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">not liable for claims during lapse</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ca12aca0-bc6f-4fe9-9221-a98ab716ed01" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">responsible for preventing lapse to maintain coverage</data>
</edge>
<edge source="88fd9259-20ff-4661-999e-5c859e4d1f74" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">may lose coverage during lapse period</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4c055ba7-8d0f-4650-9dcb-ae2d3a38b974" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">defines window for extension or conversion at expiry</data>
</edge>
