</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="a68f05ee-b6c2-4a27-be1f-bfafeddf4b0c">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy doesn’t renew automatically, reinstating it activates new conditions—including a fresh contestability window—rather than continuing prior terms seamlessly.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="e6c3a70b-5a82-471d-8ba5-5360ade9eb6b">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy does not renew automatically, lapses may occur; such lapses result in the insurer being exempt from paying claims under the terms outlined in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="be5d9596-fd48-4642-93c3-1033cc1a3da6">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy does not renew automatically, the owner must take proactive steps at expiration. This creates an opportunity to convert to permanent coverage prior to the expiry date, fulfilling a key provision within the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="6b3c39b6-2af6-4210-bf69-47e128370b19">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy does not renew automatically, the insured must take action to continue coverage, which involves paying premiums according to the specific product's terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="0c4d1411-9c02-4d7d-ae5c-767cd2ba2497">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy does not renew automatically, the insured must initiate conversion during the designated time frame outlined in the specifications to maintain coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3">
  <data key="d3">The absence of automatic renewal creates a need for alternative actions, such as converting to permanent insurance. Conversion remains available even without demonstrating insurability, offering a viable option after the term ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="cf26351d-1aa6-446d-8320-a1b56d723009">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy does not renew automatically, the insured may need to convert it to permanent life insurance. To qualify for such conversion, the insured must meet specific requirements, including being within the company’s specified maximum conversion age.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="89be458d-91c9-451d-8e88-14357ccda4fd">
  <data key="d3">The absence of automatic renewal means timely notification becomes critical so the policyholder knows when coverage ends. Notice delivery via the last known address helps ensure awareness of non-renewal status.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be">
  <data key="d3">The absence of automatic renewal underscores the importance of formal documentation; periodic statements alone cannot change this provision, ensuring consistency with the policy's binding nature.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="3063337b-6bf5-4d8f-be93-1c56bd525563">
  <data key="d3">The absence of automatic renewal means that other terms may still apply under applicable law, ensuring some contractual obligations persist even after termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d3">Without automatic renewal, the policy expires at end-of-term, making timely premium payments—including those made during the 31-day grace period—critical to avoid lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">While the policy lacks automatic renewal, it maintains validity through a grace period upon overdue payments, enabling short-term continuity even when longer-term extension isn't available.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">The absence of automatic renewal means that a lapse caused by missed premium payments becomes final unless acted upon, making timely payment even more critical.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">The absence of automatic renewal in fact_sentence_2 explains why coverage ceases upon lapse—a condition explicitly mentioned in fact_sentence_1—highlighting the permanence of termination unless timely conversion occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ebb9f34-701d-4203-a3d1-76008e5b324f" target="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">does not have automatic renewal</data>
</edge>
