  <data key="d3">The availability of conversion without proof of insurability enhances the value of the $420 annual premium by offering future protection options regardless of health changes, making the initial low-cost entry more advantageous over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3" target="ee94c388-864e-45a9-8add-95085b2c1fad">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without medical evidence supports long-term planning, making it more feasible for the insured to sustain coverage through consistent annual payments as specified in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for access</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3" target="0dd1735c-ba92-4588-9e4a-6408b636a844">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without evidence of insurability complements reinstatement by offering another route to restore protection after lapse, though it results in a fundamentally different type of policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">complies with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3" target="b0682bc0-a0b2-4059-b458-c16bdb0d9fb4">
  <data key="d3">Converting to permanent life insurance does not eliminate the suicide exclusion; it continues to govern payouts if death results from suicide within the applicable two-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3" target="510725eb-a62d-4576-83ac-ca1422d3846e">
  <data key="d3">Conversion to permanent insurance without proof of health relies on the policy remaining active, making timely premiums—and thus the grace period—important for sustaining eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on active status</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3" target="e877399f-ddc1-47c4-afa4-1ee3ff20f43e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without proving insurability offers a pathway to extended protection beyond the initial term, potentially leveraging the grace period to maintain eligibility through timely action.</data>
  <data key="d4">extends protection window</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3" target="49091360-e758-47e5-b0be-5075a6066a07">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without evidence of insurability provides a mechanism to regain coverage even after a lapse caused by missed premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables recovery from lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3" target="4f4b308d-6280-46d2-bd3f-7dd1c0a313ad">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert a lapsed policy into permanent insurance depends on prior coverage having terminated due to lapse, making the original condition of coverage end relevant to eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables reconversion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b1cd9626-7593-431d-9593-b349a5d509ac" target="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">can be converted without evidence of insurability</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bdb56b6f-5fab-4a66-a419-bc7c0e7bd99c" target="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">administers conversion without requiring evidence of insurability</data>
</edge>
