  <data key="d3">New York law governs the policy's terms, including the provision allowing conversion to permanent life insurance without evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2" target="6c958eff-bcba-442c-aeee-865d50cfdb4e">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s governance under New York law logically supports the requirement that any disputes be resolved within New York courts, ensuring consistency in legal application and enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2" target="c5189b85-3b6b-486e-aed3-92e4fdeec68a">
  <data key="d3">The policy's governance under New York law sets the baseline legal framework, while the possibility of resolving disputes outside New York courts reflects a conditional deviation based on applicable law.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2" target="89be458d-91c9-451d-8e88-14357ccda4fd">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s adherence to New York law sets the framework for administrative procedures, including how notices are delivered to the policyholder based on legally recognized protocols.</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2" target="aa0a0cc0-c8ca-4da9-83d8-db6b05142910">
  <data key="d3">The policy's governance under New York law sets the legal foundation for how contractual obligations—including notice requirements—are interpreted and enforced. This provides context for understanding when alternative notice methods might be permitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2" target="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35">
  <data key="d3">The policy's governance under New York law sets the legal foundation for interpreting contract terms, including rules around notice delivery. While the choice of law doesn't dictate where notices must go, it provides the legal backdrop against which such procedural requirements operate.</data>
  <data key="d4">governs procedure</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2" target="1fb212bb-16a8-42fb-a936-31c2b2fbbbaa">
  <data key="d3">The policy's governance under New York law provides the legal foundation for how the company delivers periodic statements and confirms coverage details. Without this jurisdictional basis, such communications might lack enforceable standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2" target="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be">
  <data key="d3">The policy's governance under New York law sets the legal framework within which all provisions, including those about modifications, operate. This context supports the rule that informal communications cannot change terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextualizes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2" target="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s governance under New York law provides the legal framework that determines how provisions are interpreted and enforced, including assessing the validity of specific clauses.</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2" target="3063337b-6bf5-4d8f-be93-1c56bd525563">
  <data key="d3">The policy's governance under New York law supports the continued effectiveness of its remaining provisions, as state law determines what parts of the contract may still apply after changes or lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
