<edge source="c5189b85-3b6b-486e-aed3-92e4fdeec68a" target="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2">
  <data key="d3">While disputes may be resolved outside New York courts due to external legal requirements, the policy still defaults to being governed by New York law unless overridden by such requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">exempted by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c5189b85-3b6b-486e-aed3-92e4fdeec68a" target="6c958eff-bcba-442c-aeee-865d50cfdb4e">
  <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 allows for out-of-state dispute resolution under mandatory legal conditions, it operates as a caveat to fact_sentence_1’s exclusive reliance on New York courts, ensuring flexibility in compliance with broader legal obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c5189b85-3b6b-486e-aed3-92e4fdeec68a" target="3063337b-6bf5-4d8f-be93-1c56bd525563">
  <data key="d3">If disputes require resolution outside New York courts due to applicable law, the clause enabling such resolution remains subject to legal permissibility. Remaining provisions, including jurisdictional ones, continue to apply where legally allowed.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
