</edge>
<edge source="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35" target="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2">
  <data key="d3">Proper notice delivery to the designated office supports enforcement of contractual obligations, ensuring that communication complies with the standards set forth under New York law, thereby maintaining consistency with the policy’s legal framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from law</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35" target="aa0a0cc0-c8ca-4da9-83d8-db6b05142910">
  <data key="d3">The default procedure mandates sending notices to the Administrative Office. However, this requirement may be overridden if the Company directs otherwise.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35" target="d026a2f0-fa01-44c1-91bc-9263e9ca7e95">
  <data key="d3">If the Policy Owner fails to inform the company of an address change, they risk missing important notices delivered to outdated addresses, potentially leading to missed deadlines or claim denials despite fulfilling obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35" target="89be458d-91c9-451d-8e88-14357ccda4fd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that notices must be delivered to the Company’s Administrative Office. This sets up the destination point for communications initiated by the Policy Owner, ensuring formal channels are followed when sending official correspondence.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35" target="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be">
  <data key="d3">Properly delivering notices to the administrative office enables enforceable modifications to the policy through authorized amendments, supporting the requirement that only official riders can change terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35" target="3063337b-6bf5-4d8f-be93-1c56bd525563">
  <data key="d3">The notice delivery rule remains in effect because it is part of the contract’s surviving provisions under applicable law.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35" target="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41">
  <data key="d3">Notice delivery procedures ensure communication compliance, which supports overall policy governance. However, even if such procedures were challenged legally, the policy's remaining terms—including those governing notice—would still stand unless invalidated entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">severability supports</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35" target="26fb45c6-1b02-446d-aa67-f95ab9f3bac0">
  <data key="d3">Notice delivery protocols depend on the governing law, meaning New York's legal principles shape the acceptable methods and consequences of delivering communications to the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="671b3dd5-d059-4cfb-b6eb-db06dd291c2b" target="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">requires notice submissions to administrative office</data>
</edge>
<edge source="07def5d1-7b7c-40f8-ac0a-8a589878d31e" target="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual timeframe for notice requirements</data>
</edge>
