  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">law</data>
</edge>
<edge source="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be" target="41ceb0a0-ac8c-491b-8945-e0f9659c850e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">provision</data>
</edge>
<edge source="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be" target="e9992b58-f0cb-4309-aa8b-99ccf5ca595c">
  <data key="d3">The rule that periodic statements don’t change policy terms ensures that critical provisions like suicide exclusions stay effective even after reinstatement, preserving consistency in coverage limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be" target="2c93e604-74f7-4280-8c64-064a764c03c7">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy explicitly avoids automatic renewal, any attempt to imply otherwise through periodic statements would be invalid unless formally amended, preserving the original non-renewal clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be" target="82a10084-3f57-48dc-9e6f-f24c360934c3">
  <data key="d3">Formal documentation is required to change policy terms, reinforcing that exceptions like automatic conversion rely on pre-defined rules rather than informal updates, thus preserving structural integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be" target="6b3c39b6-2af6-4210-bf69-47e128370b19">
  <data key="d3">The rule against unapproved modifications ensures that requirements such as timely premium payments remain enforceable under the original contract terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be" target="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2">
  <data key="d3">Since periodic statements lack binding effect unless formally amended, the requirement for official authorization aligns with the need for consistent interpretation under New York law, reinforcing legal predictability.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be" target="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35">
  <data key="d3">Only officially authorized amendments or riders can legally modify policy terms, making it essential to send such requests via the designated administrative office specified in the notice procedure.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be" target="aa0a0cc0-c8ca-4da9-83d8-db6b05142910">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 reinforces that periodic communications lack authority to change policy terms unless amended via approved means. This aligns with fact_sentence_1’s rule on notice delivery, ensuring such changes follow prescribed protocols rather than informal exchanges.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be" target="1fb212bb-16a8-42fb-a936-31c2b2fbbbaa">
  <data key="d3">Without a formal amendment or rider, any periodic confirmation remains non-binding and cannot alter existing policy conditions despite being issued by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be" target="3063337b-6bf5-4d8f-be93-1c56bd525563">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that only official amendments change policy terms supports the continued validity of remaining provisions under the law, ensuring consistency even when updates aren't made through periodic communications.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be" target="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 emphasizes that informal communications cannot change policy terms, while fact_sentence_2 reinforces this principle by ensuring that invalid provisions don’t undermine the rest of the contract, maintaining overall legal coherence.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
