<edge source="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41" target="effe3ea6-daae-4c03-b44b-e751e10ea2f2">
  <data key="d3">The clause allowing surviving provisions when one is invalidated assumes applicability within the legal system specified—here, New York law—which governs its enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41" target="6c958eff-bcba-442c-aeee-865d50cfdb4e">
  <data key="d3">The severability clause preserves contractual integrity even if parts fail, supporting the practical operation of the chosen judicial forum in New York.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41" target="8dcdc8e2-1f45-4998-84dc-c7db4250fe35">
  <data key="d3">The severability clause preserves the integrity of the policy framework, ensuring that failure of one provision (like notice rules) doesn’t nullify the whole agreement, thus indirectly supporting the continued relevance of notice protocols.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on severability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41" target="da6699b0-8745-467d-acc5-a910c61481be">
  <data key="d3">The presence of an unenforceable provision doesn't invalidate the whole policy, aligning with fact_sentence_1's rule that only official amendments can alter terms, thus upholding procedural rigor in modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41" target="3063337b-6bf5-4d8f-be93-1c56bd525563">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that invalid provisions do not nullify the rest of the contract. Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that surviving provisions remain enforceable within legal bounds, supporting the principle from sentence one.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41" target="66d34f7f-f03b-44b9-ae46-16416415bc2a">
  <data key="d3">The severability clause ensures continuity of the policy despite invalid provisions, which complements the requirement for written waivers by reinforcing that only explicit actions can alter terms, preserving legal clarity.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 affirms that invalid provisions do not nullify the rest of the policy, which aligns directly with the core idea in fact sentence 2. Both emphasize legal continuity despite partial invalidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">The severability clause in fact_sentence_1 supports the integrity of the entire agreement stated in fact_sentence_2 by ensuring that invalid sections do not undermine the validity of the remainder.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80c83885-daf8-494c-ba9e-82a540a78e41" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">Fact Sentence 1 supports the validity of the policy’s framework even when parts fail, which aligns with Fact Sentence 2's requirement that changes to terms require explicit written approval, ensuring consistency and intent preservation.</data>
  <data key="d4">severability enforced by</data>
