<edge source="8925f004-cf81-4a9a-90c0-394a37211f40" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">If a provision is found invalid, the rest of the policy remains legally effective, ensuring continuity despite partial unenforceability.</data>
  <data key="d4">severability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8925f004-cf81-4a9a-90c0-394a37211f40" target="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0">
  <data key="d3">If a provision is found invalid or unenforceable, the rest of the policy remains fully effective due to the severability principle.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8925f004-cf81-4a9a-90c0-394a37211f40" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">If a provision becomes invalid, the completeness of the agreement ensures other parts remain enforceable, supporting the overall validity of the contract despite partial failure.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8925f004-cf81-4a9a-90c0-394a37211f40" target="66d34f7f-f03b-44b9-ae46-16416415bc2a">
  <data key="d3">If a provision is found invalid, maintaining the integrity of the remaining policy depends on strictly enforcing waiver procedures. Written authorization ensures that no unintended relinquishment occurs during enforcement challenges.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8925f004-cf81-4a9a-90c0-394a37211f40" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">If a provision becomes invalid, the remaining parts stay effective; however, changes to the policy’s terms—including waivers—require explicit authorization. This ensures consistency in maintaining contractual validity when individual clauses fail.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8925f004-cf81-4a9a-90c0-394a37211f40" target="7ab0a798-1970-4a80-ae10-ad323cf06119">
  <data key="d3">If a provision becomes invalid or unenforceable, the remaining parts of the policy stay effective. This supports the idea that non-enforcement of one clause doesn't signal acceptance of its invalidity going forward.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8925f004-cf81-4a9a-90c0-394a37211f40" target="59ec3491-57bb-4404-9c45-157c0e769471">
  <data key="d3">If a provision becomes unenforceable, its invalidity does not affect the overall validity of the policy due to severability. However, failure to act on enforcement at any time cannot be interpreted as giving up the right to enforce it later.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
