  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0" target="8925f004-cf81-4a9a-90c0-394a37211f40">
  <data key="d3">The preservation of the remainder of the policy relies on the prior condition that at least one provision might be declared invalid or unenforceable.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0" target="14d9f380-89b3-451f-94aa-1ef90e6286fa">
  <data key="d3">The severability clause ensures that even if part of the policy fails, the remainder remains effective, supporting the assertion that the whole document represents the definitive agreement between the parties.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0" target="92a0c3fd-b6dc-4a3b-852d-2dde74d5850f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that invalid provisions do not nullify the entire policy. Fact_sentence_2 adds nuance by limiting the continued validity of other provisions to what is legally permissible, refining the scope of enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0" target="59ec3491-57bb-4404-9c45-157c0e769471">
  <data key="d3">The validity of remaining provisions when one is invalidated supports the broader framework where failure to act on a breach does not waive future enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0" target="66d34f7f-f03b-44b9-ae46-16416415bc2a">
  <data key="d3">The severability clause ensures continuity of the policy despite invalid provisions, while the waiver rule reinforces that rights cannot be lost through omission. Together, they strengthen legal stability but operate independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0" target="a2f514f9-483a-46e4-bd60-a528a1b42c8b">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence ensures continuity of the policy’s effectiveness despite potential invalidity of individual clauses. The second sentence reinforces control over waivers, preventing unintended relinquishment of rights even when enforcement issues arise.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00afa11e-1a32-400d-a440-38b9111578d0" target="7ab0a798-1970-4a80-ae10-ad323cf06119">
  <data key="d3">The validity of remaining provisions when one is invalidated supports the broader framework where failure to act on a breach does not waive future enforcement rights.</data>
